00:20:41,703 --> 00:20:43,372
In terms of the balance,

545
00:20:43,373 --> 00:20:46,043
I thought I was in favor.

546
00:20:46,243 --> 00:20:47,343
I'm getting anxious.

547
00:20:47,673 --> 00:20:49,942
Many of us tied.

548
00:20:49,943 --> 00:20:51,173
It made me nervous.

549
00:20:51,473 --> 00:20:53,143
This is so tough.

550
00:20:53,243 --> 00:20:55,983
I couldn't even guess. I was anxious.

551
00:20:56,083 --> 00:20:58,453
(Only Simeez and Renan left to choose)

552
00:20:58,653 --> 00:21:01,282
I was so nervous. My heart was pounding so fast.

553
00:21:01,283 --> 00:21:02,929
I'm the only one who deserves to be a director.

554
00:21:02,953 --> 00:21:05,862
It's been so long since I had someone else direct me.

555
00:21:05,863 --> 00:21:07,503
If I can't be a director, I'm going home.

556
00:21:07,863 --> 00:21:10,793
I think I'm the most suitable to be the main director.

557
00:21:11,033 --> 00:21:14,002
I deserve the director title.

558
00:21:14,003 --> 00:21:17,073
The choreographers I choose for the director candidate are...

559
00:21:17,673 --> 00:21:19,349
I'm not thinking about anything other than first place.

560
00:21:19,373 --> 00:21:21,243
I have to make the Director Credit.

561
00:21:21,343 --> 00:21:23,343
I'm taking the Director Credit.

562
00:21:23,943 --> 00:21:25,412
- I'll take it. - It's mine.

563
00:21:25,413 --> 00:21:26,713
He'll have to give up.

564
00:21:26,813 --> 00:21:30,112
Back Koo Young and NaiN.

565
00:21:30,113 --> 00:21:31,613
(4 votes each)

566
00:21:31,983 --> 00:21:35,153
NaiN and Back Koo Young.

567
00:21:35,623 --> 00:21:37,152
(2 director candidates are NaiN and Back Koo Young.)

568
00:21:37,153 --> 00:21:38,792
(Congratulations)

569
00:21:38,793 --> 00:21:39,993
Thank you.

570
00:21:40,093 --> 00:21:41,723
Way to go!

571
00:21:41,823 --> 00:21:42,832
I was really happy.

572
00:21:42,833 --> 00:21:45,632
They might have picked me...

573
00:21:45,633 --> 00:21:47,703
based on my experience.

574
00:21:47,903 --> 00:21:51,773
There is definitely something I don't have in terms of experience.

575
00:21:51,873 --> 00:21:54,272
But I hope it becomes a chance...

576
00:21:54,273 --> 00:21:56,973
for me to prove myself as a director.

577
00:21:57,073 --> 00:21:59,513
I wanted to pick someone who worked hard.

578
00:21:59,643 --> 00:22:03,483
NaiN and Koo Young's drafts had the highest quality.

579
00:22:03,783 --> 00:22:06,453
It's something anyone will like.

580
00:22:06,583 --> 00:22:08,122
It's my first time getting directed by NaiN.

581
00:22:08,123 --> 00:22:09,992
I'm looking forward to it.

582
00:22:09,993 --> 00:22:12,123
Because it's my first time seeing her directing.

583
00:22:12,223 --> 00:22:14,362
The experience makes a huge difference.

584
00:22:14,363 --> 00:22:18,333
It's a battle between the first generation and the rookie.

585
00:22:18,433 --> 00:22:20,733
It's going to be very fun.

586
00:22:21,163 --> 00:22:25,772
(Title Sequence Film Mission final director candidates)

587
00:22:25,773 --> 00:22:27,242
Gosh.

588
00:22:27,243 --> 00:22:28,319
(After selecting 2 director candidates)

589
00:22:28,343 --> 00:22:30,912
(Kasper watches NaiN's draft again.)

590
00:22:30,913 --> 00:22:31,913
(Groaning)

591
00:22:32,283 --> 00:22:34,043
I don't think I can do it.

592
00:22:34,343 --> 00:22:35,383
Nod

593
00:22:36,453 --> 00:22:40,023
That first dimensional expression is quite embarrassing.

594
00:22:40,123 --> 00:22:41,583
I was anxious.

595
00:22:41,683 --> 00:22:43,992
I'm participating as a dancer, not a director.

596
00:22:43,993 --> 00:22:44,993
It was a shame.

597
00:22:44,994 --> 00:22:47,692
I'm kind of worried about Koo Young's video.

598
00:22:47,693 --> 00:22:51,493
I have a feeling he won't make good use of me.

599
00:22:51,593 --> 00:22:54,302
It'd feel like filming a K-pop artist music video.

600
00:22:54,303 --> 00:22:57,032
So I wanted to void both NaiN and Koo Young's.

601
00:22:57,033 --> 00:22:59,642
I'm afraid NaiN won't be able to...

602
00:22:59,643 --> 00:23:00,643
bring out the best in me.

603
00:23:00,644 --> 00:23:02,942
I would've done well as a director.

604
00:23:02,943 --> 00:23:04,442
Now that I'm not a director,

605
00:23:04,443 --> 00:23:06,112
I need to prepare myself for the worst.

606
00:23:06,113 --> 00:23:07,983
The red alarm went off in my head.

607
00:23:08,083 --> 00:23:10,182
Directing all these dancers?

608
00:23:10,183 --> 00:23:11,412
(Exclaiming)

609
00:23:11,413 --> 00:23:13,252
I'm so jealous.

610
00:23:13,253 --> 00:23:14,253
I loved it.

611
00:23:14,254 --> 00:23:16,922
Honestly, I tried so hard not to smile.

612
00:23:16,923 --> 00:23:19,393
I love my job even more now.

613
00:23:19,563 --> 00:23:21,862
I wish I could be the final director.

614
00:23:21,863 --> 00:23:22,892
It's got to be me.

615
00:23:22,893 --> 00:23:24,992
It has to be me,

616
00:23:24,993 --> 00:23:26,563
so I can make a great film.

617
00:23:26,803 --> 00:23:28,462
(NaiN and Back Koo Young's Directors' Rooms.)

618
00:23:28,463 --> 00:23:29,772
For this part...

619
00:23:29,773 --> 00:23:31,032
Maybe a drone...

620
00:23:31,033 --> 00:23:32,042
In terms of clothes...

621
00:23:32,043 --> 00:23:33,742
To express them...

622
00:23:33,743 --> 00:23:34,942
There are escalators...

623
00:23:34,943 --> 00:23:36,943
I'll send it to you before today.

624
00:23:37,173 --> 00:23:38,712
They're having a meeting right away?

625
00:23:38,713 --> 00:23:39,713
(In a meeting)

626
00:23:39,714 --> 00:23:41,719
They look like they're having a meeting with the production team.

627
00:23:41,743 --> 00:23:44,653
I was jealous. I wish I was a director.

628
00:23:44,953 --> 00:23:46,083
It'd be so much fun.

629
00:23:46,453 --> 00:23:47,522
I was jealous.

630
00:23:47,523 --> 00:23:48,923
I was really jealous.

631
00:23:49,053 --> 00:23:50,552
I'm jealous.

632
00:23:50,553 --> 00:23:52,423
But the candidates have already been chosen.

633
00:23:52,523 --> 00:23:53,822
The final director has...

634
00:23:53,823 --> 00:23:56,693
the power to send us to the Last Stage.

635
00:23:56,833 --> 00:23:57,892
Now that I'm not a director,

636
00:23:57,893 --> 00:24:00,432
I have to come up with a strategy

637
00:24:00,433 --> 00:24:03,572
to avoid going to the Last Stage.

638
00:24:03,573 --> 00:24:06,142
I'd better try so hard...

639
00:24:06,143 --> 00:24:07,619
that the final director would feel awful to pick me.

640
00:24:07,643 --> 00:24:08,942
(Renan is already practicing the choreography.)

641
00:24:08,943 --> 00:24:10,643
I practiced the choreography in advance.

642
00:24:11,013 --> 00:24:12,042
(BADA visits NaiN's room.)

643
00:24:12,043 --> 00:24:13,612
- NaiN. - Yes.

644
00:24:13,613 --> 00:24:15,582
- Are you thirsty? - Really?

645
00:24:15,583 --> 00:24:18,982
I'm going to win the director candidates' favor.

646
00:24:18,983 --> 00:24:20,052
I look forward to working with you.

647
00:24:20,053 --> 00:24:21,653
I look forward to working with you too.

648
00:24:21,953 --> 00:24:23,852
Is she on it already?

649
00:24:23,853 --> 00:24:25,963
Buttering up like this...

650
00:24:26,063 --> 00:24:28,023
I think that is...

651
00:24:28,523 --> 00:24:30,492
Let me know if you need my help.

652
00:24:30,493 --> 00:24:31,693
Cunning.

653
00:24:31,893 --> 00:24:34,033
Be my keychain man again.

654
00:24:34,233 --> 00:24:35,633
(Smiling)

655
00:24:35,833 --> 00:24:36,833
No way.

656
00:24:37,033 --> 00:24:38,993
Kasper's working so hard to avoid the Last Stage.

657
00:24:39,343 --> 00:24:40,442
(BADA also delivers a drink to Back Koo Young.)

658
00:24:40,443 --> 00:24:42,973
- Nice? Yes. - That was my strategy.

659
00:24:43,073 --> 00:24:44,112
I look forward to working with you.

660
00:24:44,113 --> 00:24:46,113
I'll keep you in center for three more seconds.

661
00:24:46,583 --> 00:24:47,583
(Nice!)

662
00:24:48,083 --> 00:24:49,752
(I'm watching you.)

663
00:24:49,753 --> 00:24:51,712
If there's anything you like in my draft,

664
00:24:51,713 --> 00:24:52,722
feel free to use it.

665
00:24:52,723 --> 00:24:54,652
- It's all yours. - You can use mine too.

666
00:24:54,653 --> 00:24:56,773
- Anything you want. - Your right-hand and left-hand.

667
00:24:56,823 --> 00:24:58,292
We're both long.

668
00:24:58,293 --> 00:25:00,422
- Exactly. - We're the tallest here.

669
00:25:00,423 --> 00:25:01,562
Can you guys...

670
00:25:01,563 --> 00:25:02,732
make a chair with your arms?

671
00:25:02,733 --> 00:25:03,733
(The taste of the power)

672
00:25:03,963 --> 00:25:06,332
Look at them. They're going crazy.

673
00:25:06,333 --> 00:25:08,102
It's a matter of being in power.

674
00:25:08,103 --> 00:25:12,343
We're also evaluating the director candidates.

675
00:25:13,143 --> 00:25:15,303
(The game changer of the final director determination)

676
00:25:16,513 --> 00:25:18,983
(Vote by 8 choreographers)

677
00:25:19,013 --> 00:25:20,982
I'll have to see their direction.

678
00:25:20,983 --> 00:25:22,252
How well they express me.

679
00:25:22,253 --> 00:25:24,412
How exciting and good my part is.

680
00:25:24,413 --> 00:25:26,423
How well they bring out the best in everyone.

681
00:25:26,523 --> 00:25:30,692
We selected them based on the draft video.

682
00:25:30,693 --> 00:25:34,022
But in the end, it's all about their direction.

683
00:25:34,023 --> 00:25:35,062
I'm confident.

684
00:25:35,063 --> 00:25:36,332
I have a good understanding of this mission,

685
00:25:36,333 --> 00:25:39,862
and I know what I'm doing from all those years of experience.

686
00:25:39,863 --> 00:25:41,632
They have to direct...

687
00:25:41,633 --> 00:25:42,802
those who make a living by directing.

688
00:25:42,803 --> 00:25:44,972
It'll never be easy...

689
00:25:44,973 --> 00:25:46,542
for the youngest to control us.

690
00:25:46,543 --> 00:25:49,472
I'm expecting NaiN's to be sensational.

691
00:25:49,473 --> 00:25:52,182
I want NaiN to start a sensation...

692
00:25:52,183 --> 00:25:54,483
among the exceptionally talented people.

693
00:25:55,143 --> 00:25:57,812
Then let's do stretching and get started.

694
00:25:57,813 --> 00:25:58,823
- Okay. - All right.

695
00:25:58,923 --> 00:26:00,822
Now that the Director...

696
00:26:00,823 --> 00:26:02,552
has been officially decided,

697
00:26:02,553 --> 00:26:03,752
I'll fall right into line.

698
00:26:03,753 --> 00:26:05,899
If you need any help, please feel free to let me know.

699
00:26:05,923 --> 00:26:07,462
It's starting now.

700
00:26:07,463 --> 00:26:09,392
I think everyone was trying to read the room.

701
00:26:09,393 --> 00:26:12,062
After all, they hold the power to send someone...

702
00:26:12,063 --> 00:26:13,532
to the Last Stage.

703
00:26:13,533 --> 00:26:15,402
Since Hash's part needs a chair...

704
00:26:15,403 --> 00:26:17,072
A chair? I'll grab a chair.

705
00:26:17,073 --> 00:26:18,172
- Where? - I'll get it.

706
00:26:18,173 --> 00:26:19,473
Is this all right?

707
00:26:20,173 --> 00:26:22,242
- Deduct points for this. - Points deducted.

708
00:26:22,243 --> 00:26:23,343
Director, here you go.

709
00:26:24,073 --> 00:26:25,212
(Satisfied)

710
00:26:25,213 --> 00:26:26,942
I really wanted to run over...

711
00:26:26,943 --> 00:26:28,242
and dash for it too.

712
00:26:28,243 --> 00:26:29,982
Excuse me, could someone give me a hand with this just once?

713
00:26:29,983 --> 00:26:31,083
Let me help you out!

714
00:26:32,553 --> 00:26:33,852
Wait, Director.

715
00:26:33,853 --> 00:26:35,059
- Wait a second. - Wait, Director.

716
00:26:35,083 --> 00:26:37,252
Everyone was just so fast.

717
00:26:37,253 --> 00:26:38,962
- This is so funny. - We keep doing this.

718
00:26:38,963 --> 00:26:41,193
A man should lift this.

719
00:26:41,593 --> 00:26:43,592
The other choreographers...

720
00:26:43,593 --> 00:26:46,232
were trying so hard to treat me well and help out.

721
00:26:46,233 --> 00:26:47,632
I was so grateful.

722
00:26:47,633 --> 00:26:48,873
But INGYOO...

723
00:26:49,203 --> 00:26:50,232
I think you just need...

724
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:52,072
to push this hand out like this.

725
00:26:52,073 --> 00:26:53,073
- Okay. - Okay.

726
00:26:53,074 --> 00:26:54,649
Director, INGYOO is just doing whatever he wants.

727
00:26:54,673 --> 00:26:55,942
Deduct points from him.

728
00:26:55,943 --> 00:26:57,742
I just want to show there are other options.

729
00:26:57,743 --> 00:26:59,313
- Okay. - I can do this right away.

730
00:26:59,813 --> 00:27:00,842
This is crazy.

731
00:27:00,843 --> 00:27:02,853
INGYOO, you're on fire.

732
00:27:02,983 --> 00:27:05,253
Who would ever want to go to the Last Stage?

733
00:27:05,283 --> 00:27:06,582
Nice.

734
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:08,252
It looks great.

735
00:27:08,253 --> 00:27:09,352
(This time, he's cheering with his entire body.)

736
00:27:09,353 --> 00:27:10,353
Nice!

737
00:27:10,354 --> 00:27:11,493
What is with him?

738
00:27:11,693 --> 00:27:13,222
NaiN, a candidate for elimination is right here.

739
00:27:13,223 --> 00:27:14,422
What are you talking about?

740
00:27:14,423 --> 00:27:16,493
I'm going all out so she will look favorably on me.

741
00:27:16,793 --> 00:27:18,263
Why does he keep doing that?

742
00:27:18,393 --> 00:27:20,702
This is exactly why people go crazy over power.

743
00:27:20,703 --> 00:27:21,963
This is why.

744
00:27:22,003 --> 00:27:23,773
The kids were just so cute.

745
00:27:25,073 --> 00:27:26,073
(Sliding in)

746
00:27:27,073 --> 00:27:28,873
(Seizing the perfect chance to butter him up)

747
00:27:29,343 --> 00:27:30,772
Genius.

748
00:27:30,773 --> 00:27:31,812
This is amazing.

749
00:27:31,813 --> 00:27:33,012
It feels good anyway.

750
00:27:33,013 --> 00:27:34,382
I'm thankful, after all.

751
00:27:34,383 --> 00:27:35,812
But then this thought crossed my mind. "Wait."

752
00:27:35,813 --> 00:27:37,312
"I think they're misunderstanding something."

753
00:27:37,313 --> 00:27:39,222
I need a majority vote,

754
00:27:39,223 --> 00:27:41,182
including the public evaluation,

755
00:27:41,183 --> 00:27:43,153
to become the Director.

756
00:27:43,253 --> 00:27:46,862
Then what do I need to do to appeal...

757
00:27:46,863 --> 00:27:48,123
to the choreographers instead?

758
00:27:48,763 --> 00:27:50,492
(Back Koo's flattery begins.)

759
00:27:50,493 --> 00:27:51,932
- Great. - You're the best.

760
00:27:51,933 --> 00:27:53,032
(Standing ovation)

761
00:27:53,033 --> 00:27:54,102
Father!

762
00:27:54,103 --> 00:27:57,132
You'd be this thrilled over plum slushes and coffee?

763
00:27:57,133 --> 00:27:58,872
How thrilled will you be if I bring in a catered buffet?

764
00:27:58,873 --> 00:28:00,273
(The flattery is flowing smoothly.)

765
00:28:00,673 --> 00:28:02,642
I realized I'd made a mistake.

766
00:28:02,643 --> 00:28:04,972
The final video isn't even the real issue.

767
00:28:04,973 --> 00:28:06,842
The choreographers learn both routines...

768
00:28:06,843 --> 00:28:08,183
before casting their votes.

769
00:28:08,713 --> 00:28:10,152
I'm crying.

770
00:28:10,153 --> 00:28:12,282
Because he was already catching...

771
00:28:12,283 --> 00:28:14,652
the things I missed,

772
00:28:14,653 --> 00:28:15,853
I think I'm starting to worry.

773
00:28:16,223 --> 00:28:17,993
Keep your head up.

774
00:28:18,593 --> 00:28:20,693
I shouldn't be acting like this.

775
00:28:20,763 --> 00:28:22,162
My plan is that, no matter what,

776
00:28:22,163 --> 00:28:23,432
I need to secure at least five votes...

777
00:28:23,433 --> 00:28:25,363
from the choreographers.

778
00:28:25,433 --> 00:28:27,332
So I approached it strategically.

779
00:28:27,333 --> 00:28:29,602
What I'm aiming for in this film...

780
00:28:29,603 --> 00:28:31,643
is the distinct charm of each choreographer anyway.

781
00:28:31,673 --> 00:28:33,943
For these individual parts,

782
00:28:33,973 --> 00:28:35,919
I'd like to adjust them by discussing them with you all.

783
00:28:35,943 --> 00:28:38,242
I was trying to appeal to them...

784
00:28:38,243 --> 00:28:40,642
so they'd want to do it by carving out the parts...

785
00:28:40,643 --> 00:28:41,812
that showcase their colors.

786
00:28:41,813 --> 00:28:44,083
For this part, I just want to leave it up to you.

787
00:28:44,283 --> 00:28:45,283
(Mission in progress)

788
00:28:46,183 --> 00:28:48,083
(This is the turn of a heels dance major.)

789
00:28:51,523 --> 00:28:53,723
My job satisfaction is at 100 percent.

790
00:28:54,763 --> 00:28:57,832
I'm giving the choreographers a lot of creative freedom.

791
00:28:57,833 --> 00:29:00,462
Since they know their own colors best,

792
00:29:00,463 --> 00:29:02,873
won't they bring out a far more elevated performance?

793
00:29:04,333 --> 00:29:05,472
That's a good one.

794
00:29:05,473 --> 00:29:06,543
Nice.

795
00:29:06,773 --> 00:29:08,949
I liked it because I felt like I was being utilized properly.

796
00:29:08,973 --> 00:29:10,413
I thought he was so sharp...

797
00:29:10,443 --> 00:29:12,149
in how closely he looked at each choreographer.

798
00:29:12,173 --> 00:29:14,542
Instead of recklessly leaving them to their own devices,

799
00:29:14,543 --> 00:29:18,183
it felt like he was pushing each one's abilities to their peak.

800
00:29:18,413 --> 00:29:21,222
Every single character was so memorable.

801
00:29:21,223 --> 00:29:22,753
It was the real flavor of the piece.

802
00:29:22,793 --> 00:29:24,453
- Yes! - Yummy!

803
00:29:24,923 --> 00:29:26,523
- It's fun, isn't it? - Yes!

804
00:29:26,593 --> 00:29:27,822
It makes me feel great too.

805
00:29:27,823 --> 00:29:30,263
But NaiN must have so much on her mind now.

806
00:29:30,363 --> 00:29:31,662
I'm starting to worry.

807
00:29:31,663 --> 00:29:35,232
I'm the type to carefully read the room.

808
00:29:35,233 --> 00:29:37,332
And the reaction to the solo parts was so positive.

809
00:29:37,333 --> 00:29:40,342
"Should I also have a part where I give the choreographers..."

810
00:29:40,343 --> 00:29:41,642
"some freedom?"

811
00:29:41,643 --> 00:29:43,413
I thought like that.

812
00:29:43,473 --> 00:29:45,743
We're going to set the positions for the chorus.

813
00:29:45,813 --> 00:29:48,142
I didn't come in with fixed formations.

814
00:29:48,143 --> 00:29:49,589
Let's just build the formations as we go.

815
00:29:49,613 --> 00:29:50,613
I felt...

816
00:29:50,614 --> 00:29:52,982
pretty uncomfortable about it.

817
00:29:52,983 --> 00:29:55,622
Deciding formations on the spot is fine too.

818
00:29:55,623 --> 00:29:56,822
But...

819
00:29:56,823 --> 00:29:58,022
At first...

820
00:29:58,023 --> 00:29:59,493
Gosh, I'm torn.

821
00:29:59,763 --> 00:30:02,122
Or... Okay. Let's do this.

822
00:30:02,123 --> 00:30:03,132
(Wavering back and forth)

823
00:30:03,133 --> 00:30:04,792
Gosh, I can't decide.

824
00:30:04,793 --> 00:30:07,533
I thought it could end up being a waste of time.

825
00:30:07,603 --> 00:30:11,572
If it were me, I would have prepared everything...

826
00:30:11,573 --> 00:30:12,673
just like NaiN did.

827
00:30:12,743 --> 00:30:14,442
I came completely prepared.

828
00:30:14,443 --> 00:30:15,842
Luckily,

829
00:30:15,843 --> 00:30:18,773
I organized everything last night before going to sleep.

830
00:30:18,843 --> 00:30:20,843
This is so clean.

831
00:30:20,913 --> 00:30:22,042
It looks like a webcomic.

832
00:30:22,043 --> 00:30:23,313
I'm shy.

833
00:30:23,913 --> 00:30:24,953
It looks so neat.

834
00:30:25,013 --> 00:30:28,122
I always map everything out in advance.

835
00:30:28,123 --> 00:30:31,452
Since there were so many micro-movements this time,

836
00:30:31,453 --> 00:30:34,162
I tried to break them down...

837
00:30:34,163 --> 00:30:36,163
into Plan A, Plan B, and Plan C.

838
00:30:36,293 --> 00:30:37,992
I'm a complete J personality,

839
00:30:37,993 --> 00:30:40,102
so I wanted to learn from NaiN.

840
00:30:40,103 --> 00:30:42,402
I'd heard a lot about NaiN...

841
00:30:42,403 --> 00:30:44,772
that she keeps things seamless when working on choreography drafts.

842
00:30:44,773 --> 00:30:46,373
So I'm curious to see it.

843
00:30:46,873 --> 00:30:48,942
I'll teach you the chorus first,

844
00:30:48,943 --> 00:30:51,412
and then walk you through from the top in sequence.

845
00:30:51,413 --> 00:30:52,542
- Great. - Okay.

846
00:30:52,543 --> 00:30:54,942
We're going to start with a hand sign.

847
00:30:54,943 --> 00:30:58,012
Please keep your thumbs horizontally aligned...

848
00:30:58,013 --> 00:31:00,083
and cross the rest of your fingers.

849
00:31:00,353 --> 00:31:01,582
For me, synchronization is...

850
00:31:01,583 --> 00:31:02,923
the most important thing.

851
00:31:02,993 --> 00:31:05,553
Next, on counts 5 and 6, your left arm goes like this.

852
00:31:05,963 --> 00:31:07,969
Aren't we focusing a bit too much on matching group synchronization?

853
00:31:07,993 --> 00:31:10,433
"Don't go above this line." It felt like saying this.

854
00:31:10,633 --> 00:31:13,462
All ten dancers project different auras,

855
00:31:13,463 --> 00:31:16,133
but it felt like she wanted everyone tailored to NaiN's tone.

856
00:31:16,573 --> 00:31:17,972
It's just boring. It's not fun.

857
00:31:17,973 --> 00:31:19,172
It doesn't feel alive.

858
00:31:19,173 --> 00:31:21,542
Honestly, I didn't like it so much.

859
00:31:21,543 --> 00:31:22,543
One, two.

860
00:31:22,544 --> 00:31:23,572
(Just nod along)

861
00:31:23,573 --> 00:31:26,082
The one-dimensional lyric interpretations and things...

862
00:31:26,083 --> 00:31:27,282
weren't pleasing at all.

863
00:31:27,283 --> 00:31:28,412
It felt despairing.

864
00:31:28,413 --> 00:31:30,713
I think I nodded like 30 or 40 times.

865
00:31:30,783 --> 00:31:32,282
Nodding subtly,

866
00:31:32,283 --> 00:31:33,922
nodding to the right,

867
00:31:33,923 --> 00:31:36,222
and then nodding once more in the middle with BABYZOO.

868
00:31:36,223 --> 00:31:38,423
Anyone watching would think I'm the king of positivity.

869
00:31:38,553 --> 00:31:40,562
We'll listen at this tempo once and go back to the original speed.

870
00:31:40,563 --> 00:31:41,822
- Okay. - All right.

871
00:31:41,823 --> 00:31:43,662
What can I do? I just have to do it.

872
00:31:43,663 --> 00:31:46,203
I don't want to become the Worst Director Candidate.

873
00:31:46,233 --> 00:31:49,133
I channeled the Hee Jung from my college days.

874
00:31:49,273 --> 00:31:50,273
Sizing up the room...

875
00:31:50,274 --> 00:31:51,472
sharp and fast.

876
00:31:51,473 --> 00:31:53,542
This is actually the first time we've been drilled...

877
00:31:53,543 --> 00:31:54,642
under this tight discipline.

878
00:31:54,643 --> 00:31:56,442
We don't usually have a chance to be doing this.

879
00:31:56,443 --> 00:31:58,142
Picking everything up so briskly.

880
00:31:58,143 --> 00:31:59,942
But honestly, I thought...

881
00:31:59,943 --> 00:32:02,142
NaiN could pick INGYOO as the Worst Director Candidate.

882
00:32:02,143 --> 00:32:04,652
I think we'll shoot this part at half-speed.

883
00:32:04,653 --> 00:32:06,883
- To match the camera moves? - Yes.

884
00:32:07,053 --> 00:32:08,783
That's cheating!

885
00:32:09,923 --> 00:32:12,022
- Hey. - I just mean...

886
00:32:12,023 --> 00:32:13,262
We're just joking around among ourselves.

887
00:32:13,263 --> 00:32:14,263
It's not that I'm criticizing you.

888
00:32:14,264 --> 00:32:15,639
You know what I mean, right? It's just us.

889
00:32:15,663 --> 00:32:17,592
It looked like NaiN's expression stiffened up.

890
00:32:17,593 --> 00:32:18,893
Want

891
00:32:19,033 --> 00:32:20,033
(Joking around)

892
00:32:22,903 --> 00:32:23,932
Unbelievable.

893
00:32:23,933 --> 00:32:25,872
We might brush it off as a joke,

894
00:32:25,873 --> 00:32:28,742
but if someone doesn't take it as a joke...

895
00:32:28,743 --> 00:32:30,513
and calls it out, it becomes an issue.

896
00:32:30,873 --> 00:32:33,083
I might look a little crazy, but...

897
00:32:33,183 --> 00:32:34,243
Pretty convincing, right?

898
00:32:34,643 --> 00:32:35,782
Isn't it convincing?

899
00:32:35,783 --> 00:32:37,312
It was a way to shift the mood...

900
00:32:37,313 --> 00:32:38,612
and break the tension.

901
00:32:38,613 --> 00:32:39,852
Anyway, I think...

902
00:32:39,853 --> 00:32:41,382
Renan? I'm not sure about Renan.

903
00:32:41,383 --> 00:32:42,453
Hash.

904
00:32:42,553 --> 00:32:43,592
I'm not sure,

905
00:32:43,593 --> 00:32:44,593
but it seemed like Hash was...

906
00:32:44,594 --> 00:32:46,292
struggling to adapt during Koo Young's section.

907
00:32:46,293 --> 00:32:48,293
There seemed to be a lack of active participation.

908
00:32:48,563 --> 00:32:50,332
The premise was...

909
00:32:50,333 --> 00:32:52,132
telling us to develop...

910
00:32:52,133 --> 00:32:53,362
the choreography ourselves,

911
00:32:53,363 --> 00:32:55,302
but honestly, I believe that bringing out the development...

912
00:32:55,303 --> 00:32:57,532
is the director's responsibility.

913
00:32:57,533 --> 00:33:00,342
Depending on how the on-set directing plays out,

914
00:33:00,343 --> 00:33:01,863
I think the outcome will be different.

915
00:33:02,143 --> 00:33:06,443
(The day of the concept shoot)

916
00:33:06,883 --> 00:33:08,143
Hello.

917
00:33:08,243 --> 00:33:09,283
What's this?

918
00:33:09,513 --> 00:33:11,213
Do we have private green rooms?

919
00:33:11,413 --> 00:33:12,953
It's just us?

920
00:33:13,253 --> 00:33:14,553
I see. Okay.

921
00:33:14,953 --> 00:33:16,052
(The 8 dancers arrive at the shared waiting room.)

922
00:33:16,053 --> 00:33:17,652
Since today is the shoot,

923
00:33:17,653 --> 00:33:19,592
we have to showcase our best...

924
00:33:19,593 --> 00:33:22,223
while evaluating both directors at the same time.

925
00:33:22,293 --> 00:33:24,392
So I figured I really needed to stay sharp.

926
00:33:24,393 --> 00:33:26,562
Because they can send me to the Last Stage,

927
00:33:26,563 --> 00:33:28,032
I have to dance flawlessly...

928
00:33:28,033 --> 00:33:29,472
and watch my behavior around them,

929
00:33:29,473 --> 00:33:30,972
so I'm nervous.

930
00:33:30,973 --> 00:33:32,332
Hello.

931
00:33:32,333 --> 00:33:33,942
(All 8 dancers finish checking into the studio set.)

932
00:33:33,943 --> 00:33:35,842
The anxiety and nerves started...

933
00:33:35,843 --> 00:33:36,943
kicking in right away.

934
00:33:37,013 --> 00:33:39,882
If you get on the director's bad side, I'll be doomed.

935
00:33:39,883 --> 00:33:40,942
I need to get my act together.

936
00:33:40,943 --> 00:33:42,652
It's suffocating.

937
00:33:42,653 --> 00:33:44,412
If I get singled out as the Worst Director Candidate,

938
00:33:44,413 --> 00:33:45,582
I'm done for.

939
00:33:45,583 --> 00:33:47,983
I didn't want to leave even the tiniest flaw.

940
00:33:48,023 --> 00:33:50,292
I will become the directors' right-hand and left-hand man.

941
00:33:50,293 --> 00:33:52,413
Please don't pick me as the Worst Director Candidate.

942
00:33:53,093 --> 00:33:55,122
The Last Stage means death for us.

943
00:33:55,123 --> 00:33:57,163
If you get cut right on the first Last Stage,

944
00:33:57,233 --> 00:33:59,133
you'll literally cry tears of blood.

945
00:33:59,333 --> 00:34:00,702
Kasper, did you change your outfit?

946
00:34:00,703 --> 00:34:01,802
Yes. Do you want to take a look?

947
00:34:01,803 --> 00:34:03,003
Yes, let me see.

948
00:34:03,103 --> 00:34:05,733
I'm just going to wear what they prepped for me.

949
00:34:05,773 --> 00:34:07,073
I only kept my own shoes on.

950
00:34:07,143 --> 00:34:08,772
- Good. - Diversity is...

951
00:34:08,773 --> 00:34:10,342
the exact direction...

952
00:34:10,343 --> 00:34:11,543
I'm aiming for.

953
00:34:11,813 --> 00:34:14,582
(During the presentation of the concept)

954
00:34:14,583 --> 00:34:17,312
(Back Koo Young focused on bringing out all 10 characters.)

955
00:34:17,313 --> 00:34:19,052
(Stylist)

956
00:34:19,053 --> 00:34:22,692
(Back Koo Young requested costumes tailored to their own characters.)

957
00:34:22,693 --> 00:34:25,222
NaiN's costumes are like a crew,

958
00:34:25,223 --> 00:34:27,093
while Koo Young's were strictly individual.

959
00:34:27,123 --> 00:34:28,422
I wanted to put...

960
00:34:28,423 --> 00:34:31,433
a sharper spotlight on each individual person.

961
00:34:31,693 --> 00:34:32,803
It's way too flashy, right?

962
00:34:32,833 --> 00:34:34,403
- Everyone looks flashy. - Really?

963
00:34:34,463 --> 00:34:36,932
There was that freedom where I could wear...

964
00:34:36,933 --> 00:34:38,633
whatever I wanted.

965
00:34:38,673 --> 00:34:39,972
- I like this one. - Do you like it?

966
00:34:39,973 --> 00:34:41,242
If you like it, I like it too.

967
00:34:41,243 --> 00:34:43,342
He gave us so many open options.

968
00:34:43,343 --> 00:34:44,512
So, in a way,

969
00:34:44,513 --> 00:34:46,782
that might have been a strategic move.

970
00:34:46,783 --> 00:34:48,542
If you micromanage everything from 1 to 10,

971
00:34:48,543 --> 00:34:49,612
they might not be able...

972
00:34:49,613 --> 00:34:53,023
to showcase their own color and personality.

973
00:34:53,223 --> 00:34:54,382
- Do I look okay now? - Yes.

974
00:34:54,383 --> 00:34:55,383
I like it.

975
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:56,792
I can tell Koo Young...

976
00:34:56,793 --> 00:34:59,322
definitely prioritizes freedom.

977
00:34:59,323 --> 00:35:00,792
But that vibe...

978
00:35:00,793 --> 00:35:01,992
wasn't quite...

979
00:35:01,993 --> 00:35:04,492
what I personally was aiming for.

980
00:35:04,493 --> 00:35:06,462
I wanted viewers...

981
00:35:06,463 --> 00:35:08,032
to watch comfortably...

982
00:35:08,033 --> 00:35:10,172
rather than feeling overwhelmed and distracted.

983
00:35:10,173 --> 00:35:11,749
It's something they have to watch every single time.

984
00:35:11,773 --> 00:35:13,673
I think mine was better.

985
00:35:14,543 --> 00:35:17,043
We'll proceed with shooting the intro scene first.

986
00:35:17,613 --> 00:35:20,743
(The intro where 10 choreographers reach their hands toward the camera)

987
00:35:20,843 --> 00:35:23,613
Director, I'd like to add an option here.

988
00:35:23,783 --> 00:35:27,183
After filming everyone doing the same move one by one,

989
00:35:27,223 --> 00:35:29,452
I also want to capture individual profile shots for each.

990
00:35:29,453 --> 00:35:30,692
I want to get it done for now.

991
00:35:30,693 --> 00:35:31,852
I don't know which cut we'll end up picking.

992
00:35:31,853 --> 00:35:32,992
That was professional of him.

993
00:35:32,993 --> 00:35:34,623
Securing coverage shots is important.

994
00:35:34,693 --> 00:35:35,922
Once you hit the editing room,

995
00:35:35,923 --> 00:35:37,332
there are countless moments where you wish...

996
00:35:37,333 --> 00:35:38,992
you'd have grabbed just one more shot.

997
00:35:38,993 --> 00:35:40,463
He's someone...

998
00:35:40,503 --> 00:35:42,873
with far more experience and flexibility.

999
00:35:42,933 --> 00:35:43,973
Nice!

1000
00:35:44,033 --> 00:35:45,393
You pulled off the chorus so well.

1001
00:35:45,433 --> 00:35:47,193
I danced harder than I did for my own piece.

1002
00:35:47,473 --> 00:35:48,942
Wouldn't that effortless composure...

1003
00:35:48,943 --> 00:35:49,972
rooted in experience...

1004
00:35:49,973 --> 00:35:51,442
make people follow...

1005
00:35:51,443 --> 00:35:54,083
his lead even more?

1006
00:35:54,113 --> 00:35:56,053
I think I was a little nervous.

1007
00:35:57,513 --> 00:35:58,882
It's just...

1008
00:35:58,883 --> 00:36:00,022
(The filming is temporarily put on hold.)

1009
00:36:00,023 --> 00:36:02,623
Can someone come over here and help me out?

1010
00:36:03,593 --> 00:36:05,053
- Well... Not MIN JUN. - Who?

1011
00:36:05,193 --> 00:36:06,363
Tae Woo.

1012
00:36:06,523 --> 00:36:07,692
Yes?

1013
00:36:07,693 --> 00:36:09,793
(His sidekick springs into action.)

1014
00:36:10,533 --> 00:36:11,563
Yes, Koo Young.

1015
00:36:11,733 --> 00:36:13,203
He called me, so I went right over.

1016
00:36:13,563 --> 00:36:14,963
- Like an automatic reflex. - Yes.

1017
00:36:15,403 --> 00:36:16,432
Yes, Koo Young.

1018
00:36:16,433 --> 00:36:17,833
(What is Kasper's mission?)

1019
00:36:19,573 --> 00:36:21,142
I pushed down on the cameraman's shoulder...

1020
00:36:21,143 --> 00:36:22,872
when he was supposed to go down.

1021
00:36:22,873 --> 00:36:24,373
Then I supported BADA.

1022
00:36:24,643 --> 00:36:25,843
I was pulling double duty.

1023
00:36:27,583 --> 00:36:28,643
Worst?

1024
00:36:28,843 --> 00:36:30,283
I have no idea who he might pick.

1025
00:36:31,453 --> 00:36:32,953
I always have to stay on my toes.

1026
00:36:34,453 --> 00:36:37,122
Let's run a blocking rehearsal among ourselves once.

1027
00:36:37,123 --> 00:36:38,153
- Okay. - Okay.

1028
00:36:38,223 --> 00:36:40,062
I liked that it kept us on edge.

1029
00:36:40,063 --> 00:36:42,322
The actual set is going to be way more hectic.

1030
00:36:42,323 --> 00:36:44,533
To properly rein in...

1031
00:36:44,663 --> 00:36:47,032
the nine trouble-making choreographers...

1032
00:36:47,033 --> 00:36:49,062
having just 1 or 2 obedient guys like me...

1033
00:36:49,063 --> 00:36:51,272
isn't going to cut it.

1034
00:36:51,273 --> 00:36:53,072
Next team, please get ready.

1035
00:36:53,073 --> 00:36:54,073
- Okay. - Okay.

1036
00:36:54,074 --> 00:36:55,372
He has to lead us...

1037
00:36:55,373 --> 00:36:56,849
and win over the cameraman at the same time.

1038
00:36:56,873 --> 00:36:58,442
Director, wouldn't it be better...

1039
00:36:58,443 --> 00:37:00,319
to catch this from a low angle right from the start?

1040
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:02,543
I think it'd be great to grab a tight shot once.

1041
00:37:02,643 --> 00:37:05,212
I got to see how he communicated with the cameraman today, too.

1042
00:37:05,213 --> 00:37:06,853
He even used those technical terms.

1043
00:37:06,983 --> 00:37:08,122
Excuse me, but...

1044
00:37:08,123 --> 00:37:09,282
About the opening tilt-up...

1045
00:37:09,283 --> 00:37:12,023
But definitely, the side with the panel lights...

1046
00:37:12,093 --> 00:37:13,522
Terms like "tilt-up..."

1047
00:37:13,523 --> 00:37:14,592
and "zoom in."

1048
00:37:14,593 --> 00:37:16,592
If you don't know those terms, you know, they look down on you.

1049
00:37:16,593 --> 00:37:18,062
It's just like the Dongdaemun wholesale market.

1050
00:37:18,063 --> 00:37:19,633
They won't even sell to novices.

1051
00:37:19,833 --> 00:37:20,933
Director, do you mind...

1052
00:37:21,503 --> 00:37:23,143
if I try operating the camera for a shot?

1053
00:37:24,073 --> 00:37:26,172
(Back Koo Young even tries filming the camera take himself.)

1054
00:37:26,173 --> 00:37:29,443
Of course, I'm not a pro like the cameramen are.

1055
00:37:29,473 --> 00:37:32,443
But I created the choreography, so I know it inside out.

1056
00:37:33,383 --> 00:37:34,982
It needs to drop down like this.

1057
00:37:34,983 --> 00:37:36,753
I see. So it's okay to move a bit early.

1058
00:37:37,183 --> 00:37:39,783
He even took hold of the camera himself.

1059
00:37:39,853 --> 00:37:42,453
Now I have to step up and show moments...

1060
00:37:42,583 --> 00:37:44,352
where I don't fall behind,

1061
00:37:44,353 --> 00:37:46,363
so I feel the pressure.

1062
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:49,562
We'll now roll Take One of the dance scene.

1063
00:37:49,563 --> 00:37:53,833
The scene from BADA to BABYZOO, then INGYOO.

1064
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:55,863
- Let's test pulling him up first. - Okay.

1065
00:37:56,373 --> 00:37:57,772
(BABYZOO's section features a high-difficulty technique...)

1066
00:37:57,773 --> 00:37:59,349
(where he pops straight up off the floor in one beat.)

1067
00:37:59,373 --> 00:38:00,442
Five, six.

1068
00:38:00,443 --> 00:38:02,643
Seven, eight.

1069
00:38:03,143 --> 00:38:04,143
- Jun Hui. - Yes?

1070
00:38:04,144 --> 00:38:05,212
- Not like this. - Okay.

1071
00:38:05,213 --> 00:38:07,242
Use your core strength to rise in a straight line.

1072
00:38:07,243 --> 00:38:08,682
Four, five, six.

1073
00:38:08,683 --> 00:38:10,212
Seven.

1074
00:38:10,213 --> 00:38:11,412
(Failed)

1075
00:38:11,413 --> 00:38:12,782
(On, no.)

1076
00:38:12,783 --> 00:38:14,252
- What's the problem? - I'll try it.

1077
00:38:14,253 --> 00:38:15,383
I'll get it right.

1078
00:38:15,523 --> 00:38:17,423
BABYZOO made some mistakes there.

1079
00:38:17,693 --> 00:38:19,523
He's supposed to rise straight up like this,

1080
00:38:19,623 --> 00:38:21,193
just like Michael Jackson.

1081
00:38:21,523 --> 00:38:22,523
Squeeze your buttocks tight...

1082
00:38:22,524 --> 00:38:23,962
and make your core rock-solid.

1083
00:38:23,963 --> 00:38:25,062
From the back of your thighs.

1084
00:38:25,063 --> 00:38:26,833
You can't let yourself get scared.

1085
00:38:27,003 --> 00:38:28,332
- Okay. - If you...

1086
00:38:28,333 --> 00:38:30,432
push your hips back trying to keep your balance,

1087
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:32,032
you'll never pull this off.

1088
00:38:32,033 --> 00:38:33,042
Okay.

1089
00:38:33,043 --> 00:38:34,419
- Let's try it one more time. - All right.

1090
00:38:34,443 --> 00:38:36,273
Five, six, seven.

1091
00:38:36,473 --> 00:38:37,473
(Failed)

1092
00:38:37,474 --> 00:38:39,313
(The 4th attempt)

1093
00:38:39,513 --> 00:38:40,782
(The 5th attempt)

1094
00:38:40,783 --> 00:38:43,653
I'm so sorry. I'll do it right.

1095
00:38:44,083 --> 00:38:45,312
It took quite a bit of time.

1096
00:38:45,313 --> 00:38:46,752
Is that hard?

1097
00:38:46,753 --> 00:38:49,182
Was it too difficult to pull off to begin with? Just then...

1098
00:38:49,183 --> 00:38:50,492
(Back Koo Young ends up demonstrating it himself.)

1099
00:38:50,493 --> 00:38:51,723
Seven, eight. Like this.

1100
00:38:52,423 --> 00:38:53,522
Do you get what I mean?

1101
00:38:53,523 --> 00:38:54,523
(Impressed)

1102
00:38:54,524 --> 00:38:56,433
He popped straight up in a clean line.

1103
00:38:56,533 --> 00:38:58,413
- How did he do that? - Do you get what I mean?

1104
00:38:58,493 --> 00:39:00,932
If you're going to fail, just fall over.

1105
00:39:00,933 --> 00:39:02,462
Use your core strength as much as possible.

1106
00:39:02,463 --> 00:39:04,972
Koo Young got a bit edgy then.

1107
00:39:04,973 --> 00:39:06,749
Please check the time for me. What time is it?

1108
00:39:06,773 --> 00:39:08,242
If this doesn't work out,

1109
00:39:08,243 --> 00:39:10,242
it causes a delay because of me,

1110
00:39:10,243 --> 00:39:12,612
so I wondered if I should've gone up to him...

1111
00:39:12,613 --> 00:39:15,683
and asked, "Should we practice this beforehand?"

1112
00:39:15,813 --> 00:39:17,482
I think this is an episode that aroused...

1113
00:39:17,483 --> 00:39:20,223
because the director placed too much faith in the dancers.

1114
00:39:20,383 --> 00:39:22,052
(Back Koo Young didn't practice the technique during rehearsals.)

1115
00:39:22,053 --> 00:39:23,869
(Back Koo Young didn't practice the technique during rehearsals.)

1116
00:39:23,893 --> 00:39:25,269
"They will probably practice in advance."

1117
00:39:25,293 --> 00:39:27,923
I think he was too complacent and trusted them blindly.

1118
00:39:29,323 --> 00:39:31,063
- Darn it. - Wait. Cut.

1119
00:39:32,133 --> 00:39:34,232
(JEONG MIN JUN's mistake)

1120
00:39:34,233 --> 00:39:35,862
(The section where JEONG MIN JUN tosses the chair to Kasper)

1121
00:39:35,863 --> 00:39:38,033
It was the part where I should roll the chair over.

1122
00:39:38,173 --> 00:39:40,672
For me to slide the chair toward Hash,

1123
00:39:40,673 --> 00:39:42,243
the camera needs to move a bit faster.

1124
00:39:42,573 --> 00:39:44,712
I'm leaving this up to you.

1125
00:39:44,713 --> 00:39:46,342
(I'm leaving this up to you.)

1126
00:39:46,343 --> 00:39:47,383
Okay.

1127
00:39:47,543 --> 00:39:49,443
Stay hidden off-camera...

1128
00:39:49,583 --> 00:39:50,913
and slide it right on cue.

1129
00:39:51,313 --> 00:39:53,083
(However)

1130
00:39:53,483 --> 00:39:54,523
Please!

1131
00:39:55,453 --> 00:39:57,322
(Repeated failures)

1132
00:39:57,323 --> 00:39:58,852
- Are you okay? - I didn't actually pull it off.

1133
00:39:58,853 --> 00:40:01,323
We could have run the chair toss a few more times yesterday.

1134
00:40:01,423 --> 00:40:02,922
He could have easily said, "Do you want to run it once..."

1135
00:40:02,923 --> 00:40:04,033
"along with the blocking?"

1136
00:40:04,193 --> 00:40:05,932
Was the spot where he tossed the chair too far?

1137
00:40:05,933 --> 00:40:07,139
(Back Koo Young spots the issue on set.)

1138
00:40:07,163 --> 00:40:08,562
It cuts both ways.

1139
00:40:08,563 --> 00:40:09,703
Either incompetence,

1140
00:40:10,073 --> 00:40:11,873
or placing way too much faith in the dancers.

1141
00:40:11,933 --> 00:40:14,773
To put it nicely, Koo Young is...

1142
00:40:15,043 --> 00:40:16,242
completely free-spirited.

1143
00:40:16,243 --> 00:40:18,072
"Wear whatever outfit you want."

1144
00:40:18,073 --> 00:40:20,012
"Dance however you feel like dancing."

1145
00:40:20,013 --> 00:40:21,613
But to put it bluntly,

1146
00:40:21,713 --> 00:40:23,853
he doesn't come with much structure in advance.

1147
00:40:24,113 --> 00:40:25,813
It was like "Do whatever you want."

1148
00:40:25,953 --> 00:40:28,582
That might feel comfortable for some,

1149
00:40:28,583 --> 00:40:30,693
but for others, it can easily feel like extra labor.

1150
00:40:30,753 --> 00:40:32,622
That depends on each person.

1151
00:40:32,623 --> 00:40:34,423
That actually felt worse to me.

1152
00:40:34,663 --> 00:40:37,533
I think it puts a burden on the dancers.

1153
00:40:37,633 --> 00:40:38,862
It feels like homework.

1154
00:40:38,863 --> 00:40:41,732
In terms of winning over the choreographers,

1155
00:40:41,733 --> 00:40:44,373
I believe my approach might be the more convincing one.

1156
00:40:44,573 --> 00:40:46,643
- Good work, everyone! - Yes!

1157
00:40:46,773 --> 00:40:47,972
(Director Candidate Back Koo Young's shoot is over.)

1158
00:40:47,973 --> 00:40:49,843
- Thank you. - You're the best.

1159
00:40:50,243 --> 00:40:51,672
Hello.

1160
00:40:51,673 --> 00:40:53,382
(The next Director Candidate NaiN prepares for the shoot.)

1161
00:40:53,383 --> 00:40:55,782
I wanted to give off a trendy throne vibe,

1162
00:40:55,783 --> 00:40:57,452
so I requested a clean black-and-white look...

1163
00:40:57,453 --> 00:40:59,352
so it wouldn't look cheap or flimsy.

1164
00:40:59,353 --> 00:41:00,353
(Sleeping makeup)

1165
00:41:00,523 --> 00:41:02,282
I took on a style...

1166
00:41:02,283 --> 00:41:04,992
completely opposite to earlier.

1167
00:41:04,993 --> 00:41:06,123
Do I look sexy?

1168
00:41:07,123 --> 00:41:08,622
(Shy)

1169
00:41:08,623 --> 00:41:10,033
How was Koo Young's directing?

1170
00:41:10,563 --> 00:41:11,933
He's very free-spirited.

1171
00:41:12,493 --> 00:41:14,002
It felt like he gave...

1172
00:41:14,003 --> 00:41:16,572
each individual the freedom of a soloist.

1173
00:41:16,573 --> 00:41:19,173
"Break through your ceiling with your own unique style."

1174
00:41:19,373 --> 00:41:21,673
- And NaiN is tightly structured. - Yes.

1175
00:41:21,843 --> 00:41:23,943
But honestly, I prefer structured setups.

1176
00:41:23,973 --> 00:41:24,973
(Surprised)

1177
00:41:24,974 --> 00:41:27,259
There's a distinct thrill that comes from razor-sharp precision.

1178
00:41:27,283 --> 00:41:29,613
With NaiN, everything is...

1179
00:41:29,713 --> 00:41:31,252
crisp and clearly directed,

1180
00:41:31,253 --> 00:41:32,789
so it might have more mainstream appeal.

1181
00:41:32,813 --> 00:41:34,682
Actually, we still hold the upper hand...

1182
00:41:34,683 --> 00:41:36,152
since we're the ones casting the votes.

1183
00:41:36,153 --> 00:41:38,252
If Koo Young says "Minus 2 points,"

1184
00:41:38,253 --> 00:41:39,253
I'll go, "What?"

1185
00:41:39,254 --> 00:41:41,392
"You're bringing up the points first?"

1186
00:41:41,393 --> 00:41:43,439
"You'd better watch out." I think this is what it is.

1187
00:41:43,463 --> 00:41:44,662
(Director Candidate 1 can't let his guard down.)

1188
00:41:44,663 --> 00:41:46,332
- I predict NaiN's is going... - I know.

1189
00:41:46,333 --> 00:41:47,563
To turn out much cleaner.

1190
00:41:47,833 --> 00:41:48,862
I drew out...

1191
00:41:48,863 --> 00:41:53,542
the camera angles beforehand just in case I might get confused.

1192
00:41:53,543 --> 00:41:56,472
I also preset eye-lines for each section.

1193
00:41:56,473 --> 00:41:58,242
I mapped out the stage area in advance...

1194
00:41:58,243 --> 00:42:00,082
and organized exactly where we'd shoot.

1195
00:42:00,083 --> 00:42:01,942
This is for when I become the director.

1196
00:42:01,943 --> 00:42:04,683
I came up with some ideas in advance.

1197
00:42:05,083 --> 00:42:06,922
Please shoot this one from a high diagonal angle.

1198
00:42:06,923 --> 00:42:09,122
(NaiN briefs the cameramen on her draft video.)

1199
00:42:09,123 --> 00:42:10,292
You want the final edit to cut...

1200
00:42:10,293 --> 00:42:11,492
- like the reference video, right? - Yes.

1201
00:42:11,493 --> 00:42:14,023
The angles and timing, completely identical.

1202
00:42:14,393 --> 00:42:15,862
So I don't think we need to grab...

1203
00:42:15,863 --> 00:42:18,362
multiple coverage shots like Koo Young did earlier.

1204
00:42:18,363 --> 00:42:19,732
We will just tackle each shot listed here,

1205
00:42:19,733 --> 00:42:21,332
- one by one. - Exactly.

1206
00:42:21,333 --> 00:42:23,603
Since we have more cuts than earlier,

1207
00:42:23,633 --> 00:42:24,732
if a take is good,

1208
00:42:24,733 --> 00:42:26,272
please let me know right away so we can move on.

1209
00:42:26,273 --> 00:42:29,242
Koo Young didn't have that many sections,

1210
00:42:29,243 --> 00:42:31,213
but NaiN has nearly twice the cuts.

1211
00:42:31,343 --> 00:42:33,042
Koo Young only...

1212
00:42:33,043 --> 00:42:36,212
broke things down into five one-take sections.

1213
00:42:36,213 --> 00:42:38,659
NaiN has double the cuts, but there is barely any blocking movement.

1214
00:42:38,683 --> 00:42:40,452
There's no risk for the dancers,

1215
00:42:40,453 --> 00:42:43,173
but setting the camera each time could eat up a huge amount of time.

1216
00:42:43,523 --> 00:42:45,892
Everything is cleanly organized in my head,

1217
00:42:45,893 --> 00:42:48,493
so the real key will be how quickly I can push things forward.

1218
00:42:49,023 --> 00:42:50,332
- Hi. - Hi.

1219
00:42:50,333 --> 00:42:51,793
- Did you get some rest? - Yes.

1220
00:42:51,963 --> 00:42:53,363
- I like your outfit. - I know.

1221
00:42:53,503 --> 00:42:55,333
You know how to pull off an outfit.

1222
00:42:55,503 --> 00:42:57,333
Our director really knows how to motivate us,

1223
00:42:57,673 --> 00:42:59,109
- I mean... - giving out compliments like that.

1224
00:42:59,133 --> 00:43:00,643
It's really pretty.

1225
00:43:01,043 --> 00:43:02,043
(Energy up)

1226
00:43:02,044 --> 00:43:03,643
Are you conducting an orchestra?

1227
00:43:03,843 --> 00:43:04,972
- NaiN. - Yes?

1228
00:43:04,973 --> 00:43:08,543
I stacked these rings so my hands stand out more.

1229
00:43:08,943 --> 00:43:10,182
- Is this okay? - Yes.

1230
00:43:10,183 --> 00:43:11,382
I was worried it might look too flashy on me.

1231
00:43:11,383 --> 00:43:13,183
- Just make sure they don't fly off. - Okay.

1232
00:43:14,383 --> 00:43:15,782
(I'm the only one with rings.)

1233
00:43:15,783 --> 00:43:17,453
I just can't handle this.

1234
00:43:17,693 --> 00:43:20,462
Since I'm also in a position where I have to prove myself,

1235
00:43:20,463 --> 00:43:23,122
I brought out the rings, hoping they'd add...

1236
00:43:23,123 --> 00:43:24,333
some extra highlight.

1237
00:43:24,493 --> 00:43:26,633
- Give me a ring too. - Which one do you want?

1238
00:43:26,733 --> 00:43:28,432
You can choose between these two.

1239
00:43:28,433 --> 00:43:29,433
I want this.

1240
00:43:29,434 --> 00:43:30,972
I want to wear something glittering too.

1241
00:43:30,973 --> 00:43:32,873
- Koo Young wants one. - How about this one?

1242
00:43:33,073 --> 00:43:34,542
- How about this? - This...

1243
00:43:34,543 --> 00:43:36,542
What if he loses one more ring...

1244
00:43:36,543 --> 00:43:38,112
and ends up with nothing?

1245
00:43:38,113 --> 00:43:40,412
- Can I try it on for just a second? - Kasper doesn't have one either.

1246
00:43:40,413 --> 00:43:41,413
Just for a second.

1247
00:43:41,414 --> 00:43:44,382
Stylists! Where are they?

1248
00:43:44,383 --> 00:43:45,512
(BABYZOO is left bare-handed.)

1249
00:43:45,513 --> 00:43:46,582
Where did they go?

1250
00:43:46,583 --> 00:43:48,852
- I should show this one. - They carefully fitted...

1251
00:43:48,853 --> 00:43:51,123
four rings to my size, but I lost them all.

1252
00:43:51,493 --> 00:43:53,052
The stylists will bring more over.

1253
00:43:53,053 --> 00:43:55,362
- Let's all wear a lot of rings. - I'll give all of yours back.

1254
00:43:55,363 --> 00:43:56,393
Okay.

1255
00:43:56,933 --> 00:43:58,653
How are you feeling, NaiN? Are you nervous?

1256
00:43:59,433 --> 00:44:00,503
Yes, a little.

1257
00:44:01,033 --> 00:44:02,203
I think it will be fun.

1258
00:44:02,433 --> 00:44:05,472
Dancers for the first cut, please step in.

1259
00:44:05,473 --> 00:44:06,773
- Thank you. - All right.

1260
00:44:06,873 --> 00:44:09,743
For the opening "fight" part, please do it a bit like this.

1261
00:44:09,843 --> 00:44:12,313
- "Fight." - Yes. That would be great. Thanks.

1262
00:44:12,513 --> 00:44:14,983
You can subtly lip-sync the word "fight" if you want.

1263
00:44:15,113 --> 00:44:16,653
Giving the gaze alone is fine too.

1264
00:44:16,983 --> 00:44:18,182
Please keep...

1265
00:44:18,183 --> 00:44:19,752
our spacing consistent throughout.

1266
00:44:19,753 --> 00:44:20,823
Okay. Good.

1267
00:44:21,023 --> 00:44:23,052
As soon as I do this,

1268
00:44:23,053 --> 00:44:24,152
- you drop in almost simultaneously. - "Simultaneously?"

1269
00:44:24,153 --> 00:44:25,223
Yes. Thank you.

1270
00:44:25,353 --> 00:44:27,893
NaiN is a monster for details.

1271
00:44:28,793 --> 00:44:31,162
(She checks every detail before monitoring playback.)

1272
00:44:31,163 --> 00:44:32,163
Good.

1273
00:44:33,663 --> 00:44:34,762
Please let the hand be in frame!

1274
00:44:34,763 --> 00:44:36,332
(Clean)

1275
00:44:36,333 --> 00:44:37,973
- Okay. - Good. Let's move on.

1276
00:44:38,233 --> 00:44:39,473
- Thank you. - All right.

1277
00:44:39,673 --> 00:44:42,242
Simeez, Hash, please step up.

1278
00:44:42,243 --> 00:44:43,243
Okay.

1279
00:44:43,244 --> 00:44:45,542
NaiN's choreography is so crisp,

1280
00:44:45,543 --> 00:44:47,442
the structure is locked in,

1281
00:44:47,443 --> 00:44:49,443
and all the cuts are mapped out, you know.

1282
00:44:49,883 --> 00:44:52,212
It makes me think she's like an AI.

1283
00:44:52,213 --> 00:44:53,922
I can see NaiN from my room.

1284
00:44:53,923 --> 00:44:56,423
The "ai" in her name jumped out at me.

1285
00:44:56,723 --> 00:44:58,352
- I was like, "Is she GemiNaiN?" - "GemiNaiN?"

1286
00:44:58,353 --> 00:44:59,922
You'll be standing here on your outer foot, right?

1287
00:44:59,923 --> 00:45:01,792
You just need to move your entire body as one unit.

1288
00:45:01,793 --> 00:45:03,832
Director, could you push in a bit faster than that?

1289
00:45:03,833 --> 00:45:04,833
- Okay. - Thank you.

1290
00:45:04,834 --> 00:45:06,062
Can you make it feel...

1291
00:45:06,063 --> 00:45:07,332
- a bit more like you? - Okay.

1292
00:45:07,333 --> 00:45:08,603
- Full power. - Okay.

1293
00:45:09,033 --> 00:45:11,473
(NaiN's direction rendering in real time)

1294
00:45:12,133 --> 00:45:14,372
Good. Let's move on.

1295
00:45:14,373 --> 00:45:17,243
NaiN just breezes through everything exactly as she prepared.

1296
00:45:17,373 --> 00:45:19,772
I'm the type who values pinpoint precision.

1297
00:45:19,773 --> 00:45:21,483
NaiN suits my style better.

1298
00:45:21,683 --> 00:45:24,412
I think NaiN offered clearer direction.

1299
00:45:24,413 --> 00:45:27,222
NaiN was a lot better at delivering cues...

1300
00:45:27,223 --> 00:45:29,022
that dancers can process intuitively.

1301
00:45:29,023 --> 00:45:31,793
Her seamless directing makes me feel a bit on edge.

1302
00:45:32,153 --> 00:45:34,963
This is going to wrap faster than my take did.

1303
00:45:35,293 --> 00:45:37,262
But the sofa scene is going to eat up quite a bit of time.

1304
00:45:37,263 --> 00:45:38,632
Renan has the rolling chair too.

1305
00:45:38,633 --> 00:45:40,532
But once they nail it in one go, that's a wrap.

1306
00:45:40,533 --> 00:45:41,633
So...

1307
00:45:41,863 --> 00:45:46,473
The chair didn't slide as well as I expected.

1308
00:45:47,243 --> 00:45:48,273
Watch out.

1309
00:45:48,443 --> 00:45:50,343
I think I stayed anxious because of the prop.

1310
00:45:51,213 --> 00:45:52,342
It's not sliding.

1311
00:45:52,343 --> 00:45:53,859
(Renan drilled the chair routine at every spare moment.)

1312
00:45:53,883 --> 00:45:56,712
Props are impossible to control.

1313
00:45:56,713 --> 00:45:58,712
They're impossible to control,

1314
00:45:58,713 --> 00:46:00,222
so I just have to give my all to what I can control.

1315
00:46:00,223 --> 00:46:01,522
I need to get comfortable with this thing.

1316
00:46:01,523 --> 00:46:03,152
I've been practicing nonstop to the music,

1317
00:46:03,153 --> 00:46:04,752
even down to the timing of kicking it and turning with it.

1318
00:46:04,753 --> 00:46:07,063
I practiced really hard, nonstop.

1319
00:46:07,263 --> 00:46:08,263
Five, six.

1320
00:46:08,264 --> 00:46:09,662
(The sofa scene shoot gets underway)

1321
00:46:09,663 --> 00:46:10,963
- Hey. - Goodness.

1322
00:46:11,193 --> 00:46:12,292
Too fast.

1323
00:46:12,293 --> 00:46:14,632
You're starting a little early.

1324
00:46:14,633 --> 00:46:15,733
Five, six.

1325
00:46:15,963 --> 00:46:16,972
(Stopping)

1326
00:46:16,973 --> 00:46:19,633
(Renan keeps missing the cue)

1327
00:46:19,773 --> 00:46:21,242
I think NaiN clenched her teeth there.

1328
00:46:21,243 --> 00:46:23,042
Let's try that again.

1329
00:46:23,043 --> 00:46:25,512
You need to turn as soon as you start moving.

1330
00:46:25,513 --> 00:46:27,112
And when you come over, you can come right up next to me.

1331
00:46:27,113 --> 00:46:28,282
Yes.

1332
00:46:28,283 --> 00:46:30,482
Renan seemed to have some trouble...

1333
00:46:30,483 --> 00:46:33,212
catching the rhythm on set today,

1334
00:46:33,213 --> 00:46:35,353
so that was a little disappointing.

1335
00:46:35,953 --> 00:46:38,422
The chair isn't supposed to come in right away at the beginning.

1336
00:46:38,423 --> 00:46:39,722
It's supposed to be like the draft video.

1337
00:46:39,723 --> 00:46:41,062
When we do this part,

1338
00:46:41,063 --> 00:46:43,192
- could you shoot it from the front? - Sure.

1339
00:46:43,193 --> 00:46:44,992
You've been shooting from the side the whole time.

1340
00:46:44,993 --> 00:46:48,233
You need to move over to the side for the staggered timing move.

1341
00:46:48,663 --> 00:46:51,173
Please shoot it as close to this video as possible.

1342
00:46:51,533 --> 00:46:53,272
INGYOO, what I'm realizing is,

1343
00:46:53,273 --> 00:46:54,273
NaiN shot her draft video with a team of dancers...

1344
00:46:54,274 --> 00:46:56,142
who already work...

1345
00:46:56,143 --> 00:46:58,842
really well with her.

1346
00:46:58,843 --> 00:47:01,212
And each of us has such a strong individual style...

1347
00:47:01,213 --> 00:47:03,382
that I don't think we're getting the same level of unison.

1348
00:47:03,383 --> 00:47:04,852
- As TURNS. - Clearly.

1349
00:47:04,853 --> 00:47:07,852
It's designed to be performed by TURNS.

1350
00:47:07,853 --> 00:47:09,052
That's what I realize now.

1351
00:47:09,053 --> 00:47:11,852
Everyone has to fit into the framework NaiN created.

1352
00:47:11,853 --> 00:47:13,562
I wonder how many people...

1353
00:47:13,563 --> 00:47:15,293
will actually be happy with that direction.

1354
00:47:15,923 --> 00:47:19,063
Could all the men gather in the center, please?

1355
00:47:19,763 --> 00:47:21,232
(Dancing, then cut almost immediately)

1356
00:47:21,233 --> 00:47:22,902
Great.

1357
00:47:22,903 --> 00:47:24,572
(Stops moving)

1358
00:47:24,573 --> 00:47:26,472
We're just going to change the setup a little.

1359
00:47:26,473 --> 00:47:27,642
Changing to the zoom lens takes about ten minutes, right?

1360
00:47:27,643 --> 00:47:28,643
I think it'll take about ten minutes.

1361
00:47:28,644 --> 00:47:31,773
We'll change lenses and start at 55.

1362
00:47:33,913 --> 00:47:35,012
Good, good.

1363
00:47:35,013 --> 00:47:36,042
(One move into the next take, and cut again)

1364
00:47:36,043 --> 00:47:37,712
Let's shoot the opposite angle.

1365
00:47:37,713 --> 00:47:40,423
We have so many scenes, so it's taking longer.

1366
00:47:42,083 --> 00:47:43,823
Great. Let's move on.

1367
00:47:44,493 --> 00:47:47,362
Because we kept dancing, stopping, dancing, and stopping,

1368
00:47:47,363 --> 00:47:49,192
cutting it here and cutting it there,

1369
00:47:49,193 --> 00:47:51,709
we never really got that feeling of building momentum, honestly.

1370
00:47:51,733 --> 00:47:53,133
So now we're shooting from above.

1371
00:47:53,393 --> 00:47:55,332
Could we go a little higher?

1372
00:47:55,333 --> 00:47:56,333
Can you give me ten minutes, then?

1373
00:47:56,334 --> 00:47:57,472
- Yes. - Bring in the jib.

1374
00:47:57,473 --> 00:48:00,142
She was even asking production to follow the exact shot order,

1375
00:48:00,143 --> 00:48:01,742
she'd sent over, so it took an enormous amount of time.

1376
00:48:01,743 --> 00:48:04,442
The direction for each individual cut may have been clear,

1377
00:48:04,443 --> 00:48:06,512
but when it comes to running the set,

1378
00:48:06,513 --> 00:48:08,382
that's not clarity. That's stubbornness.

1379
00:48:08,383 --> 00:48:10,782
It wasn't efficient, the energy on set dropped,

1380
00:48:10,783 --> 00:48:11,959
and the flow kept getting broken.

1381
00:48:11,983 --> 00:48:14,022
The directing style...

1382
00:48:14,023 --> 00:48:16,322
and the dancers' energy were almost on the same level.

1383
00:48:16,323 --> 00:48:17,752
We could never hit that peak.

1384
00:48:17,753 --> 00:48:20,392
After about three cuts, just when we're about to go,

1385
00:48:20,393 --> 00:48:22,363
she suddenly went, "That's the cut."

1386
00:48:22,693 --> 00:48:25,192
I know you're all tired. Thank you.

1387
00:48:25,193 --> 00:48:26,902
- Let's go! - It's fun!

1388
00:48:26,903 --> 00:48:29,032
- Let's go! We're almost there. - Let's go!

1389
00:48:29,033 --> 00:48:30,402
Five cuts left.

1390
00:48:30,403 --> 00:48:31,403
Easy peasy.

1391
00:48:31,404 --> 00:48:32,532
With them running out of time,

1392
00:48:32,533 --> 00:48:34,342
losing stamina was obviously an issue,

1393
00:48:34,343 --> 00:48:36,642
but I also had to fit everything I wanted into the time we had.

1394
00:48:36,643 --> 00:48:38,313
I think that really weighed on me.

1395
00:48:39,513 --> 00:48:41,382
We had to shoot the group choreography...

1396
00:48:41,383 --> 00:48:43,242
when everyone was already exhausted.

1397
00:48:43,243 --> 00:48:45,052
And we had to get the slow-motion shots too.

1398
00:48:45,053 --> 00:48:48,652
We were shooting the dance in these incredibly short bursts.

1399
00:48:48,653 --> 00:48:50,822
And with so many cuts when everyone was already tired,

1400
00:48:50,823 --> 00:48:54,193
I think the fatigue was inevitable.

1401
00:48:56,163 --> 00:48:57,862
(Simeez crashes during the break.)

1402
00:48:57,863 --> 00:48:59,832
She really looks like she's asleep.

1403
00:48:59,833 --> 00:49:02,153
Does she have a wireless charger on her back or something?

1404
00:49:03,163 --> 00:49:05,332
Honestly, I was pretty upset.

1405
00:49:05,333 --> 00:49:07,742
I knew everyone was exhausted, so I kept feeling self-conscious.

1406
00:49:07,743 --> 00:49:10,342
But I still had to show that I can hold my own...

1407
00:49:10,343 --> 00:49:12,112
as a director.

1408
00:49:12,113 --> 00:49:15,542
Everyone, for the ending formation in the straight line...

1409
00:49:15,543 --> 00:49:17,652
Can we do another version of that formation?

1410
00:49:17,653 --> 00:49:21,582
Is there another cut we can shoot with this camera setup?

1411
00:49:21,583 --> 00:49:22,682
Please get it.

1412
00:49:22,683 --> 00:49:24,152
- Let's do this. - Let's do this.

1413
00:49:24,153 --> 00:49:26,052
You can relax for now.

1414
00:49:26,053 --> 00:49:28,373
I could tell NaiN was feeling the clock closing in on her.

1415
00:49:28,463 --> 00:49:30,932
Producer, how much time do we have?

1416
00:49:30,933 --> 00:49:32,632
How much longer is it going to take?

1417
00:49:32,633 --> 00:49:33,762
While waiting,

1418
00:49:33,763 --> 00:49:35,662
- should we set the positions first? - Sounds great.

1419
00:49:35,663 --> 00:49:38,172
We're running out of time.

1420
00:49:38,173 --> 00:49:40,072
It's not over until we get the shot.

1421
00:49:40,073 --> 00:49:41,172
It's okay, NaiN.

1422
00:49:41,173 --> 00:49:42,472
Since we were really pressed for time,

1423
00:49:42,473 --> 00:49:44,573
I needed to get everything wrapped up at the end.

1424
00:49:44,873 --> 00:49:47,742
Let's just start from the chorus formation...

1425
00:49:47,743 --> 00:49:49,312
and shoot straight through to the end.

1426
00:49:49,313 --> 00:49:51,082
Everyone, that's a wrap for us.

1427
00:49:51,083 --> 00:49:52,389
(NaiN's shoot wraps after the final shot.)

1428
00:49:52,413 --> 00:49:54,153
We were running way over schedule.

1429
00:49:54,253 --> 00:49:56,322
I think she got a little overwhelmed by the pressure.

1430
00:49:56,323 --> 00:49:59,422
I think a director needs to have a certain commanding presence.

1431
00:49:59,423 --> 00:50:02,462
You need to feel like you're really in control of the whole thing.

1432
00:50:02,463 --> 00:50:04,462
Koo Young seemed more like he was handling the situation,

1433
00:50:04,463 --> 00:50:06,862
while NaiN seemed like she was under a bit more pressure.

1434
00:50:06,863 --> 00:50:08,462
She's not really someone with a deep understanding...

1435
00:50:08,463 --> 00:50:10,063
of how things run on a set.

1436
00:50:10,133 --> 00:50:13,232
And it was probably her first time taking the lead...

1437
00:50:13,233 --> 00:50:14,542
and carrying a situation like this all the way through.

1438
00:50:14,543 --> 00:50:15,942
As for the direction itself,

1439
00:50:15,943 --> 00:50:18,643
I feel like mine might be more convincing.

1440
00:50:20,583 --> 00:50:22,623
(NaiN returns to the waiting room after the shoot.)

1441
00:50:24,753 --> 00:50:26,082
(She tears up a little.)

1442
00:50:26,083 --> 00:50:28,352
It's all right. You did well.

1443
00:50:28,353 --> 00:50:29,452
Thank you.

1444
00:50:29,453 --> 00:50:31,792
You must have felt a great deal of pressure.

1445
00:50:31,793 --> 00:50:32,992
I sure did.

1446
00:50:32,993 --> 00:50:35,563
They'll count it against me.

1447
00:50:35,993 --> 00:50:37,992
It makes me think about...

1448
00:50:37,993 --> 00:50:41,232
how I can respond more flexibly the next time...

1449
00:50:41,233 --> 00:50:42,733
I'm in a situation like this.

1450
00:50:44,973 --> 00:50:48,343
(The draft video shoots are over.)

1451
00:50:49,243 --> 00:50:50,243
Wait a second.

1452
00:50:50,244 --> 00:50:52,089
(What is handed to the two director candidates?)

1453
00:50:52,113 --> 00:50:53,953
You're really dropping a bomb like this on me?

1454
00:50:54,513 --> 00:50:56,713
(Deep in thought)

1455
00:50:56,783 --> 00:50:58,182
Did NaiN think it through?

1456
00:50:58,183 --> 00:50:59,312
I've decided.

1457
00:50:59,313 --> 00:51:00,322
(She's done making a decision.)

1458
00:51:00,323 --> 00:51:02,553
(NaiN immediately writes down her pick for worst.)

1459
00:51:02,783 --> 00:51:04,592
I'm going to base my vote on today.

1460
00:51:04,593 --> 00:51:06,493
(Determined)

1461
00:51:06,823 --> 00:51:08,923
(Who did they pick as the Worst Director Candidate?)

1462
00:51:11,033 --> 00:51:12,893
(D-Day for the Final Director Selection)

1463
00:51:14,563 --> 00:51:15,703
I'm nervous.

1464
00:51:16,033 --> 00:51:17,832
- Why did they change the spot? - The chairs!

1465
00:51:17,833 --> 00:51:19,373
Why am I next to NaiN?

1466
00:51:19,673 --> 00:51:21,442
Back Koo Young versus NaiN.

1467
00:51:21,443 --> 00:51:22,943
"Final Director Selection."

1468
00:51:23,543 --> 00:51:24,842
My goodness.

1469
00:51:24,843 --> 00:51:26,772
Seeing Back Koo Young versus NaiN up there...

1470
00:51:26,773 --> 00:51:29,342
made me so nervous. My heart was seriously pounding.

1471
00:51:29,343 --> 00:51:30,852
NaiN, do you want it? To be the director?

1472
00:51:30,853 --> 00:51:31,883
Of course.

1473
00:51:32,053 --> 00:51:33,512
Give the rookie a chance.

1474
00:51:33,513 --> 00:51:34,522
(Eyes wide)

1475
00:51:34,523 --> 00:51:36,723
(Rookie madness before the final pick)

1476
00:51:36,753 --> 00:51:37,792
She's something.

1477
00:51:37,793 --> 00:51:39,569
- She's really something. - She's really something.

1478
00:51:39,593 --> 00:51:42,622
They put something terrifying up on that monitor again.

1479
00:51:42,623 --> 00:51:45,062
How could I not feel pressured? Maybe...

1480
00:51:45,063 --> 00:51:47,732
it's bordering on overconfidence,

1481
00:51:47,733 --> 00:51:49,632
but I have to believe in myself. What else can I do?

1482
00:51:49,633 --> 00:51:51,572
I know I can do a good job too.

1483
00:51:51,573 --> 00:51:54,572
There's no way I wouldn't be nervous.

1484
00:51:54,573 --> 00:51:56,842
(The two Director Candidates, caught between nerves and confidence)

1485
00:51:56,843 --> 00:51:57,942
What do I do?

1486
00:51:57,943 --> 00:52:00,072
How am I supposed to choose?

1487
00:52:00,073 --> 00:52:01,712
Did you watch the videos?

1488
00:52:01,713 --> 00:52:03,012
How are you supposed to choose between these?

1489
00:52:03,013 --> 00:52:04,412
It's the decision day.

1490
00:52:04,413 --> 00:52:05,813
This is seriously hard.

1491
00:52:06,483 --> 00:52:09,653
Who do I pick? I still hadn't decided.

1492
00:52:09,853 --> 00:52:11,852
(The two concept videos...)

1493
00:52:11,853 --> 00:52:15,422
(released early for the Public Judge vote)

1494
00:52:15,423 --> 00:52:17,992
The A, B concept videos we shot...

1495
00:52:17,993 --> 00:52:19,993
are going up on YouTube.

1496
00:52:20,233 --> 00:52:22,503
I want to see how they actually turned out.

1497
00:52:22,703 --> 00:52:24,273
So this is how it came out.

1498
00:52:24,733 --> 00:52:26,373
Koo Young is incredible.

1499
00:52:27,943 --> 00:52:30,442
This wasn't really about who choreographed better.

1500
00:52:30,443 --> 00:52:33,342
The process and the final result can be pretty different.

1501
00:52:33,343 --> 00:52:34,343
Seriously, it looks so good.

1502
00:52:34,344 --> 00:52:36,282
I think watching the videos might change my mind a little.

1503
00:52:36,283 --> 00:52:37,752
I think the video I hit Like on...

1504
00:52:37,753 --> 00:52:39,182
and the person I actually choose will be different.

1505
00:52:39,183 --> 00:52:41,882
I liked the video because the video itself was good,

1506
00:52:41,883 --> 00:52:43,792
but at the end of the day, we're choosing a director.

1507
00:52:43,793 --> 00:52:45,299
Those are two different things for me.

1508
00:52:45,323 --> 00:52:49,722
I don't think you can judge them only by their directing process.

1509
00:52:49,723 --> 00:52:52,262
The final result matters, how well I'm showcased matters,

1510
00:52:52,263 --> 00:52:54,602
and how much energy I'm able to bring during the process matters.

1511
00:52:54,603 --> 00:52:56,202
I think all of that is important.

1512
00:52:56,203 --> 00:52:58,672
The audience doesn't know what happened on set.

1513
00:52:58,673 --> 00:53:00,172
If the choreography is tight,

1514
00:53:00,173 --> 00:53:01,842
they'll think that person was a good director.

1515
00:53:01,843 --> 00:53:04,842
But who did a better job leading the entire production...

1516
00:53:04,843 --> 00:53:06,942
is also part of what makes someone a good director.

1517
00:53:06,943 --> 00:53:08,912
Personally, I thought both of them fell a little short.

1518
00:53:08,913 --> 00:53:12,782
When NaiN ran into situations outside what she'd expected,

1519
00:53:12,783 --> 00:53:14,982
it took her some time to deal with them.

1520
00:53:14,983 --> 00:53:17,022
NaiN worked hard. She worked hard,

1521
00:53:17,023 --> 00:53:20,193
but she lacks the ability to work in sync with production.

1522
00:53:20,523 --> 00:53:22,992
(The chair isn't supposed to come in right away at the beginning.)

1523
00:53:22,993 --> 00:53:24,132
(It's supposed to be like the draft video.)

1524
00:53:24,133 --> 00:53:26,962
(Please make it as close to this video as possible.)

1525
00:53:26,963 --> 00:53:28,833
(Can we shoot this part from the front?)

1526
00:53:28,903 --> 00:53:29,903
Director.

1527
00:53:29,904 --> 00:53:31,672
NaiN keeps going back to her own draft video.

1528
00:53:31,673 --> 00:53:34,172
For me, that inability to adapt or take things in...

1529
00:53:34,173 --> 00:53:36,242
shows that she's not cut out to be a director.

1530
00:53:36,243 --> 00:53:38,372
First of all, Koo Young's video...

1531
00:53:38,373 --> 00:53:39,412
turned out badly.

1532
00:53:39,413 --> 00:53:41,942
In terms of who directed better or worse,

1533
00:53:41,943 --> 00:53:43,482
I thought they were pretty similar.

1534
00:53:43,483 --> 00:53:44,952
Both shoots ran behind.

1535
00:53:44,953 --> 00:53:47,012
And as far as giving us instructions goes,

1536
00:53:47,013 --> 00:53:48,822
there honestly wasn't that much either of them needed to tell us.

1537
00:53:48,823 --> 00:53:51,022
So I think I'd choose based on whether the video turned out well,

1538
00:53:51,023 --> 00:53:52,822
whether the final product was good.

1539
00:53:52,823 --> 00:53:54,722
And Koo Young's came out kind of chaotic.

1540
00:53:54,723 --> 00:53:56,992
In terms of the visuals themselves, NaiN's video came out better.

1541
00:53:56,993 --> 00:53:59,132
If we're judging pure directing ability, then it's Koo Young.

1542
00:53:59,133 --> 00:54:01,302
NaiN wants something that's very controlled and locked in,

1543
00:54:01,303 --> 00:54:03,202
while Koo Young wants something a little looser and freer.

1544
00:54:03,203 --> 00:54:04,572
With Director Koo Young,

1545
00:54:04,573 --> 00:54:07,372
you can really feel his years of experience.

1546
00:54:07,373 --> 00:54:08,373
But I like it.

1547
00:54:08,374 --> 00:54:10,072
I would've directed like NaiN too.

1548
00:54:10,073 --> 00:54:12,143
I made my choice.

1549
00:54:12,543 --> 00:54:14,782
I chose this person.

1550
00:54:14,783 --> 00:54:17,612
(NaiN versus Back Koo Young)

1551
00:54:17,613 --> 00:54:21,383
(Who did the 8 choreographers, serving as dancers, choose?)

1552
00:54:21,483 --> 00:54:22,652
This is scary.

1553
00:54:22,653 --> 00:54:26,052
Of course, there are definitely things about his years...

1554
00:54:26,053 --> 00:54:28,992
of experience that I simply can't match.

1555
00:54:28,993 --> 00:54:32,762
But I created a video that makes people want to dance,

1556
00:54:32,763 --> 00:54:34,032
so I'm confident.

1557
00:54:34,033 --> 00:54:36,032
I genuinely think I can become the Final Director.

1558
00:54:36,033 --> 00:54:38,473
I believed they were going to choose me.

1559
00:54:38,733 --> 00:54:40,372
(Who will become the Final Director...)

1560
00:54:40,373 --> 00:54:41,973
(in the Title Sequence Film Mission?)

1561
00:54:42,643 --> 00:54:46,143
(Finally, it's time to choose the Final Director.)

1562
00:54:46,513 --> 00:54:48,589
(Between the two, who will become the Final Director?)

1563
00:54:48,613 --> 00:54:49,642
I was confident.

1564
00:54:49,643 --> 00:54:52,152
Because my piece lets each person stand out and look appealing,

1565
00:54:52,153 --> 00:54:55,022
I feel like mine might be a little more convincing...

1566
00:54:55,023 --> 00:54:57,953
to these directors.

1567
00:54:58,593 --> 00:54:59,852
I am nervous.

1568
00:54:59,853 --> 00:55:00,862
But unlike...

1569
00:55:00,863 --> 00:55:03,492
Koo Young's visual style,

1570
00:55:03,493 --> 00:55:05,362
if they prefer clean, tightly organized...

1571
00:55:05,363 --> 00:55:07,232
group choreography,

1572
00:55:07,233 --> 00:55:09,333
then I think they might like my video more.

1573
00:55:10,263 --> 00:55:12,272
I'm really curious about who you picked.

1574
00:55:12,273 --> 00:55:14,643
I just looked at the final result.

1575
00:55:14,843 --> 00:55:17,242
The whole point of the process is to ultimately...

1576
00:55:17,243 --> 00:55:18,712
create a good result.

1577
00:55:18,713 --> 00:55:22,343
I actually went around and casually asked everyone.

1578
00:55:22,413 --> 00:55:24,373
- I have no idea about this one. - Is that right?

1579
00:55:24,683 --> 00:55:26,983
- No idea. - Is it neck and neck?

1580
00:55:27,523 --> 00:55:30,823
(An outcome no one could have predicted)

1581
00:55:31,593 --> 00:55:33,853
- No way! - Goodness.

1582
00:55:34,893 --> 00:55:36,922
- Aiki! - Aiki!

1583
00:55:36,923 --> 00:55:39,232
I'm Aiki, your special MC.

1584
00:55:39,233 --> 00:55:40,393
Hello, everyone.

1585
00:55:40,763 --> 00:55:43,162
(Welcome!)

1586
00:55:43,163 --> 00:55:44,432
Aiki!

1587
00:55:44,433 --> 00:55:46,172
Title Sequence Film Mission.

1588
00:55:46,173 --> 00:55:48,343
Back Koo Young versus NaiN.

1589
00:55:48,543 --> 00:55:50,272
The two director candidates,

1590
00:55:50,273 --> 00:55:53,112
each created a piece that showcased...

1591
00:55:53,113 --> 00:55:56,813
their own distinct style and directing approach.

1592
00:55:57,143 --> 00:55:59,853
Now, with the results moments away...

1593
00:56:00,413 --> 00:56:02,223
- Now? - What else is there?

1594
00:56:02,523 --> 00:56:03,953
The two Director Candidates...

1595
00:56:04,053 --> 00:56:06,369
each chose the choreographer they were least satisfied with...

1596
00:56:06,393 --> 00:56:08,293
as their Worst Director Candidate.

1597
00:56:08,393 --> 00:56:10,663
We'll reveal the Worst Director Candidate.

1598
00:56:11,093 --> 00:56:13,033
We're revealing that first?

1599
00:56:13,433 --> 00:56:15,263
- What do we do? - Oh, my gosh.

1600
00:56:15,763 --> 00:56:17,203
Wait, all of a sudden?

1601
00:56:17,503 --> 00:56:18,503
Could it be...

1602
00:56:18,573 --> 00:56:19,573
Worst Director Candidate.

1603
00:56:19,574 --> 00:56:21,342
I'd be annoyed right off the bat.

1604
00:56:21,343 --> 00:56:23,073
It means they think you did badly.

1605
00:56:23,273 --> 00:56:25,472
I'd bawl my eyes out right there.

1606
00:56:25,473 --> 00:56:28,113
If you're named a Worst Director Candidate,

1607
00:56:28,213 --> 00:56:30,419
I'd say there's a 90% chance you'll go to the Last Stage.

1608
00:56:30,443 --> 00:56:32,482
I always give everything my all,

1609
00:56:32,483 --> 00:56:34,052
so I don't think I'd be the Worst Director Candidate.

1610
00:56:34,053 --> 00:56:35,152
Maybe INGYOO, rather than me?

1611
00:56:35,153 --> 00:56:36,652
INGYOO is naturally free-spirited,

1612
00:56:36,653 --> 00:56:38,652
NaiN likes everything structured.

1613
00:56:38,653 --> 00:56:41,213
So can two complete opposites understand each other? They can't.

1614
00:56:41,493 --> 00:56:43,092
I don't think so. I don't think it's me.

1615
00:56:43,093 --> 00:56:44,433
As long as it's not me.

1616
00:56:44,693 --> 00:56:46,532
How do you even pick someone for elimination here?

1617
00:56:46,533 --> 00:56:48,902
It'll be hard. Everyone worked so hard.

1618
00:56:48,903 --> 00:56:50,203
I have no idea with this one.

1619
00:56:50,303 --> 00:56:53,273
First, Director Candidate Back Koo Young,

1620
00:56:53,373 --> 00:56:55,973
please announce the Worst Director Candidate you chose.

1621
00:56:56,073 --> 00:56:57,743
(Out of my own mouth?)

1622
00:56:57,843 --> 00:56:59,542
(Right after filming, Back Koo Young narrows it down to two.)

1623
00:56:59,543 --> 00:57:03,042
With BABYZOO, a few mistakes...

1624
00:57:03,043 --> 00:57:05,383
cost us a few takes.

1625
00:57:05,553 --> 00:57:09,483
MIN JUN tends to make things too much his own style.

1626
00:57:09,823 --> 00:57:10,852
It didn't quite fit.

1627
00:57:10,853 --> 00:57:12,653
He didn't blend it.

1628
00:57:12,853 --> 00:57:13,892
(Back Koo Young narrowed the Worst Director Candidates down to two.)

1629
00:57:13,893 --> 00:57:14,993
(JEONG MIN JUN, BABYZOO)

1630
00:57:15,393 --> 00:57:17,222
(Who will be the Worst Director Candidate: MIN JUN or BABYZOO?)

1631
00:57:17,223 --> 00:57:20,493
The Worst Director Candidate I chose is...

1632
00:57:20,633 --> 00:57:21,703
BABYZOO.

1633
00:57:23,203 --> 00:57:24,602
(Back Koo Young's Worst Director Candidate, BABYZOO)

1634
00:57:24,603 --> 00:57:26,533
Why? I was so thrown off.

1635
00:57:26,773 --> 00:57:28,773
(Worst Director Candidate, BABYZOO)

1636
00:57:29,543 --> 00:57:31,073
No way. Why?

1637
00:57:31,173 --> 00:57:32,712
Is this for real?

1638
00:57:32,713 --> 00:57:34,243
No.

1639
00:57:34,743 --> 00:57:36,612
Why? BABYZOO is so good...

1640
00:57:36,613 --> 00:57:39,612
so I couldn't help but question it.

1641
00:57:39,613 --> 00:57:43,182
During the shoot, BABYZOO...

1642
00:57:43,183 --> 00:57:44,623
messed up that get-up a few times...

1643
00:57:44,653 --> 00:57:47,863
so we ended up with unusable takes.

1644
00:57:47,993 --> 00:57:49,592
What feels a little unfair is...

1645
00:57:49,593 --> 00:57:51,062
I got it in 2, 3 tries.

1646
00:57:51,063 --> 00:57:54,032
If I were the director and... the dancers were struggling,

1647
00:57:54,033 --> 00:57:55,863
wouldn't some of that be on me too?

1648
00:57:55,963 --> 00:57:57,872
It wasn't choosing a candidate,

1649
00:57:57,873 --> 00:58:00,072
but finding a reason to pick one...

1650
00:58:00,073 --> 00:58:01,743
that took me a really long time.

1651
00:58:02,543 --> 00:58:03,643
I don't know.

1652
00:58:03,943 --> 00:58:06,042
If Koo Young becomes the director...

1653
00:58:06,043 --> 00:58:08,942
there's probably a good chance I'll end up on the Last Stage.

1654
00:58:08,943 --> 00:58:12,453
Can I really vote...

1655
00:58:12,683 --> 00:58:15,223
without any emotion at all under these circumstances?

1656
00:58:15,983 --> 00:58:20,023
Then who did NaiN choose as her Worst Director Candidate?

1657
00:58:20,193 --> 00:58:21,492
I really have no idea who it'll be.

1658
00:58:21,493 --> 00:58:23,222
Oh, dear.

1659
00:58:23,223 --> 00:58:26,793
During the shoot, it was Renan and Hash.

1660
00:58:27,163 --> 00:58:30,902
(Renan repeatedly missed the timing.)

1661
00:58:30,903 --> 00:58:32,772
It felt like Hash didn't give it everything.

1662
00:58:32,773 --> 00:58:33,849
(Hash didn't show full potential)

1663
00:58:33,873 --> 00:58:37,843
The Worst Director Candidate I chose is...

1664
00:58:38,373 --> 00:58:40,143
I honestly wasn't worried.

1665
00:58:40,243 --> 00:58:45,152
Her directing style was very similar to what I aim for.

1666
00:58:45,153 --> 00:58:46,183
I worked hard...

1667
00:58:46,513 --> 00:58:48,659
so I didn't think I'd be the Worst Director Candidate.

1668
00:58:48,683 --> 00:58:51,653
I'd be really upset if NaiN picked me.

1669
00:58:54,193 --> 00:58:55,663
It's Renan.

1670
00:58:55,763 --> 00:58:57,692
(Worst Director Candidate, Renan)

1671
00:58:57,693 --> 00:58:59,193
She picked me as the Worst?

1672
00:58:59,393 --> 00:59:01,663
I was going to vote for NaiN...

1673
00:59:01,963 --> 00:59:03,163
but this makes no sense.

1674
00:59:03,633 --> 00:59:05,332
(Worst Director Candidate, Renan)

1675
00:59:05,333 --> 00:59:08,543
The chair part was really tough...

1676
00:59:08,873 --> 00:59:12,272
If she'd seen how hard I practiced off to the side,

1677
00:59:12,273 --> 00:59:14,019
I don't think she would've picked me as the Worst Director Candidate.

1678
00:59:14,043 --> 00:59:16,813
I really hope Koo Young becomes the Director.

1679
00:59:16,943 --> 00:59:18,612
I think it was because of the chair part.

1680
00:59:18,613 --> 00:59:19,613
I think so.

1681
00:59:19,614 --> 00:59:21,523
At rehearsals and during filming...

1682
00:59:21,653 --> 00:59:23,852
It's nerve-racking because everyone's so good.

1683
00:59:23,853 --> 00:59:27,022
One small mistake could make me the Worst Director Candidate.

1684
00:59:27,023 --> 00:59:28,663
So I need to stay fully focused.

1685
00:59:28,823 --> 00:59:31,392
After NaiN picked me,

1686
00:59:31,393 --> 00:59:33,633
I really hoped Koo Young would get it.

1687
00:59:33,733 --> 00:59:35,603
I couldn't help but feel that way.

1688
00:59:35,863 --> 00:59:37,772
I really don't want to go to the Last Stage anymore.

1689
00:59:37,773 --> 00:59:39,632
I hope NaiN gets it.

1690
00:59:39,633 --> 00:59:41,373
I really, really hope she does.

1691
00:59:41,643 --> 00:59:43,563
The Worst Director Candidates revealed so far...

1692
00:59:43,643 --> 00:59:45,612
- are just candidates. - Right.

1693
00:59:45,613 --> 00:59:47,583
No one is safe.

1694
00:59:47,743 --> 00:59:50,612
The eight choreographers who didn't become Director Candidates...

1695
00:59:50,613 --> 00:59:54,652
and the Director Candidate who misses out on the final spot.

1696
00:59:54,653 --> 00:59:56,552
The nine choreographers...

1697
00:59:56,553 --> 00:59:59,423
will be evaluated by the Final Director and the judges...

1698
00:59:59,523 --> 01:00:03,393
to determine who goes to the Last Stage.

1699
01:00:03,563 --> 01:00:06,463
The number of choreographers going to the first Last Stage is...

1700
01:00:06,863 --> 01:00:09,262
- She's saying it. - Please!

1701
01:00:09,263 --> 01:00:11,972
- Please. - Let it be as few as possible.

1702
01:00:11,973 --> 01:00:13,773
This is seriously so scary.

1703
01:00:14,673 --> 01:00:15,673
Three.

1704
01:00:16,143 --> 01:00:17,819
(A total of 3 out of 9 will go to the Last Stage.)

1705
01:00:17,843 --> 01:00:19,543
That's brutal. Three people.

1706
01:00:19,773 --> 01:00:21,412
Two get eliminated, and only one survives.

1707
01:00:21,413 --> 01:00:22,413
That's true.

1708
01:00:22,414 --> 01:00:26,353
Only one of the three can survive.

1709
01:00:26,483 --> 01:00:28,123
Only one survives.

1710
01:00:28,223 --> 01:00:29,483
That's seriously brutal.

1711
01:00:29,583 --> 01:00:32,193
That's the cruelest number. The absolute cruelest.

1712
01:00:32,293 --> 01:00:35,163
Two go home and one survives. That's what makes it thrilling.

1713
01:00:35,693 --> 01:00:36,693
That's seriously brutal.

1714
01:00:36,793 --> 01:00:38,963
It's like surviving a fire pit.

1715
01:00:39,393 --> 01:00:40,533
They must be desperate.

1716
01:00:40,763 --> 01:00:42,133
I just hope it's not me.

1717
01:00:42,233 --> 01:00:45,973
I seriously don't want to go to the Last Stage. No matter what.

1718
01:00:46,533 --> 01:00:47,673
This is already painful.

1719
01:00:48,073 --> 01:00:51,243
I just have to nail everything and give it my all.

1720
01:00:51,643 --> 01:00:54,443
As someone who always considers the worst-case scenario,

1721
01:00:54,713 --> 01:00:57,342
it's better to prepare myself than not be prepared at all.

1722
01:00:57,343 --> 01:01:00,883
Still, I'll stay laser-focused and give it everything I've got.

1723
01:01:01,223 --> 01:01:02,483
Will they survive...

1724
01:01:02,583 --> 01:01:06,192
or become the star of the very first Last Stage?

1725
01:01:06,193 --> 01:01:07,522
I really don't want to be that star.

1726
01:01:07,523 --> 01:01:11,563
And the one person who gets the greatest authority...

1727
01:01:11,633 --> 01:01:12,633
The director

1728
01:01:13,493 --> 01:01:16,162
We will now announce...

1729
01:01:16,163 --> 01:01:18,272
the Final Director of the Title Sequence Film Mission.

1730
01:01:18,273 --> 01:01:19,532
(Tension)

1731
01:01:19,533 --> 01:01:22,172
If I go to the Last Stage as the Worst Director Candidate,

1732
01:01:22,173 --> 01:01:24,473
wouldn't that feel absolutely awful?

1733
01:01:24,573 --> 01:01:26,713
I have to be the Final Director.

1734
01:01:27,073 --> 01:01:28,383
I've come this far.

1735
01:01:28,483 --> 01:01:30,243
I don't think I can let this go.

1736
01:01:30,443 --> 01:01:33,352
First, let's take a look at...

1737
01:01:33,353 --> 01:01:36,153
Director Candidate Back Koo Young's final concept video.

1738
01:01:36,253 --> 01:01:37,483
(He means it will be fun.)

1739
01:01:38,023 --> 01:01:39,953
- Let's see. - Okay.

1740
01:01:40,823 --> 01:01:42,562
But I purposely didn't watch it...

1741
01:01:42,563 --> 01:01:44,003
because I thought I'd figure it out.

1742
01:01:44,093 --> 01:01:45,163
There's a bit of tension.

1743
01:01:45,463 --> 01:01:48,603
I focused on the idea of a film that represents all of us,

1744
01:01:48,703 --> 01:01:51,433
and tried to showcase everyone.

1745
01:01:51,773 --> 01:01:54,273
I hope that came through well.

1746
01:01:55,343 --> 01:01:56,343
Yes!

1747
01:01:56,873 --> 01:01:58,413
The intro feels a little lacking.

1748
01:01:59,313 --> 01:02:00,773
It might be a little bland.

1749
01:02:08,183 --> 01:02:09,282
(The scene that led BABYZOO to be named Worst Director Candidate)

1750
01:02:09,283 --> 01:02:10,422
Yes!

1751
01:02:10,423 --> 01:02:12,323
The hat is so cute.

1752
01:02:16,593 --> 01:02:19,093
I think it came out really clean.

1753
01:02:22,203 --> 01:02:23,303
Yes!

1754
01:02:24,133 --> 01:02:25,372
Yes!

1755
01:02:25,373 --> 01:02:26,933
Koo Young was neat,

1756
01:02:27,033 --> 01:02:28,273
and everyone stands out.

1757
01:02:28,473 --> 01:02:30,343
I stood out too.

1758
01:02:30,573 --> 01:02:34,343
It opens up space for each person to dance.

1759
01:02:34,713 --> 01:02:37,382
There are too many added zoom-ins and zoom-outs in post,

1760
01:02:37,383 --> 01:02:38,463
so it feels really chaotic.

1761
01:02:40,483 --> 01:02:41,523
I love it.

1762
01:02:44,423 --> 01:02:45,753
(Loving it)

1763
01:02:47,993 --> 01:02:49,422
It feels too divided up?

1764
01:02:49,423 --> 01:02:52,062
In parts that could've had more group choreography,

1765
01:02:52,063 --> 01:02:53,263
we split up too often.

1766
01:02:56,063 --> 01:02:58,233
And we only dance together briefly in the chorus,

1767
01:02:58,333 --> 01:03:00,173
so that was a little disappointing.

1768
01:03:09,643 --> 01:03:11,253
You can really see each person.

1769
01:03:12,083 --> 01:03:13,482
(Well done, everyone.)

1770
01:03:13,483 --> 01:03:14,553
It turned out really well.

1771
01:03:14,653 --> 01:03:17,452
I didn't set a strict framework and make them follow it.

1772
01:03:17,453 --> 01:03:19,292
With the choreography I gave them,

1773
01:03:19,293 --> 01:03:21,593
they developed it in their style.

1774
01:03:21,693 --> 01:03:23,562
And in that respect,

1775
01:03:23,563 --> 01:03:25,963
I trusted they'd choose me.

1776
01:03:26,193 --> 01:03:29,532
The way the choreography transitioned...

1777
01:03:29,533 --> 01:03:31,302
felt a bit like what I do.

1778
01:03:31,303 --> 01:03:32,872
Comparing the two,

1779
01:03:32,873 --> 01:03:36,642
I thought mine felt cleaner and more polished.

1780
01:03:36,643 --> 01:03:38,143
I really want it now.

1781
01:03:41,913 --> 01:03:44,243
This is going to be so close.

1782
01:03:46,713 --> 01:03:49,853
All ten vary in intensity,

1783
01:03:49,953 --> 01:03:51,723
style, and the aura they give off.

1784
01:03:52,093 --> 01:03:54,463
But she seems to want them all to dance in NaiN's style.

1785
01:04:01,903 --> 01:04:03,203
I love this part so much.

1786
01:04:04,203 --> 01:04:06,272
Technically, it fell a bit short.

1787
01:04:06,273 --> 01:04:08,543
It's something other dancers could've done too.

1788
01:04:10,843 --> 01:04:11,843
(The key moment that made Renan a Worst Director Candidate)

1789
01:04:11,844 --> 01:04:13,912
The concept had a pillar to kick,

1790
01:04:13,913 --> 01:04:15,012
but it wasn't there when I did it.

1791
01:04:15,013 --> 01:04:16,213
So of course it was difficult.

1792
01:04:24,453 --> 01:04:26,352
It was compact and clean.

1793
01:04:26,353 --> 01:04:28,163
It was simply well organized.

1794
01:04:28,323 --> 01:04:30,092
It had to feel fresher than mine.

1795
01:04:30,093 --> 01:04:32,093
Because hers is way trendier.

1796
01:04:32,293 --> 01:04:34,163
Mine felt a little fresher to me.

1797
01:04:38,573 --> 01:04:41,543
We went from using mirrors to using acrylic...

1798
01:04:41,973 --> 01:04:44,843
NaiN's concept felt like a fresher experience to me.

1799
01:04:51,383 --> 01:04:54,523
NaiN's concept video was..

1800
01:04:54,983 --> 01:04:56,723
Like a super polished artist demo.

1801
01:05:00,323 --> 01:05:02,363
(Agrees)

1802
01:05:02,463 --> 01:05:04,493
It came out as well as I'd imagined.

1803
01:05:04,593 --> 01:05:05,862
It's clean,

1804
01:05:05,863 --> 01:05:08,763
and the camera transitions are really tightly packed.

1805
01:05:09,533 --> 01:05:11,372
If they like what I like,

1806
01:05:11,373 --> 01:05:12,873
I think they would've chosen me.

1807
01:05:13,073 --> 01:05:15,743
I need five director votes.

1808
01:05:16,173 --> 01:05:17,473
I think I can get them.

1809
01:05:18,573 --> 01:05:20,343
All evaluations are now complete.

1810
01:05:20,573 --> 01:05:23,913
The Final Director of the Title Sequence Film Mission...

1811
01:05:24,183 --> 01:05:26,389
will be decided without votes from the two Director Candidates,

1812
01:05:26,413 --> 01:05:28,622
using the other eight choreographers' votes...

1813
01:05:28,623 --> 01:05:31,822
plus one Public Judge vote.

1814
01:05:31,823 --> 01:05:33,452
Based on today's result,

1815
01:05:33,453 --> 01:05:36,263
the Director Candidate who doesn't become Final Director...

1816
01:05:36,423 --> 01:05:39,263
could go to the Last Stage.

1817
01:05:39,363 --> 01:05:41,362
I really don't want to go.

1818
01:05:41,363 --> 01:05:42,732
It's the worst.

1819
01:05:42,733 --> 01:05:44,533
One person will gain authority...

1820
01:05:44,633 --> 01:05:46,572
while another faces a crisis.

1821
01:05:46,573 --> 01:05:50,243
Who will become the Final Director?

1822
01:05:50,343 --> 01:05:52,073
It's not even me. Why am I so nervous?

1823
01:05:52,613 --> 01:05:54,112
I don't know. I'm nervous.

1824
01:05:54,113 --> 01:05:56,982
Which director candidate will win the Public Judges' vote...

1825
01:05:56,983 --> 01:05:58,553
and secure one vote?

1826
01:05:58,583 --> 01:06:00,013
Let's reveal it now.

1827
01:06:00,053 --> 01:06:01,382
I think the public...

1828
01:06:01,383 --> 01:06:02,822
likes NaiN.

1829
01:06:02,823 --> 01:06:04,152
Based on the demo,

1830
01:06:04,153 --> 01:06:06,052
I liked NaiN's choreography.

1831
01:06:06,053 --> 01:06:07,352
I wanted to perform it.

1832
01:06:07,353 --> 01:06:08,662
If Koo Young becomes the director,

1833
01:06:08,663 --> 01:06:11,233
I'll end up in the Last Stage.

1834
01:06:11,333 --> 01:06:12,932
I think Koo Young will be chosen.

1835
01:06:12,933 --> 01:06:14,093
The public will vote for him.

1836
01:06:14,163 --> 01:06:15,632
I'm a hype meter.

1837
01:06:15,633 --> 01:06:17,703
I thought Koo Young's video was nice.

1838
