Why on earth? How should I understand it?

2104
01:15:54,373 --> 01:15:57,542
BABYZOO worked so hard and did a good job during rehearsal.

2105
01:15:57,543 --> 01:15:59,212
His hips spilled out a few times.

2106
01:15:59,213 --> 01:16:00,852
I was like, "Could he actually become the worst candidate?"

2107
01:16:00,853 --> 01:16:02,183
I was really shocked.

2108
01:16:02,583 --> 01:16:04,183
But I'm just the worst "candidate."

2109
01:16:04,283 --> 01:16:05,992
When you put that kind of pressure on us,

2110
01:16:05,993 --> 01:16:07,852
we're able to keep refining things...

2111
01:16:07,853 --> 01:16:09,062
until we come up with something better.

2112
01:16:09,063 --> 01:16:11,262
That's one of a director's strengths.

2113
01:16:11,263 --> 01:16:12,692
He found my weakness.

2114
01:16:12,693 --> 01:16:15,132
That means I should conceal it from now on.

2115
01:16:15,133 --> 01:16:16,732
I need to work on my weaknesses...

2116
01:16:16,733 --> 01:16:18,832
and create an even bigger wow factor.

2117
01:16:18,833 --> 01:16:20,402
All I can think about is making up for what I lost.

2118
01:16:20,403 --> 01:16:21,403
"Making up."

2119
01:16:21,404 --> 01:16:23,242
I feel so bad...

2120
01:16:23,243 --> 01:16:25,672
about choosing someone as the worst candidate.

2121
01:16:25,673 --> 01:16:27,073
I feel sorry.

2122
01:16:27,473 --> 01:16:29,742
But that's my priority.

2123
01:16:29,743 --> 01:16:32,053
I'll have to think about it a lot.

2124
01:16:33,953 --> 01:16:35,422
- Oh, no. - No way.

2125
01:16:35,423 --> 01:16:36,783
Please change the sound.

2126
01:16:36,983 --> 01:16:38,053
It startled me.

2127
01:16:38,283 --> 01:16:40,553
Why are you doing this to me?

2128
01:16:41,863 --> 01:16:43,393
(I see.)

2129
01:16:43,993 --> 01:16:45,662
(Director's seat)

2130
01:16:45,663 --> 01:16:46,863
(Running)

2131
01:16:47,533 --> 01:16:49,103
(1 second of being a director)

2132
01:16:50,103 --> 01:16:51,802
Now, Koo Young is not only a director...

2133
01:16:51,803 --> 01:16:53,433
but also a judge.

2134
01:16:55,003 --> 01:16:56,343
(Relaxed and chill)

2135
01:16:56,543 --> 01:16:58,073
Here comes the director.

2136
01:16:59,273 --> 01:17:00,642
(They welcome their director with loud cheers.)

2137
01:17:00,643 --> 01:17:02,643
(They don't stop cheering.)

2138
01:17:03,643 --> 01:17:05,352
Here comes the director.

2139
01:17:05,353 --> 01:17:07,152
I can already feel the taste of power.

2140
01:17:07,153 --> 01:17:09,182
- He's different from earlier. - I know.

2141
01:17:09,183 --> 01:17:11,223
- Right. - He couldn't even look up earlier.

2142
01:17:11,623 --> 01:17:13,453
I'm so jealous of his position.

2143
01:17:13,653 --> 01:17:15,122
Where's the red carpet?

2144
01:17:15,123 --> 01:17:16,622
(Without hesitation)

2145
01:17:16,623 --> 01:17:18,362
(100 points for flattery)

2146
01:17:18,363 --> 01:17:19,433
He just earned 100 points.

2147
01:17:20,233 --> 01:17:22,579
Hello, it's nice to see all of you, the best choreographers.

2148
01:17:22,603 --> 01:17:23,963
I'm Director Back Koo Young.

2149
01:17:24,363 --> 01:17:26,932
(Praising Koo Young)

2150
01:17:26,933 --> 01:17:30,102
This is the announcement for the best choreographers.

2151
01:17:30,103 --> 01:17:31,773
I'm so scared.

2152
01:17:31,973 --> 01:17:35,742
As the director, I wanted to commission choreography...

2153
01:17:35,743 --> 01:17:37,843
from three choreographers.

2154
01:17:38,043 --> 01:17:39,982
I was always the one receiving commissions,

2155
01:17:39,983 --> 01:17:41,412
so being the one giving the orders for once...

2156
01:17:41,413 --> 01:17:43,329
really made me realize that I became a director.

2157
01:17:43,353 --> 01:17:45,322
He won't be both the director and the choreographer.

2158
01:17:45,323 --> 01:17:48,292
He'll only direct.

2159
01:17:48,293 --> 01:17:49,362
I envied him so much.

2160
01:17:49,363 --> 01:17:50,422
The request is...

2161
01:17:50,423 --> 01:17:53,192
to create choreography that showcases the director.

2162
01:17:53,193 --> 01:17:54,632
Choreography that showcases you or us?

2163
01:17:54,633 --> 01:17:56,162
The director.

2164
01:17:56,163 --> 01:17:58,103
- We're not directors now. - Oh, right.

2165
01:17:58,633 --> 01:18:01,473
We had our director titles taken away for a while.

2166
01:18:01,673 --> 01:18:04,003
So Koo Young is the only director now.

2167
01:18:04,173 --> 01:18:05,642
The three choreographers...

2168
01:18:05,643 --> 01:18:08,273
will present their original choreography to the director.

2169
01:18:08,443 --> 01:18:10,843
After the director's final review,

2170
01:18:11,043 --> 01:18:13,183
only one choreography will be selected.

2171
01:18:13,353 --> 01:18:15,052
The chosen choreographer...

2172
01:18:15,053 --> 01:18:17,823
will be credited as the choreographer.

2173
01:18:18,053 --> 01:18:20,852
I chose the section of the song.

2174
01:18:20,853 --> 01:18:22,792
(Individual Choreography Section)

2175
01:18:22,793 --> 01:18:25,932
This is the outro of the song.

2176
01:18:25,933 --> 01:18:27,132
(The choreographers must create choreography for the outro...)

2177
01:18:27,133 --> 01:18:28,392
(of the title track, with the goal of making the director stand out.)

2178
01:18:28,393 --> 01:18:29,463
The outro.

2179
01:18:29,733 --> 01:18:30,762
It's the outro.

2180
01:18:30,763 --> 01:18:32,923
So they will create choreography for the same section.

2181
01:18:33,033 --> 01:18:34,102
It's a competition.

2182
01:18:34,103 --> 01:18:37,873
The three choreographers I want to commission are...

2183
01:18:38,043 --> 01:18:39,872
I hope he commissions me.

2184
01:18:39,873 --> 01:18:41,073
It's my chance to earn points.

2185
01:18:41,273 --> 01:18:44,282
Koo Young has never chosen me.

2186
01:18:44,283 --> 01:18:46,583
I really hope he picks me.

2187
01:18:47,013 --> 01:18:49,182
I'm the only one he chose as the worst candidate.

2188
01:18:49,183 --> 01:18:51,453
I think I have to show something now.

2189
01:18:51,993 --> 01:18:55,523
The three choreographers I want to commission are...

2190
01:18:56,023 --> 01:18:58,493
BADA, INGYOO, and BABYZOO.

2191
01:19:00,193 --> 01:19:03,562
I think BADA will bring out unique energy.

2192
01:19:03,563 --> 01:19:05,503
I like INGYOO's choreography style.

2193
01:19:05,573 --> 01:19:07,932
And BABYZOO knows how to make my choreography work.

2194
01:19:07,933 --> 01:19:10,572
If he creates the choreography with me in mind,

2195
01:19:10,573 --> 01:19:12,412
I think I'll ll be able to pull it off really well too.

2196
01:19:12,413 --> 01:19:14,573
His choreography is absolutely amazing.

2197
01:19:15,043 --> 01:19:17,042
Since this choreography will be the finale of the film,

2198
01:19:17,043 --> 01:19:19,513
please make it amazing.

2199
01:19:21,453 --> 01:19:24,322
I was disappointed that I wasn't included.

2200
01:19:24,323 --> 01:19:26,622
As soon as I heard the outro, I was confident.

2201
01:19:26,623 --> 01:19:28,503
I'm upset I can't create choreography for that.

2202
01:19:28,893 --> 01:19:31,292
I feel like I was given a chance to make up for my mistake.

2203
01:19:31,293 --> 01:19:32,933
I'll do my best.

2204
01:19:33,233 --> 01:19:35,802
I'll give it my all...

2205
01:19:35,803 --> 01:19:37,503
to earn that choreographer credit.

2206
01:19:37,733 --> 01:19:39,532
I'll serve him beautifully polished choreography...

2207
01:19:39,533 --> 01:19:42,072
on a silver platter,

2208
01:19:42,073 --> 01:19:43,172
so he can turn it into something amazing.

2209
01:19:43,173 --> 01:19:44,173
Skrr.

2210
01:19:44,174 --> 01:19:45,842
The second announcement...

2211
01:19:45,843 --> 01:19:47,372
is to create choreography in groups of three...

2212
01:19:47,373 --> 01:19:50,542
for the Director's Cut section.

2213
01:19:50,543 --> 01:19:54,182
The 9 choreographers will form teams of 3...

2214
01:19:54,183 --> 01:19:55,352
and create not only the choreography,

2215
01:19:55,353 --> 01:19:58,023
but also the formations and overall staging.

2216
01:19:58,153 --> 01:20:01,293
Let me play the music section for you.

2217
01:20:04,323 --> 01:20:06,062
(Director's Cut Choreography Section)

2218
01:20:06,063 --> 01:20:07,762
(A 7-second section following the 1st chorus)

2219
01:20:07,763 --> 01:20:11,633
(Requirement: The car trunk must be incorporated.)

2220
01:20:11,803 --> 01:20:15,873
All three drafts will be filmed during the shoot.

2221
01:20:16,143 --> 01:20:18,712
After filming all three versions,

2222
01:20:18,713 --> 01:20:21,672
the director will select the version that works best...

2223
01:20:21,673 --> 01:20:23,659
during post-production and use it in the final film.

2224
01:20:23,683 --> 01:20:26,163
So he'll film all 3 groups, but only 1 of them will be chosen.

2225
01:20:26,283 --> 01:20:28,353
This is the final announcement.

2226
01:20:28,683 --> 01:20:30,782
Additional choreography from the draft may be selected.

2227
01:20:30,783 --> 01:20:33,522
If I want to use...

2228
01:20:33,523 --> 01:20:35,092
a memorable part of a draft,

2229
01:20:35,093 --> 01:20:37,522
I will approach the choreographer,

2230
01:20:37,523 --> 01:20:40,193
ask for permission, and use their choreography in the final film.

2231
01:20:40,393 --> 01:20:42,132
All choreographers whose choreography makes it...

2232
01:20:42,133 --> 01:20:44,502
into the final film through any of the three categories...

2233
01:20:44,503 --> 01:20:47,173
will be credited.

2234
01:20:47,903 --> 01:20:48,903
What about the others?

2235
01:20:48,904 --> 01:20:50,143
Using them as dancers?

2236
01:20:50,373 --> 01:20:53,142
Those who do not receive a choreography credit...

2237
01:20:53,143 --> 01:20:55,443
will participate in the mission as dancers.

2238
01:20:55,483 --> 01:20:57,782
I want to participate as a choreographer.

2239
01:20:57,783 --> 01:21:00,052
I want to add my name to the credits.

2240
01:21:00,053 --> 01:21:02,252
I want to earn the title of choreographer...

2241
01:21:02,253 --> 01:21:04,282
so I don't end up as just a dancer.

2242
01:21:04,283 --> 01:21:07,293
That's how I can avoid the Last Stage.

2243
01:21:07,623 --> 01:21:11,193
Choreographers and directors are considered to contribute more,

2244
01:21:11,393 --> 01:21:12,832
so being credited only as a dancer...

2245
01:21:12,833 --> 01:21:15,193
would increase my chances of ending up in the Last Stage.

2246
01:21:15,633 --> 01:21:17,802
For the Director's Cut Choreography Section,

2247
01:21:17,803 --> 01:21:21,873
please split into 3 groups of 3.

2248
01:21:22,003 --> 01:21:23,302
(They start teaming up.)

2249
01:21:23,303 --> 01:21:24,703
What do I do?

2250
01:21:24,773 --> 01:21:27,043
Should we turn around and wait to be chosen?

2251
01:21:27,373 --> 01:21:29,143
Anyone who wants to work with me?

2252
01:21:29,383 --> 01:21:30,442
Who wants to team up with me?

2253
01:21:30,443 --> 01:21:32,042
You can use my body however you want.

2254
01:21:32,043 --> 01:21:33,152
I need to be part of the Director's Cut.

2255
01:21:33,153 --> 01:21:34,552
I need to make my presence felt...

2256
01:21:34,553 --> 01:21:37,123
to lower my chances of ending up in the Last Stage.

2257
01:21:37,253 --> 01:21:38,583
What do I do?

2258
01:21:39,223 --> 01:21:40,893
- Oh, my gosh. - So this is how it goes?

2259
01:21:41,353 --> 01:21:44,763
They just let us choose like that. I was rather perplexed.

2260
01:21:44,823 --> 01:21:46,092
(Reading the room)

2261
01:21:46,093 --> 01:21:48,133
We were all trying to read each other.

2262
01:21:48,633 --> 01:21:50,402
I was flustered. I'm the worst candidate, after all.

2263
01:21:50,403 --> 01:21:52,323
I was like, "No one would want to work with me."

2264
01:21:52,733 --> 01:21:53,733
What do I do?

2265
01:21:53,734 --> 01:21:56,002
The song is intense. There's no room to breathe.

2266
01:21:56,003 --> 01:21:57,142
I'm confident I can deliver intense choreography.

2267
01:21:57,143 --> 01:21:59,342
Look at my arms. This part is perfect for waacking.

2268
01:21:59,343 --> 01:22:01,172
- I can tell. - I can turn like crazy.

2269
01:22:01,173 --> 01:22:04,042
- I can do both. - I can do anything.

2270
01:22:04,043 --> 01:22:06,052
- I can do both. - I...

2271
01:22:06,053 --> 01:22:07,212
- Dancing, technique... - I can do anything.

2272
01:22:07,213 --> 01:22:08,382
I've got it all.

2273
01:22:08,383 --> 01:22:11,323
- It's perfect for waacking. - I'll deliver a flashy performance.

2274
01:22:11,423 --> 01:22:12,792
You need these moves.

2275
01:22:12,793 --> 01:22:14,222
Fast-paced, intense choreography is my specialty.

2276
01:22:14,223 --> 01:22:15,253
I mean...

2277
01:22:15,593 --> 01:22:17,162
- Why is it so hilarious? - I can deliver intense moves...

2278
01:22:17,163 --> 01:22:18,723
in a different way.

2279
01:22:19,233 --> 01:22:21,032
They were all trying to convince them.

2280
01:22:21,033 --> 01:22:23,502
I didn't want to beg them to team up with me.

2281
01:22:23,503 --> 01:22:25,009
I was confident I'd do well no matter who I worked with.

2282
01:22:25,033 --> 01:22:27,172
Tell us how you want to structure the choreography.

2283
01:22:27,173 --> 01:22:28,902
How about we team up with people who have similar ideas?

2284
01:22:28,903 --> 01:22:30,003
Hold on. Let me think.

2285
01:22:30,443 --> 01:22:31,873
But it doesn't actually matter.

2286
01:22:32,043 --> 01:22:33,819
BABYZOO, MIN JUN, do you want to team up with me?

2287
01:22:33,843 --> 01:22:35,072
(What?)

2288
01:22:35,073 --> 01:22:36,142
I was like, "This will never end."

2289
01:22:36,143 --> 01:22:37,282
So I picked them first.

2290
01:22:37,283 --> 01:22:39,813
In moments like that, you have to take the lead.

2291
01:22:40,253 --> 01:22:41,353
- Step back. - What?

2292
01:22:41,483 --> 01:22:42,522
"What's going on?"

2293
01:22:42,523 --> 01:22:44,253
"What? BABYZOO is mine."

2294
01:22:44,383 --> 01:22:46,752
Hash, do you want to work with me?

2295
01:22:46,753 --> 01:22:48,352
- Sorry? - Do you want to team up with me?

2296
01:22:48,353 --> 01:22:50,193
I do. Very much.

2297
01:22:50,263 --> 01:22:52,492
I'd love to see how your choreography...

2298
01:22:52,493 --> 01:22:55,093
- Me? Let's work together then. - works with my body.

2299
01:22:55,903 --> 01:22:57,062
You can do this, right?

2300
01:22:57,063 --> 01:22:58,262
- I'll take him. - No.

2301
01:22:58,263 --> 01:22:59,672
- I want him. - Okay.

2302
01:22:59,673 --> 01:23:00,902
No.

2303
01:23:00,903 --> 01:23:02,703
- No. - Come with me.

2304
01:23:02,873 --> 01:23:04,242
BABYZOO is popular.

2305
01:23:04,243 --> 01:23:05,843
- You choose. - Wait.

2306
01:23:06,013 --> 01:23:07,872
Actually, I want him too.

2307
01:23:07,873 --> 01:23:09,883
- Wait. - Okay. You choose. Step up.

2308
01:23:10,183 --> 01:23:12,452
- I want to work with him. - So it's all of us.

2309
01:23:12,453 --> 01:23:13,512
I was just perplexed.

2310
01:23:13,513 --> 01:23:16,922
I'm the worst candidate. There's no way they'd choose me.

2311
01:23:16,923 --> 01:23:18,282
But I guess they wanted to work with me...

2312
01:23:18,283 --> 01:23:20,893
because they saw my potential.

2313
01:23:21,693 --> 01:23:23,222
I want to join you.

2314
01:23:23,223 --> 01:23:24,262
- Okay. - I want to join you.

2315
01:23:24,263 --> 01:23:26,832
I was actually thinking about the three of us as a team.

2316
01:23:26,833 --> 01:23:28,832
Hold on. I'm sorry.

2317
01:23:28,833 --> 01:23:30,232
- I'm so sorry. - Please come to us.

2318
01:23:30,233 --> 01:23:31,362
You know what we can do.

2319
01:23:31,363 --> 01:23:32,672
Don't you think the three of us would have incredible chemistry?

2320
01:23:32,673 --> 01:23:34,532
- We can do anything. - Yes. We can do anything.

2321
01:23:34,533 --> 01:23:36,502
You should bring lots of ideas...

2322
01:23:36,503 --> 01:23:38,473
- Wait. - and show them something different.

2323
01:23:38,943 --> 01:23:41,372
The timing was perfect.

2324
01:23:41,373 --> 01:23:42,483
Hold on.

2325
01:23:42,983 --> 01:23:46,153
If I consider how we'd look in the video...

2326
01:23:47,013 --> 01:23:48,752
BABYZOO, I'll make it up to you...

2327
01:23:48,753 --> 01:23:51,423
for being chosen as the worst candidate.

2328
01:23:52,183 --> 01:23:54,053
(Wavering)

2329
01:23:54,123 --> 01:23:56,892
No way. He told me to work together first.

2330
01:23:56,893 --> 01:23:58,163
He won't betray me.

2331
01:23:58,293 --> 01:23:59,362
I need BABYZOO.

2332
01:23:59,363 --> 01:24:01,693
I needed BABAYZOO to be in the highlight.

2333
01:24:03,433 --> 01:24:05,102
Hash, I'm so sorry.

2334
01:24:05,103 --> 01:24:07,032
- Sorry for what? - I want to join the guys.

2335
01:24:07,033 --> 01:24:08,302
I think I'll stand out...

2336
01:24:08,303 --> 01:24:09,623
- among the guys. - You're sorry?

2337
01:24:09,673 --> 01:24:11,202
- I'm so sorry. - You suggested...

2338
01:24:11,203 --> 01:24:13,272
- we work together first. - I...

2339
01:24:13,273 --> 01:24:14,642
- This situation is... - This is...

2340
01:24:14,643 --> 01:24:16,383
terrifying.

2341
01:24:16,883 --> 01:24:17,983
It's driving me nuts.

2342
01:24:18,843 --> 01:24:20,682
No, it isn't your fault. It's mine.

2343
01:24:20,683 --> 01:24:22,383
- I'm sorry. - No, it's not your fault.

2344
01:24:22,983 --> 01:24:24,899
As long as we create great choreography, we'll be fine.

2345
01:24:24,923 --> 01:24:26,492
(Bitter)

2346
01:24:26,493 --> 01:24:29,022
The three of us have very distinct personalities.

2347
01:24:29,023 --> 01:24:30,993
Good. I'm confident in my distinct style.

2348
01:24:31,123 --> 01:24:32,293
- Let's do it. - Okay!

2349
01:24:32,933 --> 01:24:35,092
- The three of us will team up. - We'll work together.

2350
01:24:35,093 --> 01:24:36,662
(NaiN, BADA, and Simeez teamed up.)

2351
01:24:36,663 --> 01:24:38,303
Shall we...

2352
01:24:38,563 --> 01:24:39,933
- The 3 of us? - The 3 of us?

2353
01:24:40,003 --> 01:24:42,373
Honestly, I'm okay with anyone.

2354
01:24:43,003 --> 01:24:45,043
- We'll make a good one. - Right.

2355
01:24:45,473 --> 01:24:48,272
Actually, the choreography is important,

2356
01:24:48,273 --> 01:24:50,119
but the positioning of the dancers will be just as important.

2357
01:24:50,143 --> 01:24:52,019
For example, if BADA was already in the front during the chorus...

2358
