01:34:12,913 --> 01:34:14,273
I felt confident in doing so.

2621
01:34:15,173 --> 01:34:16,282
Let's go down first.

2622
01:34:16,283 --> 01:34:17,283
Okay.

2623
01:34:17,284 --> 01:34:19,082
I'll meet BABYZOO for a while.

2624
01:34:19,083 --> 01:34:20,252
Okay. Oh, right!

2625
01:34:20,253 --> 01:34:21,282
- He also gave me a message. - Really?

2626
01:34:21,283 --> 01:34:22,613
- Let's go. - Let's go.

2627
01:34:22,923 --> 01:34:23,923
He sent me a message.

2628
01:34:23,924 --> 01:34:26,223
"Could you help me after you're done?"

2629
01:34:26,753 --> 01:34:28,792
Actually,

2630
01:34:28,793 --> 01:34:30,523
I'm very desperate right now.

2631
01:34:30,793 --> 01:34:32,993
(Koo Young chose BABYZOO to become a Worst Candidate.)

2632
01:34:33,563 --> 01:34:35,392
I was Koo Young's only Worst Candidate.

2633
01:34:35,393 --> 01:34:37,962
I had to earn points from Director Koo Young.

2634
01:34:37,963 --> 01:34:41,073
(The three choreographers I wish to ask for a part...)

2635
01:34:41,303 --> 01:34:44,002
(are BADA, INGYOO, and BABYZOO.)

2636
01:34:44,003 --> 01:34:46,972
And he gave me a chance to come up with the outro.

2637
01:34:46,973 --> 01:34:50,013
I had to put my name up on the choreographer list.

2638
01:34:50,283 --> 01:34:51,343
My strategy is...

2639
01:34:51,543 --> 01:34:54,053
I want to ask you two for a favor.

2640
01:34:54,283 --> 01:34:55,453
Performing with you?

2641
01:34:55,753 --> 01:34:57,722
Right.

2642
01:34:57,723 --> 01:34:59,282
For Director Koo Young,

2643
01:34:59,283 --> 01:35:00,552
it will feel different when it's three...

2644
01:35:00,553 --> 01:35:03,562
instead of me doing the choreography on my own.

2645
01:35:03,563 --> 01:35:05,693
That was why I asked them to help me.

2646
01:35:05,823 --> 01:35:07,169
Could you come a bit early tomorrow?

2647
01:35:07,193 --> 01:35:08,392
- Sure. - Sure.

2648
01:35:08,393 --> 01:35:10,833
I'll treat you two to something really good.

2649
01:35:10,933 --> 01:35:12,832
They gladly agreed to help.

2650
01:35:12,833 --> 01:35:14,353
I have a lot of good people around me.

2651
01:35:14,733 --> 01:35:18,342
I asked them not to tell BADA and INGYOO.

2652
01:35:18,343 --> 01:35:20,143
I'm sure they won't.

2653
01:35:20,513 --> 01:35:21,572
Where are they?

2654
01:35:21,573 --> 01:35:23,043
(Tapping)

2655
01:35:24,443 --> 01:35:25,542
- Gosh! - Gosh!

2656
01:35:25,543 --> 01:35:26,582
- Thank you! - Thank you!

2657
01:35:26,583 --> 01:35:27,612
These are for you.

2658
01:35:27,613 --> 01:35:28,712
Gosh, you're the best!

2659
01:35:28,713 --> 01:35:32,083
- Thank you. - Well, I want to ask for a favor.

2660
01:35:32,183 --> 01:35:34,122
- What is it? - The outro part.

2661
01:35:34,123 --> 01:35:37,192
I wondered if the two of you could join me when I show it.

2662
01:35:37,193 --> 01:35:38,193
(Startled)

2663
01:35:38,194 --> 01:35:39,522
(BADA asked for their help just like BABYZOO.)

2664
01:35:39,523 --> 01:35:40,893
Well, I'm fine with it.

2665
01:35:40,993 --> 01:35:42,793
We can't tell her, right?

2666
01:35:43,103 --> 01:35:44,103
What is it?

2667
01:35:44,633 --> 01:35:46,673
Should we not tell her? I think we should.

2668
01:35:47,033 --> 01:35:48,033
Right?

2669
01:35:48,034 --> 01:35:49,072
(Understanding the situation)

2670
01:35:49,073 --> 01:35:50,703
We would love to help you.

2671
01:35:50,873 --> 01:35:52,743
Are you helping someone else? BABYZOO?

2672
01:35:52,903 --> 01:35:54,412
He asked for our help.

2673
01:35:54,413 --> 01:35:56,459
So that was why the three of you were talking together.

2674
01:35:56,483 --> 01:35:59,883
(BADA saw the three of them talking to each other.)

2675
01:36:00,153 --> 01:36:01,413
We had the same idea.

2676
01:36:01,613 --> 01:36:03,552
What's stuck in my head...

2677
01:36:03,553 --> 01:36:06,352
is the desire to put my name up in the choreographer credit.

2678
01:36:06,353 --> 01:36:09,093
Koo Young never chose me.

2679
01:36:09,893 --> 01:36:11,692
Director Koo Young...

2680
01:36:11,693 --> 01:36:12,993
(What is Father's decision?)

2681
01:36:13,733 --> 01:36:15,732
kept choosing INGYOO.

2682
01:36:15,733 --> 01:36:18,333
He never picked me.

2683
01:36:18,803 --> 01:36:21,872
I want to use BABYZOO's part.

2684
01:36:21,873 --> 01:36:24,342
I have to get permission for Kasper's choreography.

2685
01:36:24,343 --> 01:36:25,502
(Back Koo Young asked the others for their choreography.)

2686
01:36:25,503 --> 01:36:27,272
I was never asked for my choreography.

2687
01:36:27,273 --> 01:36:28,413
I felt so anxious.

2688
01:36:28,613 --> 01:36:31,242
If I don't get chosen for the outro,

2689
01:36:31,243 --> 01:36:33,552
I was filled with the thought of,

2690
01:36:33,553 --> 01:36:36,283
"Will I be the one to be heading to the Last Stage?"

2691
01:36:36,623 --> 01:36:37,623
We really want to help you.

2692
01:36:37,624 --> 01:36:39,152
We can do really well.

2693
01:36:39,153 --> 01:36:40,393
Then don't help BABYZOO.

2694
01:36:40,853 --> 01:36:42,052
- What? - Don't help BABYZOO.

2695
01:36:42,053 --> 01:36:43,222
- Don't help him? - Yes.

2696
01:36:43,223 --> 01:36:44,223
(Startled)

2697
01:36:44,323 --> 01:36:46,062
(Mental breakdown)

2698
01:36:46,063 --> 01:36:49,703
NaiN! What do we do?

2699
01:36:49,803 --> 01:36:51,933
Was she also afraid of ending up on the Last Stage?

2700
01:36:52,933 --> 01:36:54,502
Gosh, well...

2701
01:36:54,503 --> 01:36:55,832
(Simeez struggles to answer.)

2702
01:36:55,833 --> 01:36:56,842
Well...

2703
01:36:56,843 --> 01:36:58,572
No! I was joking.

2704
01:36:58,573 --> 01:37:00,072
No. She wasn't joking.

2705
01:37:00,073 --> 01:37:01,389
I was going to take them away from him,

2706
01:37:01,413 --> 01:37:03,483
(Laughing)

2707
01:37:03,583 --> 01:37:05,583
but that isn't fair.

2708
01:37:05,683 --> 01:37:08,712
If I express my style with the same dancers,

2709
01:37:08,713 --> 01:37:10,323
I believe I have a better chance.

2710
01:37:10,383 --> 01:37:13,692
I'll be performing it with two amazing women.

2711
01:37:13,693 --> 01:37:14,693
I'm full of confidence.

2712
01:37:14,793 --> 01:37:15,852
It wasn't important.

2713
01:37:15,853 --> 01:37:19,933
Instead of having to quickly input my ideas to someone else,

2714
01:37:20,033 --> 01:37:22,092
I thought it would be more appealing...

2715
01:37:22,093 --> 01:37:24,203
if I could express it on my own.

2716
01:37:24,533 --> 01:37:26,533
(D-Day of the outro choreography reveal)

2717
01:37:26,633 --> 01:37:27,933
INGYOO hasn't come.

2718
01:37:28,533 --> 01:37:30,749
(INGYOO's room is empty before the choreography reveal.)

2719
01:37:30,773 --> 01:37:31,843
Is INGYOO sick?

2720
01:37:33,003 --> 01:37:34,872
- He's running late. - Gosh.

2721
01:37:34,873 --> 01:37:36,682
Whether it be a choreographer or dancer,

2722
01:37:36,683 --> 01:37:39,482
there can't be insincerity or tardiness.

2723
01:37:39,483 --> 01:37:41,752
Do we get to take a break?

2724
01:37:41,753 --> 01:37:42,753
Yes.

2725
01:37:44,283 --> 01:37:47,322
(The choreographers fall asleep while waiting for INGYOO.)

2726
01:37:47,323 --> 01:37:50,522
The ones who become a hindrance at the site.

2727
01:37:50,523 --> 01:37:54,333
I cannot stand those people when I'm the director.

2728
01:37:54,433 --> 01:37:56,533
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

2729
01:37:56,703 --> 01:37:58,602
I'm sorry.

2730
01:37:58,603 --> 01:37:59,703
I'm sorry, MIN JUN.

2731
01:38:00,603 --> 01:38:01,603
I'm sorry.

2732
01:38:01,603 --> 01:38:02,603
(Bowing down)

2733
01:38:02,604 --> 01:38:03,702
(The back of his head is full of rage.)

2734
01:38:03,703 --> 01:38:05,773
He seemed to vent his anger.

2735
01:38:06,173 --> 01:38:08,412
- INGYOO! - I'm so sorry.

2736
01:38:08,413 --> 01:38:09,612
Was your phone off?

2737
01:38:09,613 --> 01:38:10,982
Yes.

2738
01:38:10,983 --> 01:38:13,682
I've never seen a jerk like him bow down so low like that.

2739
01:38:13,683 --> 01:38:14,913
Get up.

2740
01:38:15,013 --> 01:38:16,053
I'm so sorry.

2741
01:38:16,283 --> 01:38:18,182
Get warmed up for the reveal, okay?

2742
01:38:18,183 --> 01:38:20,323
- Right. Gosh. - Right.

2743
01:38:20,623 --> 01:38:23,223
Being late? That's a nonstop ticket to the Last Stage.

2744
01:38:23,393 --> 01:38:25,162
INGYOO deserves to go to the Last Stage.

2745
01:38:25,163 --> 01:38:29,292
I was going through an exhausting schedule.

2746
01:38:29,293 --> 01:38:32,262
I forgot to charge my phone and I missed the alarm.

2747
01:38:32,263 --> 01:38:33,633
I felt very sorry.

2748
01:38:35,033 --> 01:38:38,043
Please gather up, directors.

2749
01:38:39,003 --> 01:38:40,343
- Gosh! - Gosh!

2750
01:38:40,973 --> 01:38:44,043
Gosh, it feels intimidating.

2751
01:38:44,343 --> 01:38:47,153
Hello, choreographers. This is Director Back Koo Young.

2752
01:38:47,513 --> 01:38:49,082
(Welcoming the director)

2753
01:38:49,083 --> 01:38:50,153
Hello.

2754
01:38:50,253 --> 01:38:51,522
(Feeling nervous)

2755
01:38:51,523 --> 01:38:54,322
Out of the nine choreographers in front of me,

2756
01:38:54,323 --> 01:38:57,963
I asked three choreographers to come up with the outro.

2757
01:38:58,063 --> 01:39:01,732
We will check the outro parts now!

2758
01:39:01,733 --> 01:39:03,832
(The time has come.)

2759
01:39:03,833 --> 01:39:05,132
Let's go!

2760
01:39:05,133 --> 01:39:07,233
(Screaming)

2761
01:39:07,903 --> 01:39:10,302
I didn't become the director. I can't be Dancer One.

2762
01:39:10,303 --> 01:39:12,242
To avoid the Last Stage,

2763
01:39:12,243 --> 01:39:14,842
I had to get the title as choreographer no matter what.

2764
01:39:14,843 --> 01:39:16,149
I feel really desperate right now.

2765
01:39:16,173 --> 01:39:20,382
Putting my name up on the choreographer credit...

2766
01:39:20,383 --> 01:39:23,222
is my current goal.

2767
01:39:23,223 --> 01:39:25,482
- Let's start with BABYZOO. - Right.

2768
01:39:25,483 --> 01:39:28,523
Could you give us an explanation of your choreography?

2769
01:39:28,623 --> 01:39:31,623
First of all, I thought that you had to stand out.

2770
01:39:31,723 --> 01:39:34,032
To express Director Koo Young's...

2771
01:39:34,033 --> 01:39:36,262
good musicality,

2772
01:39:36,263 --> 01:39:39,662
I added some acting parts.

2773
01:39:39,663 --> 01:39:43,543
I don't really like acting parts in the outro.

2774
01:39:43,773 --> 01:39:45,733
It doesn't seem like a good match with the outro.

2775
01:39:45,973 --> 01:39:50,382
I asked NaiN and Simeez for their help.

2776
01:39:50,383 --> 01:39:55,513
I thought they could help me express my part even more.

2777
01:39:55,613 --> 01:39:58,053
I'm confident that it will be impactful.

2778
01:39:58,153 --> 01:40:00,522
Being expressive is my strength.

2779
01:40:00,523 --> 01:40:02,023
Don't miss it, bro!

2780
01:40:02,293 --> 01:40:04,023
Don't miss it, Koo Young.

2781
01:40:04,563 --> 01:40:08,393
(How will BABYZOO's outro part look?)

2782
01:40:10,203 --> 01:40:12,062
There were many interesting parts.

2783
01:40:12,063 --> 01:40:13,063
Hey!

2784
01:40:13,064 --> 01:40:15,402
I liked the engagement that could be felt from his face.

2785
01:40:15,403 --> 01:40:16,433
Hey!

2786
01:40:17,703 --> 01:40:20,613
The moves felt quite small.

2787
01:40:23,173 --> 01:40:25,982
(So clean)

2788
01:40:25,983 --> 01:40:27,553
(Impressed)

2789
01:40:28,753 --> 01:40:29,753
That was impressive.

2790
01:40:30,483 --> 01:40:33,322
I was startled by the great part he came up with.

2791
01:40:33,323 --> 01:40:34,852
The musicality was great.

2792
01:40:34,853 --> 01:40:37,523
He expressed different textures.

2793
01:40:37,623 --> 01:40:39,863
That made the music sound clearer.

2794
01:40:39,963 --> 01:40:43,332
Just like BABYZOO mentioned,

2795
01:40:43,333 --> 01:40:47,003
it was a part that emphasized the musicality.

2796
01:40:47,233 --> 01:40:50,743
But when considering this as the ending,

2797
01:40:51,073 --> 01:40:56,613
the moves felt rather small.

2798
01:40:56,983 --> 01:41:01,082
When this is seen in a bigger picture,

2799
01:41:01,083 --> 01:41:03,482
I have a bit of a concern...

2800
01:41:03,483 --> 01:41:05,429
if this part will be captured by the camera well.

2801
01:41:05,453 --> 01:41:09,422
He basically meant I took the wrong direction.

2802
01:41:09,423 --> 01:41:10,962
I had to think of the big picture,

2803
01:41:10,963 --> 01:41:13,163
but I went the other way.

2804
01:41:13,263 --> 01:41:17,162
But if this is a mission to make the director stand out,

2805
01:41:17,163 --> 01:41:21,032
I still think it's right for the director to do...

2806
01:41:21,033 --> 01:41:22,732
something they are good at.

2807
01:41:22,733 --> 01:41:24,702
I have a similar opinion with what Koo Young mentioned.

2808
01:41:24,703 --> 01:41:26,842
It felt like a part that would look better...

2809
01:41:26,843 --> 01:41:29,373
for a smaller group than a larger group.

2810
01:41:29,943 --> 01:41:33,083
It didn't feel satisfying to be the ending.

2811
01:41:33,453 --> 01:41:35,413
We will check INGYOO's part.

2812
01:41:35,513 --> 01:41:36,513
(Second outro part reveal, INGYOO)

2813
01:41:36,514 --> 01:41:37,683
Let's go, INGYOO!

2814
01:41:37,783 --> 01:41:39,753
- Let's go! - Please get ready.

2815
01:41:40,293 --> 01:41:42,623
Yo!

2816
01:41:43,153 --> 01:41:44,923
I was excited to see INGYOO's part.

2817
01:41:45,023 --> 01:41:46,693
He always came up with great parts.

2818
01:41:46,893 --> 01:41:49,163
Actually, I was quite concerned about INGYOO.

2819
01:41:49,433 --> 01:41:51,833
(During the signature choreography match)

2820
01:41:53,473 --> 01:41:55,702
(Koo Young liked INGYOO's choreography.)

2821
01:41:55,703 --> 01:41:57,072
(I love it.)

2822
01:41:57,073 --> 01:41:58,672
Whatever INGYOO came up with,

2823
01:41:58,673 --> 01:42:00,613
I expected Koo Young to like it.

2824
01:42:00,713 --> 01:42:01,872
My part is delicious.

2825
01:42:01,873 --> 01:42:04,183
I can already see myself filming for it on my own.

2826
01:42:04,283 --> 01:42:07,083
Please give us an explanation of your part.

2827
01:42:07,813 --> 01:42:11,323
My choreography was based on what Koo Young mentioned earlier...

2828
01:42:11,423 --> 01:42:12,752
about the scale of a large group.

2829
01:42:12,753 --> 01:42:14,892
I created this part with the thought of a wide angle.

2830
01:42:14,893 --> 01:42:19,022
I'm a creator who fulfills everyone's needs.

2831
01:42:19,023 --> 01:42:22,533
I went for Koo Young's needs this time by...

2832
01:42:22,633 --> 01:42:25,002
He seems to like my choreography style.

2833
01:42:25,003 --> 01:42:27,603
I added everything tasty to fit him perfectly.

2834
01:42:27,773 --> 01:42:28,972
I will start!

2835
01:42:28,973 --> 01:42:31,272
- Let's go! - Let's go!

2836
01:42:31,273 --> 01:42:33,742
I personally like his choreography and composition.

2837
01:42:33,743 --> 01:42:35,673
I was excited and curious.

2838
01:42:35,773 --> 01:42:36,883
Yes, sir!

2839
01:42:37,943 --> 01:42:39,443
Wouldn't my part get chosen?

2840
01:42:43,883 --> 01:42:46,423
The impactful parts made it more interesting.

2841
01:42:47,853 --> 01:42:50,863
He expressed catchy parts from the simple rhythm.

2842
01:42:50,993 --> 01:42:54,193
He knew when to stretch out and get tight.

2843
01:42:55,433 --> 01:42:56,462
(Right here)

2844
01:42:56,463 --> 01:42:57,463
Cut transition!

2845
01:42:58,133 --> 01:42:59,633
Oh, the cut transition?

2846
01:43:00,273 --> 01:43:01,273
(Give me)

2847
01:43:01,273 --> 01:43:02,273
Thank you.

2848
01:43:02,274 --> 01:43:05,143
I preferred INGYOO's part.

2849
01:43:05,203 --> 01:43:07,742
I wanted to dance those free moves.

2850
01:43:07,743 --> 01:43:08,743
It looked like a fun part to do.

2851
01:43:08,744 --> 01:43:10,482
I thought it was a party.

2852
01:43:10,483 --> 01:43:12,142
I thought it was a party at first,

2853
01:43:12,143 --> 01:43:15,582
but the moves became powerful toward the end.

2854
01:43:15,583 --> 01:43:17,252
That was when it got my attention.

2855
01:43:17,253 --> 01:43:20,623
Director Koo Young might go with this one.

2856
01:43:20,653 --> 01:43:23,593
As INGYOO mentioned,

2857
01:43:23,693 --> 01:43:26,092
he has considered the bigger picture.

2858
01:43:26,093 --> 01:43:29,663
The musicality was kept within that frame as well.

2859
01:43:29,763 --> 01:43:31,733
I was impressed by that.

2860
01:43:31,863 --> 01:43:34,473
It was the ending,

2861
01:43:34,573 --> 01:43:39,173
but it felt slightly mild.

2862
01:43:40,243 --> 01:43:41,243
I...

2863
01:43:41,244 --> 01:43:43,072
(What is he about to say?)

2864
01:43:43,073 --> 01:43:46,853
can come up with a part every 30 minutes!

2865
01:43:46,953 --> 01:43:47,953
(Laughing)

2866
01:43:47,953 --> 01:43:48,953
(He promotes himself all of a sudden.)

2867
01:43:48,954 --> 01:43:50,983
- Nice. - This took you 30 minutes?

2868
01:43:51,083 --> 01:43:52,823
I think it took around that much.

2869
01:43:53,383 --> 01:43:55,793
I wasn't trying to be boastful. I promoted myself.

2870
01:43:55,893 --> 01:43:59,123
I thought that INGYOO came up with a great part,

2871
01:43:59,223 --> 01:44:02,292
but it didn't seem to go with the flow.

2872
01:44:02,293 --> 01:44:06,062
I wasn't sure what he wanted to express.

2873
01:44:06,063 --> 01:44:08,703
INGYOO's part was abstract.

2874
01:44:08,803 --> 01:44:12,073
It didn't feel like an outro.

2875
01:44:12,203 --> 01:44:13,912
I did pretty well.

2876
01:44:13,913 --> 01:44:14,913
(Satisfied)

2877
01:44:14,914 --> 01:44:18,343
Lastly, we will check BADA's part.

2878
01:44:18,683 --> 01:44:20,852
(Last outro part reveal, BADA)

2879
01:44:20,853 --> 01:44:21,853
Let's go!

2880
01:44:21,983 --> 01:44:24,552
I asked Simeez and NaiN for help.

2881
01:44:24,553 --> 01:44:26,382
Instead of doing it on my own,

2882
01:44:26,383 --> 01:44:28,822
I wanted to show him that it was a part...

2883
01:44:28,823 --> 01:44:29,952
that looked better when performed as a group.

2884
01:44:29,953 --> 01:44:32,423
They're even dressed the same. That's crazy.

2885
01:44:32,823 --> 01:44:34,562
In order to look in sync,

2886
01:44:34,563 --> 01:44:36,792
I thought that we had to dress similarly.

2887
01:44:36,793 --> 01:44:38,333
I can't believe it.

2888
01:44:38,603 --> 01:44:40,533
Please give an explanation of your part.

2889
01:44:40,633 --> 01:44:41,802
I was focused on two things.

2890
01:44:41,803 --> 01:44:43,802
How it looked together and how it looked for you.

2891
01:44:43,803 --> 01:44:45,549
I thought about what would be more impactful...

2892
01:44:45,573 --> 01:44:47,412
and make you stand out more.

2893
01:44:47,413 --> 01:44:49,472
That was my main focus when coming up with this part.

2894
01:44:49,473 --> 01:44:50,942
Also,

2895
01:44:50,943 --> 01:44:52,582
Then I wanted to add a bit of my own dance flavor to it.

2896
01:44:52,583 --> 01:44:55,883
I tried my best to balance the two elements.

2897
01:44:55,913 --> 01:44:58,222
Her long arms and legs give her dancing a unique vibe...

2898
01:44:58,223 --> 01:45:00,452
that drives up the energy.

2899
01:45:00,453 --> 01:45:03,093
She was one of the dancers I was excited to see.

2900
01:45:03,523 --> 01:45:05,892
I'll do my best to get my name up on the Credit Board...

2901
01:45:05,893 --> 01:45:06,933
as a choreographer.

2902
01:45:10,763 --> 01:45:11,763
(Impressed)

2903
01:45:13,063 --> 01:45:14,802
As soon as I saw the first part, I thought...

2904
01:45:14,803 --> 01:45:16,883
her choreography was well-structured with key moves.

2905
01:45:16,943 --> 01:45:18,673
She owned the rhythm...

2906
01:45:18,743 --> 01:45:21,073
and elevated the energy with her big movements.

2907
01:45:23,883 --> 01:45:25,013
This is crazy.

2908
01:45:31,483 --> 01:45:35,393
(Approving)

2909
01:45:35,593 --> 01:45:37,763
I thought she did a good job with her choreography.

2910
01:45:37,793 --> 01:45:38,993
She nailed the texture.

2911
01:45:39,193 --> 01:45:41,463
And she knows how to make her moves stand out.

2912
01:45:41,533 --> 01:45:43,333
I still remember this move in the beginning.

2913
01:45:43,393 --> 01:45:45,732
This move for "give me" is also memorable.

2914
01:45:45,733 --> 01:45:48,003
Her choreography had many memorable parts.

2915
01:45:48,173 --> 01:45:51,642
You kept the rhythm really simple for the ending.

2916
01:45:51,643 --> 01:45:52,943
I thought...

2917
01:45:53,003 --> 01:45:55,372
that decision gave us a much more direct connection...

2918
01:45:55,373 --> 01:45:56,773
to music, so it was a plus for me.

2919
01:45:57,013 --> 01:46:00,852
I liked your overall choreography including the key moves.

2920
01:46:00,853 --> 01:46:04,953
You put together an unforgettable choreography.

2921
01:46:05,053 --> 01:46:06,753
So I really liked that.

2922
01:46:07,053 --> 01:46:09,452
But simplifying the rhythm for your routine...

2923
01:46:09,453 --> 01:46:10,862
might have cost you...

2924
01:46:10,863 --> 01:46:14,733
some of the detailed textures in your moves.

2925
01:46:15,033 --> 01:46:16,839
It was disappointing, but there was nothing I could do.

2926
01:46:16,863 --> 01:46:18,262
I was looking forward to her choreography.

2927
01:46:18,263 --> 01:46:20,672
The musicality was too simple, perhaps.

2928
01:46:20,673 --> 01:46:21,702
It's disappointing.

2929
01:46:21,703 --> 01:46:23,232
(Back Koo Young is reviewing the choreography...)

2930
01:46:23,233 --> 01:46:24,742
(before the final decision.)

2931
01:46:24,743 --> 01:46:26,803
They're such good dancers.

2932
01:46:26,903 --> 01:46:29,443
Hee Jung and NaiN should get an award.

2933
01:46:30,283 --> 01:46:31,942
(Thinking)

2934
01:46:31,943 --> 01:46:33,753
BABYZOO's choreography was great too.

2935
01:46:34,583 --> 01:46:36,453
This is so fascinating.

2936
01:46:36,513 --> 01:46:38,152
I'm writing down the evaluations for these three.

2937
01:46:38,153 --> 01:46:39,723
They're all connected.

2938
01:46:39,783 --> 01:46:43,493
They feed into each other, forming a complete cycle.

2939
01:46:44,223 --> 01:46:46,493
I like her choreography. It's nice and powerful.

2940
01:46:46,723 --> 01:46:48,832
But it's lacking texture in her movements.

2941
01:46:48,833 --> 01:46:51,563
BABYZOO's movement texture is great.

2942
01:46:51,703 --> 01:46:53,409
But it falls a bit short when looking at the overall scale.

2943
01:46:53,433 --> 01:46:55,733
INGYOO's choreography delivers a good sense of scale.

2944
01:46:56,033 --> 01:46:57,143
But it's too plain.

2945
01:46:58,103 --> 01:47:01,073
Their strength and weakness are too distinct.

2946
01:47:01,213 --> 01:47:03,173
I'm really torn.

2947
01:47:03,573 --> 01:47:05,442
I think I'm going to win...

2948
01:47:05,443 --> 01:47:07,152
because my choreography is special.

2949
01:47:07,153 --> 01:47:09,112
Please let me win. I'm really looking forward to it.

2950
01:47:09,113 --> 01:47:10,382
I'll probably...

2951
01:47:10,383 --> 01:47:12,552
go to Last Stage without this win. I'm serious.

2952
01:47:12,553 --> 01:47:13,992
I'm worried.

2953
01:47:13,993 --> 01:47:16,222
I don't know which way Koo Young is going to lean...

2954
01:47:16,223 --> 01:47:17,562
when he makes his decision.

2955
01:47:17,563 --> 01:47:19,662
I just put together a bombing choreography for him,

2956
01:47:19,663 --> 01:47:21,292
so he could pick me.

2957
01:47:21,293 --> 01:47:22,992
I might have a chance to win.

2958
01:47:22,993 --> 01:47:25,732
If I'm the first one to get eliminated from Last Stage,

2959
01:47:25,733 --> 01:47:27,132
then this place...

2960
01:47:27,133 --> 01:47:28,402
will turn gray.

2961
01:47:28,403 --> 01:47:30,072
Everything will look bleak.

2962
01:47:30,073 --> 01:47:32,802
I worked really hard to get picked by him.

2963
01:47:32,803 --> 01:47:34,963
I want to put my name as a choreographer on the board.

2964
01:47:35,013 --> 01:47:37,543
(Which one of them will get to put their name on the board?)

2965
01:47:38,113 --> 01:47:39,142
Guys.

2966
01:47:39,143 --> 01:47:41,412
- Let's practice and get this done. - Okay.

2967
01:47:41,413 --> 01:47:44,622
So what else do we need to work on?

2968
01:47:44,623 --> 01:47:46,382
- This will be our formation. - Okay.

2969
01:47:46,383 --> 01:47:48,422
- Five and five here. - Okay.

2970
01:47:48,423 --> 01:47:51,093
Mark your spots.

2971
01:47:51,223 --> 01:47:53,522
Everyone is great and working hard.

2972
01:47:53,523 --> 01:47:56,132
They learned the choreography beforehand.

2973
01:47:56,133 --> 01:47:58,409
I was really happy that our practice session went smoothly.

2974
01:47:58,433 --> 01:48:00,549
I'll do my best to be a good leader at the shoot too.

2975
01:48:00,573 --> 01:48:03,302
(The day of the shoot for the Title Sequence Film Mission)

2976
01:48:03,303 --> 01:48:05,542
(Everyone is getting ready for the shoot.)

2977
01:48:05,543 --> 01:48:09,173
(What's about to unfold on set today with the scale dialed up?)

2978
01:48:11,643 --> 01:48:13,013
- Gosh. - This is the set.

2979
01:48:13,043 --> 01:48:14,213
This is huge.

2980
01:48:14,283 --> 01:48:15,352
(Impressed)

2981
01:48:15,353 --> 01:48:16,353
They did a great job with the lighting setup.

2982
01:48:16,354 --> 01:48:17,422
It's beautiful.

2983
01:48:17,423 --> 01:48:18,822
It's definitely going to look massive on camera.

2984
01:48:18,823 --> 01:48:20,283
It delivered a huge sense of scale.

2985
01:48:20,493 --> 01:48:22,492
The truck had a strong presence on set.

2986
01:48:22,493 --> 01:48:23,922
I thought it was going to look so cool.

2987
01:48:23,923 --> 01:48:24,923
But the thing is,

2988
01:48:24,924 --> 01:48:25,992
we never know.

2989
01:48:25,993 --> 01:48:27,932
The video we film today...

2990
01:48:27,933 --> 01:48:29,992
might send me to Last Stage.

2991
01:48:29,993 --> 01:48:31,332
I cannot make a mistake.

2992
01:48:31,333 --> 01:48:32,662
I have to nail the choreography.

2993
01:48:32,663 --> 01:48:34,572
I'm a bit worried whether I can faithfully follow...

2994
01:48:34,573 --> 01:48:35,932
the directions from Koo Young...

2995
01:48:35,933 --> 01:48:37,302
without getting negative feedback...

2996
01:48:37,303 --> 01:48:39,903
and still pull off a good performance.

2997
01:48:40,203 --> 01:48:41,542
Which way is it? This?

2998
01:48:41,543 --> 01:48:42,572
It's this way.

2999
01:48:42,573 --> 01:48:43,642
(Simeez asks BABYZOO which way to turn her head.)

3000
01:48:43,643 --> 01:48:45,282
(Trembling, frozen)

3001
01:48:45,283 --> 01:48:47,113
(What did you say, Simeez?)

3002
01:48:47,183 --> 01:48:48,582
How could you ask a question...

3003
01:48:48,583 --> 01:48:50,359
about the choreography on the day of the shoot?

3004
01:48:50,383 --> 01:48:52,259
How is that possible? What do you think about that?

3005
01:48:52,283 --> 01:48:54,052
I was terrified.

3006
01:48:54,053 --> 01:48:55,933
It felt like a nightmare was creeping up on me.

3007
01:48:55,993 --> 01:48:56,993
I'm in trouble.

3008
01:48:57,023 --> 01:49:00,432
My name isn't on the board as a choreographer.

3009
01:49:00,433 --> 01:49:02,563
So I need to work really hard today.

3010
01:49:02,663 --> 01:49:04,932
When we're filming today,

3011
01:49:04,933 --> 01:49:07,273
I need to observe closely who I want to send...

3012
01:49:07,373 --> 01:49:08,803
to Last Stage.

3013
01:49:08,933 --> 01:49:10,803
Let's film the outro.

3014
01:49:10,903 --> 01:49:13,372
(The sun has gone down, and they start filming the outro.)

3015
01:49:13,373 --> 01:49:15,272
I asked the following choreographers...

3016
01:49:15,273 --> 01:49:16,449
to come up with the outro choreography.

3017
01:49:16,473 --> 01:49:17,542
BADA.

3018
01:49:17,543 --> 01:49:20,952
(Choreography by BADA)

3019
01:49:20,953 --> 01:49:21,953
BABYZOO.

3020
01:49:21,954 --> 01:49:24,652
(Choreography by BABYZOO)

3021
01:49:24,653 --> 01:49:26,682
INGYOO.

3022
01:49:26,683 --> 01:49:28,293
(Choreography by INGYOO)

3023
01:49:28,453 --> 01:49:30,793
The choreography I selected is...

3024
01:49:30,893 --> 01:49:33,253
(Whose choreography was chosen among the 3 choreographers?)

3025
01:49:33,323 --> 01:49:36,193
I chose BADA's choreography.

3026
01:49:36,433 --> 01:49:38,702
It's the choreography I can execute well.

3027
01:49:38,703 --> 01:49:40,773
And it was a better fit for the ending.

3028
01:49:40,973 --> 01:49:43,902
Choreography contribution is a key part of my evaluation.

3029
01:49:43,903 --> 01:49:44,903
- Her choreography was chosen. - One,

3030
01:49:44,904 --> 01:49:46,349
- two, one. - So she'll get points for that.

3031
01:49:46,373 --> 01:49:48,772
Then the odds of her going to Last Stage might go down.

3032
01:49:48,773 --> 01:49:50,073
You know?

3033
01:49:50,273 --> 01:49:52,582
(Outro Choreographer, BADA)

3034
01:49:52,583 --> 01:49:54,552
I won!

3035
01:49:54,553 --> 01:49:56,312
It's a high-stakes mission...

3036
01:49:56,313 --> 01:49:57,652
because elimination is on the line.

3037
01:49:57,653 --> 01:50:00,053
I was so happy that I got my name on the Credit Board...

3038
01:50:00,723 --> 01:50:02,223
as a choreographer.

3039
01:50:03,123 --> 01:50:04,162
I was bummed out.

3040
01:50:04,163 --> 01:50:07,293
I was a bit disappointed that mine didn't get chosen.

3041
01:50:07,333 --> 01:50:08,832
She did a great job with her choreography,

3042
01:50:08,833 --> 01:50:09,993
so I understood his decision.

3043
01:50:10,903 --> 01:50:13,602
I really want to add this move from your routine.

3044
01:50:13,603 --> 01:50:14,632
Really? Okay.

3045
01:50:14,633 --> 01:50:16,549
(BABYZOO's routine included a collar-biting move.)

3046
01:50:16,573 --> 01:50:19,672
I added a key dance move from BABYZOO's choreography...

3047
01:50:19,673 --> 01:50:20,772
- to the chorus. - Thank you.

3048
01:50:20,773 --> 01:50:22,072
I was grateful.

3049
01:50:22,073 --> 01:50:23,342
He's using one of my moves.

3050
01:50:23,343 --> 01:50:24,719
Does it mean I'll get credited for it?

3051
01:50:24,743 --> 01:50:25,903
Will my name be on the board?

3052
01:50:25,943 --> 01:50:26,983
No way.

3053
01:50:27,083 --> 01:50:30,652
(While getting ready to film BABYZOO's chorus choreography...)

3054
01:50:30,653 --> 01:50:32,252
Hee Jung can't do this.

3055
01:50:32,253 --> 01:50:34,052
Simeez and Hash can't do it.

3056
01:50:34,053 --> 01:50:35,192
The same goes for Renan.

3057
01:50:35,193 --> 01:50:36,292
What do you mean?

3058
01:50:36,293 --> 01:50:37,493
This move.

3059
01:50:38,093 --> 01:50:39,162
(Koo Young selected the collar-biting move...)

3060
01:50:39,163 --> 01:50:40,222
(from BABYZOO's choreography.)

3061
01:50:40,223 --> 01:50:42,333
(The chorus with BABYZOO's choreography)

3062
01:50:43,293 --> 01:50:46,302
I didn't think this through and failed to see that...

3063
01:50:46,303 --> 01:50:47,802
it wouldn't work with their outfits.

3064
01:50:47,803 --> 01:50:50,472
He checked the outfits on the day of the shoot.

3065
01:50:50,473 --> 01:50:52,672
"What do we do if they're not wearing a jacket?"

3066
01:50:52,673 --> 01:50:54,189
BADA, you're in the center for this, right?

3067
01:50:54,213 --> 01:50:56,472
I thought I could make it work if BADA who was in the center..

3068
01:50:56,473 --> 01:50:57,782
Could execute...

3069
01:50:57,783 --> 01:50:59,042
the collar-biting move.

3070
01:50:59,043 --> 01:51:00,382
When I got to the shoot,

3071
01:51:00,383 --> 01:51:03,782
I saw sharp metal zings on her collar.

3072
01:51:03,783 --> 01:51:05,023
It won't be safe.

3073
01:51:05,083 --> 01:51:07,792
The metal zings on the collar would scratch me.

3074
01:51:07,793 --> 01:51:09,053
- They're really sharp. - Yes.

3075
01:51:09,123 --> 01:51:11,393
I didn't want to risk her safety for it.

3076
01:51:11,563 --> 01:51:14,792
Or how about holding the collar out? Just to show the vibe.

3077
01:51:14,793 --> 01:51:16,132
I showed him another option.

3078
01:51:16,133 --> 01:51:17,832
If even one of my moves got chosen for this,

3079
01:51:17,833 --> 01:51:19,302
my name would go on the Credit Board.

3080
01:51:19,303 --> 01:51:21,233
That's what was at stake for me.

3081
01:51:21,933 --> 01:51:23,402
No. I don't want to use this...

3082
01:51:23,403 --> 01:51:25,343
- unless we can bite the collar. - Wait.

3083
01:51:25,473 --> 01:51:27,842
The director wanted us to bite the collar no matter what.

3084
01:51:27,843 --> 01:51:29,272
Without that, this won't work.

3085
01:51:29,273 --> 01:51:30,443
The biting part is the key.

3086
01:51:30,543 --> 01:51:34,112
He knew that our outfit would come into play.

3087
01:51:34,113 --> 01:51:38,523
The fact that he checked the outfits on the day of the shoot...

3088
01:51:39,353 --> 01:51:40,553
didn't make sense.

3089
01:51:41,153 --> 01:51:42,293
Let's go with this instead.

3090
01:51:42,393 --> 01:51:43,452
- Okay. - Okay.

3091
01:51:43,453 --> 01:51:45,022
My hands were tied. There wasn't time...

3092
01:51:45,023 --> 01:51:46,362
for me to keep pushing for it.

3093
01:51:46,363 --> 01:51:49,632
"Does it mean my name won't be on the Credit Board?"

3094
01:51:49,633 --> 01:51:51,462
I couldn't be self-serving at the shoot.

3095
01:51:51,463 --> 01:51:52,702
Considering my position,

3096
01:51:52,703 --> 01:51:55,373
it was just disappointing.

3097
01:51:55,403 --> 01:51:56,672
Of course, this is disappointing.

3098
01:51:56,673 --> 01:51:58,202
If I were in his shoes,

3099
01:51:58,203 --> 01:51:59,442
I would've been so disappointed.

3100
01:51:59,443 --> 01:52:01,572
Having your name on the board...

3101
01:52:01,573 --> 01:52:03,172
will be a major difference.

3102
01:52:03,173 --> 01:52:04,742
But we had to keep filming.

3103
01:52:04,743 --> 01:52:05,882
We didn't have much time either.

3104
01:52:05,883 --> 01:52:07,043
I just decided to do my best.

3105
01:52:07,183 --> 01:52:08,813
That was my focus then.

3106
01:52:09,613 --> 01:52:12,022
First group, could you wait over there?

3107
01:52:12,023 --> 01:52:13,082
- Okay. - Okay.

3108
01:52:13,083 --> 01:52:15,252
(The first scene starts with BADA and shows BABYZOO getting up.)

3109
01:52:15,253 --> 01:52:17,662
(The first scene starts with BADA and shows BABYZOO getting up.)

3110
01:52:17,663 --> 01:52:19,292
(But Kasper is in BABYZOO's spot.)

3111
01:52:19,293 --> 01:52:20,992
(And BABYZOO is monitoring the scene.)

3112
01:52:20,993 --> 01:52:22,862
(Their places have switched. What happened to them?)

3113
01:52:22,863 --> 01:52:25,162
BABYZOO's part is my favorite.

3114
01:52:25,163 --> 01:52:27,132
I took BABYZOO's part which I liked...

3115
01:52:27,133 --> 01:52:29,073
from NaiN's choreography.

3116
01:52:29,333 --> 01:52:30,602
- It's really cool. - Okay.

3117
01:52:30,603 --> 01:52:32,472
I love that part. So...

3118
01:52:32,473 --> 01:52:34,973
Kasper will take BABYZOO's part where he was supposed to...

3119
01:52:35,113 --> 01:52:36,843
- get up from the floor. - Okay.

3120
01:52:37,443 --> 01:52:39,012
I was relieved...

3121
01:52:39,013 --> 01:52:40,043
because...

3122
01:52:41,183 --> 01:52:42,352
To be honestly,

3123
01:52:42,353 --> 01:52:43,713
that was a difficult one for me.

3124
01:52:43,783 --> 01:52:47,182
Five, six, seven, eight.

3125
01:52:47,183 --> 01:52:48,522
I'm sorry. Let me try again.

3126
01:52:48,523 --> 01:52:50,553
I'm sorry. I'll do it better.

3127
01:52:50,793 --> 01:52:52,963
This morning, we had to pull him by the bottom...

3128
01:52:52,993 --> 01:52:55,392
Koo Young picked me as the worst. Maybe, he felt bad.

3129
01:52:55,393 --> 01:52:56,762
I really don't know.

3130
01:52:56,763 --> 01:52:58,632
Anyway, I'm really grateful.

3131
01:52:58,633 --> 01:53:01,873
He gave me a part I could execute so much better.

3132
01:53:02,803 --> 01:53:04,202
I'm so grateful.

3133
01:53:04,203 --> 01:53:05,742
I think he helped me, so I could redeem myself.

3134
01:53:05,743 --> 01:53:07,302
I really think so.

3135
01:53:07,303 --> 01:53:09,172
Five, six, seven, eight.

3136
01:53:09,173 --> 01:53:10,472
(Kasper gets up on his first try.)

3137
01:53:10,473 --> 01:53:14,083
(Embarrassed)

3138
01:53:14,153 --> 01:53:15,283
I did well, didn't I?

3139
01:53:15,513 --> 01:53:17,583
But will this really help his case?

3140
01:53:17,623 --> 01:53:20,792
(Sounding cryptic)

3141
01:53:20,793 --> 01:53:22,952
(Messing it up)

3142
01:53:22,953 --> 01:53:25,122
(They continue filming.)

3143
01:53:25,123 --> 01:53:26,562
(Koo Young seems unhappy.)

3144
01:53:26,563 --> 01:53:28,563
I think Renan is off the beat.

3145
01:53:29,433 --> 01:53:31,513
He's actually saying that out loud as he walks over?

3146
01:53:31,603 --> 01:53:33,363
My gosh. If I were in her shoes...

3147
01:53:33,403 --> 01:53:34,603
I was scared.

3148
01:53:34,803 --> 01:53:35,932
Renan.

3149
01:53:35,933 --> 01:53:38,203
You're off the beat.

3150
01:53:38,303 --> 01:53:39,472
This part?

3151
01:53:39,473 --> 01:53:41,542
- This has to go fast too. - Okay.

3152
01:53:41,543 --> 01:53:43,572
- Your tempo is off. - Okay.

3153
01:53:43,573 --> 01:53:44,642
(She has to stop on the beat.)

3154
01:53:44,643 --> 01:53:47,982
Having a director tell you that you're off the beat...

3155
01:53:47,983 --> 01:53:50,252
is a huge problem.

3156
01:53:50,253 --> 01:53:52,783
Renan took a long time to finish her scene.

3157
01:53:52,983 --> 01:53:57,052
(He watches Renan film with a serious look on his face.)

3158
01:53:57,053 --> 01:54:01,432
(They film the same scene again.)

3159
01:54:01,433 --> 01:54:02,932
Renan. The thing is,

3160
01:54:02,933 --> 01:54:04,803
your movements aren't on the beat.

3161
01:54:05,033 --> 01:54:06,132
This is what you're doing.

3162
01:54:06,133 --> 01:54:07,162
(He's giving her the same direction again.)

3163
01:54:07,163 --> 01:54:08,603
That's what you're doing. Watch.

3164
01:54:09,033 --> 01:54:12,672
Renan couldn't dance on the beat.

3165
01:54:12,673 --> 01:54:14,872
I went over to her several times to give her directions.

3166
01:54:14,873 --> 01:54:17,112
I'm disappointed too.

3167
01:54:17,113 --> 01:54:19,642
I'm always disappointed when I perform as a dancer.

3168
01:54:19,643 --> 01:54:21,582
- I gave every possible direction. - Just balance it.

3169
01:54:21,583 --> 01:54:22,912
I gave directions to everyone.

3170
01:54:22,913 --> 01:54:26,182
Some dancers executed my directions on their first try.

3171
01:54:26,183 --> 01:54:29,222
Or some pulled them off on their 2nd or 3rd tries.

3172
01:54:29,223 --> 01:54:31,563
So that was the difference.

3173
01:54:31,763 --> 01:54:33,062
As for his evaluation criteria,

3174
01:54:33,063 --> 01:54:35,933
I think he focuses on the level of execution at the shoot.

3175
01:54:35,963 --> 01:54:37,392
So I felt bad for her.

3176
01:54:37,393 --> 01:54:38,762
Gosh, I'm doomed.

3177
01:54:38,763 --> 01:54:41,032
My choreography or any of my moves got chosen.

3178
01:54:41,033 --> 01:54:42,932
And he gave me negative feedback at the shoot.

3179
01:54:42,933 --> 01:54:45,702
The only shot I have left is the Director's Cut.

3180
01:54:45,703 --> 01:54:49,213
I need to get chosen for the Director's Cut.

3181
01:54:49,573 --> 01:54:50,573
If I at least have that,

3182
01:54:50,574 --> 01:54:52,943
I would feel a little safe about my position here.

3183
01:54:53,443 --> 01:54:55,583
We'll start filming for the Director's Cut.

3184
01:54:55,713 --> 01:54:58,073
This is driving me crazy. I have to win the Director's Cut.

3185
01:54:58,183 --> 01:55:00,423
Without this, I might end up going to Last Stage.

3186
01:55:00,483 --> 01:55:01,492
Please!

3187
01:55:01,493 --> 01:55:04,792
I'll go to Last Stage without this win for sure.

3188
01:55:04,793 --> 01:55:06,192
I'm pretty sure it will be me.

3189
01:55:06,193 --> 01:55:07,932
I have to win it no matter what.

3190
01:55:07,933 --> 01:55:09,162
We must secure it...

3191
01:55:09,163 --> 01:55:10,532
because it gives us the benefit...

3192
01:55:10,533 --> 01:55:11,939
that the director is happy with our performance.

3193
01:55:11,963 --> 01:55:14,573
So that might lower our chance of going to Last Stage.

3194
01:55:14,803 --> 01:55:17,033
Kasper, Renan, and Hash. You will go first.

3195
01:55:17,133 --> 01:55:19,602
It's a mystery what they'll do for the Director's Cut.

3196
01:55:19,603 --> 01:55:21,573
I have no idea what they're going to do.

3197
01:55:22,073 --> 01:55:23,473
I'm going to lie down here.

3198
01:55:24,143 --> 01:55:25,942
(Kasper lies down on the trunk.)

3199
01:55:25,943 --> 01:55:27,183
And then...

3200
01:55:27,513 --> 01:55:28,513
What?

3201
01:55:28,514 --> 01:55:30,183
- What? - The camera...

3202
01:55:30,653 --> 01:55:32,352
(They can't stop laughing.)

3203
01:55:32,353 --> 01:55:34,823
Their use of props was quite unique.

3204
01:55:35,053 --> 01:55:36,692
He put his phone in front of his mouth.

3205
01:55:36,693 --> 01:55:38,173
He replaced his mouth with the phone.

3206
01:55:38,663 --> 01:55:40,422
When I lie down and have the phone in front of me,

3207
01:55:40,423 --> 01:55:43,032
it looks like I'm dead and lifeless, but my mouth is rapping.

3208
01:55:43,033 --> 01:55:44,632
I was looking for a new angle or a new structure.

3209
01:55:44,633 --> 01:55:47,533
I tried to come up with an interesting structure.

3210
01:55:47,633 --> 01:55:49,203
We have to study Koo Young's reaction.

3211
01:55:49,833 --> 01:55:51,503
He's laughing.

3212
01:55:52,043 --> 01:55:54,043
So far, it's funny. Hold on.

3213
01:55:54,413 --> 01:55:57,543
I wonder how they'll incorporate this idea into the performance.

3214
01:55:58,183 --> 01:56:01,352
He loves anything that's unique and out of the box.

3215
01:56:01,353 --> 01:56:03,313
So I respect him for it.

3216
01:56:03,413 --> 01:56:04,822
Go all the way over there.

3217
01:56:04,823 --> 01:56:07,383
- And Renan will grab the camera. - Okay.

3218
01:56:08,093 --> 01:56:09,353
Let's do it one shot at a time.

3219
01:56:09,993 --> 01:56:12,063
We start with a close-up shot of my lips.

3220
01:56:12,323 --> 01:56:15,063
Hash and I are going to perform the choreography.

3221
01:56:15,263 --> 01:56:17,362
It will look like Renan is dancing on the tips of Hash's toes.

3222
01:56:17,363 --> 01:56:19,009
So we'll express the lyrics through our moves.

3223
01:56:19,033 --> 01:56:20,662
- They overthought this. - The rehearsal...

3224
01:56:20,663 --> 01:56:21,872
It's a short part.

3225
01:56:21,873 --> 01:56:23,832
They're trying to express all the lyrics.

3226
01:56:23,833 --> 01:56:24,942
So the moves don't pop.

3227
01:56:24,943 --> 01:56:27,442
They haven't let go of their greed yet.

3228
01:56:27,443 --> 01:56:28,472
Too much stuff is going on.

3229
01:56:28,473 --> 01:56:30,882
We added a lot of transitions, angles, and effects...

3230
01:56:30,883 --> 01:56:33,183
even though our part was pretty short.

3231
01:56:33,383 --> 01:56:34,452
I like following the flow...

3232
01:56:34,453 --> 01:56:36,513
showing the performance in various angles.

3233
01:56:36,713 --> 01:56:37,983
They had a fresh take on it.

3234
01:56:38,083 --> 01:56:40,952
It made me see that Kasper had the ability to come up with...

3235
01:56:40,953 --> 01:56:42,922
original ideas and tackle the mission...

3236
01:56:42,923 --> 01:56:44,192
with a goal-oriented mind.

3237
01:56:44,193 --> 01:56:47,693
But it would've been good if they focused more on the dancing.

3238
01:56:47,733 --> 01:56:49,993
With three girls on the truck,

3239
01:56:50,363 --> 01:56:52,062
they're giving off the queen vibes.

3240
01:56:52,063 --> 01:56:54,203
They went with a feminine approach.

3241
01:56:54,633 --> 01:56:56,172
- Can you show us in real time? - Yes.

3242
01:56:56,173 --> 01:56:57,942
- We need to know how to time this. - Sure.

3243
01:56:57,943 --> 01:56:59,002
(They begin the rehearsal to check the angles.)

3244
01:56:59,003 --> 01:57:01,143
So pull out after that.

3245
01:57:02,173 --> 01:57:05,183
Their performance was predictable.

3246
01:57:05,283 --> 01:57:06,982
I knew NaiN, BADA, and Simeez...

3247
01:57:06,983 --> 01:57:08,459
would accentuate their feminine side.

3248
01:57:08,483 --> 01:57:11,352
But I'm not sure if this sexy concept fits here.

3249
01:57:11,353 --> 01:57:13,852
They have the risk of giving off "Street Woman Fighter" vibes.

3250
01:57:13,853 --> 01:57:16,292
They should show us something creative...

3251
01:57:16,293 --> 01:57:18,662
only directors can pull off.

3252
01:57:18,663 --> 01:57:20,062
But their performance didn't leave an impression.

3253
01:57:20,063 --> 01:57:22,263
We thought about drawing a crown on our neck.

3254
01:57:22,693 --> 01:57:24,732
So we could lift our hair to show the crown.

3255
01:57:24,733 --> 01:57:27,003
And that could be our highlight.

3256
01:57:27,633 --> 01:57:30,332
We have to do more than just dance for this. We have to kill it.

3257
01:57:30,333 --> 01:57:32,543
And the key point would be the crown.

3258
01:57:32,703 --> 01:57:35,273
We wanted to do something only we could do as female dancers.

3259
01:57:35,373 --> 01:57:37,072
We thought...

3260
01:57:37,073 --> 01:57:38,542
if the three of us crushed it with a powerful choreography,

3261
01:57:38,543 --> 01:57:40,183
it would work.

3262
01:57:40,913 --> 01:57:41,913
(Impressed)

3263
01:57:41,914 --> 01:57:42,953
Nice and neat.

3264
01:57:43,053 --> 01:57:45,133
The three of them definitely had their own presence.

3265
01:57:45,353 --> 01:57:47,052
Cut. That was great.

3266
01:57:47,053 --> 01:57:48,392
- Play it. - Let's play it.

3267
01:57:48,393 --> 01:57:49,522
They're clapping.

3268
01:57:49,523 --> 01:57:51,893
- Okay. - Did they like it? Really?

3269
01:57:51,993 --> 01:57:53,913
The response during the shoot is most important.

3270
01:57:54,023 --> 01:57:55,833
We were the only group people clapped for.

3271
01:57:56,133 --> 01:57:57,632
But who knows?

3272
01:57:57,633 --> 01:57:59,953
I don't think their scene left that much of an impression.

3273
01:58:00,133 --> 01:58:02,073
But on the flip side,

3274
01:58:02,103 --> 01:58:04,072
our performance includes action-forward elements.

3275
01:58:04,073 --> 01:58:05,802
We crafted a routine, centering around our teamwork.

3276
01:58:05,803 --> 01:58:08,112
A routine that brought us closer.

3277
01:58:08,113 --> 01:58:10,173
It's something other groups can pull off.

3278
01:58:10,443 --> 01:58:12,343
But it's something we can execute perfectly.

3279
01:58:12,683 --> 01:58:14,242
(BABYZOO, INGYOO, and MIN JUN start filming the Director's Cut.)

3280
01:58:14,243 --> 01:58:16,659
(BABYZOO, INGYOO, and MIN JUN start filming the Director's Cut.)

3281
01:58:16,683 --> 01:58:18,529
They actually included some contemporary vibes.

3282
01:58:18,553 --> 01:58:20,623
They heavily incorporated contemporary elements.

3283
01:58:20,783 --> 01:58:23,052
But considering the progression, would that be a right fit?

3284
01:58:23,053 --> 01:58:24,922
Would that be a wow factor of the choreography?

3285
01:58:24,923 --> 01:58:26,793
That was questionable.

3286
01:58:26,923 --> 01:58:29,563
Rather than going all-out from the start,

3287
01:58:29,693 --> 01:58:32,232
opening with a restrained tone would work much better.

3288
01:58:32,233 --> 01:58:33,563
It's like an intermission.

3289
01:58:34,263 --> 01:58:36,532
We thought physical contact was a great idea.

3290
01:58:36,533 --> 01:58:38,319
So we went with the freestyle vibe with physical contact.

3291
01:58:38,343 --> 01:58:40,702
We kept it simple with our tiptoes. And for the seamless connection,

3292
01:58:40,703 --> 01:58:42,273
we added a transition effect.

3293
01:58:42,373 --> 01:58:45,342
It didn't look like anything they've done before.

3294
01:58:45,343 --> 01:58:47,159
I find it quite interesting which wasn't expected.

3295
01:58:47,183 --> 01:58:48,183
Hey.

3296
01:58:48,184 --> 01:58:50,883
The jumping part was the most memorable for me.

3297
01:58:51,123 --> 01:58:53,352
It was a new idea.

3298
01:58:53,353 --> 01:58:56,023
We tried to make it look like a scene in an action movie.

3299
01:58:56,393 --> 01:58:58,092
When we had to use the truck as our prop,

3300
01:58:58,093 --> 01:58:59,292
I wanted to portray a scene...

3301
01:58:59,293 --> 01:59:01,292
where we jumped off a running truck.

3302
01:59:01,293 --> 01:59:02,293
That's good.

3303
01:59:02,294 --> 01:59:03,762
The jump scene was cool.

3304
01:59:03,763 --> 01:59:05,832
When it came to highlighting the music,

3305
01:59:05,833 --> 01:59:08,003
it was a good approach.

3306
01:59:08,173 --> 01:59:09,572
Looking at other groups' Director's Cuts,

3307
01:59:09,573 --> 01:59:12,142
I think ours is quite special.

3308
01:59:12,143 --> 01:59:13,942
I think my group is going to win.

3309
01:59:13,943 --> 01:59:17,272
For any choreography to shine, there has to be...

3310
01:59:17,273 --> 01:59:19,183
a creative side.

3311
01:59:19,283 --> 01:59:22,312
All three groups had great ideas.

3312
01:59:22,313 --> 01:59:23,913
Their styles are all different.

3313
01:59:24,053 --> 01:59:26,059
I have to consider the overall flow before making my decision.

3314
01:59:26,083 --> 01:59:27,992
- Good work! - Good work!

3315
01:59:27,993 --> 01:59:29,253
Great job.

3316
01:59:29,423 --> 01:59:32,623
I gave my all to every single scene.

3317
01:59:32,763 --> 01:59:34,969
I worked harder for this than I would do for my own project.

3318
01:59:34,993 --> 01:59:36,333
I gave my 100 percent.

3319
01:59:36,533 --> 01:59:38,703
I was practically his assistant.

3320
01:59:38,803 --> 01:59:39,933
I wasn't worried.

3321
01:59:40,033 --> 01:59:42,073
I don't want to go to Last Stage.

3322
01:59:42,173 --> 01:59:44,173
I don't want to go to Last Stage for this mission.

3323
01:59:44,573 --> 01:59:45,673
Who is it going to be?

3324
01:59:46,143 --> 01:59:47,812
Three of us will go to Last Stage. That's a lot.

3325
01:59:47,813 --> 01:59:49,473
A third of us will be up for elimination.

3326
01:59:50,043 --> 01:59:53,042
I wonder who it's going to be.

3327
01:59:53,043 --> 01:59:54,342
(Anxious)

3328
01:59:54,343 --> 01:59:56,882
People whose names aren't on the Credit Board...

3329
01:59:56,883 --> 01:59:59,043
might be facing the possibility of getting eliminated.

3330
02:00:00,323 --> 02:00:02,853
Getting credited only as a dancer makes me nervous.

3331
02:00:03,093 --> 02:00:05,423
It means I have a higher chance of going to Last Stage.

3332
02:00:06,863 --> 02:00:08,333
I'm too nervous to do this.

3333
02:00:08,933 --> 02:00:11,103
I think BADA is totally safe.

3334
02:00:11,403 --> 02:00:15,333
BADA was the only one whose choreography was chosen.

3335
02:00:15,803 --> 02:00:18,603
(BADA's choreography for the outro was chosen.)

3336
02:00:19,173 --> 02:00:20,873
(I got picked!)

3337
02:00:21,343 --> 02:00:22,973
Oh, my gosh!

3338
02:00:24,073 --> 02:00:25,843
And she taught the dancers too.

3339
02:00:26,143 --> 02:00:27,483
Well, that does it for her.

3340
02:00:27,613 --> 02:00:28,652
Gosh, she's safe.

3341
02:00:28,653 --> 02:00:29,983
And she totally nailed this too.

3342
02:00:30,953 --> 02:00:32,283
I'm nervous.

3343
02:00:33,283 --> 02:00:35,023
I'm 100 percent sure it won't be INGYOO.

3344
02:00:35,193 --> 02:00:36,853
He's good at everything he does.

3345
02:00:37,093 --> 02:00:39,522
If my group wins the Director's Cut, I'm safe.

3346
02:00:39,523 --> 02:00:41,733
If we don't, I won't be safe.

3347
02:00:41,933 --> 02:00:42,992
I got the chorus.

3348
02:00:42,993 --> 02:00:46,663
But that might not be enough to guarantee my survival.

3349
02:00:46,863 --> 02:00:48,673
The Director's Cut will be important.

3350
02:00:49,203 --> 02:00:50,203
I agree.

3351
02:00:50,204 --> 02:00:52,002
If your group wins the Director's Cut,

3352
02:00:52,003 --> 02:00:54,473
I'll start thinking that I'm in big trouble then.

3353
02:00:54,713 --> 02:00:56,672
I'm in bigger trouble than you are.

3354
02:00:56,673 --> 02:00:58,483
I was chosen as the Worst Candidate.

3355
02:00:58,743 --> 02:01:00,682
(The Worst Candidate chosen by Director Back Koo Young was...)

3356
02:01:00,683 --> 02:01:02,883
(BABYZOO.)

3357
02:01:03,183 --> 02:01:04,312
If I don't win the Director's Cut,

3358
02:01:04,313 --> 02:01:06,583
I'll go to Last Stage without this win for sure.

3359
02:01:06,783 --> 02:01:11,162
I think the one on the right will probably go to Last Stage.

3360
02:01:11,163 --> 02:01:12,163
Totally, right?

3361
02:01:12,164 --> 02:01:14,193
Renan barely got any parts.

3362
02:01:14,733 --> 02:01:15,763
Right.

3363
02:01:16,793 --> 02:01:19,403
I don't have a lot of parts in the routine.

3364
02:01:19,703 --> 02:01:21,873
They'll judge based on the video.

3365
02:01:22,133 --> 02:01:23,773
I'm barely in the video.

3366
02:01:24,173 --> 02:01:25,703
Kasper was...

3367
02:01:25,873 --> 02:01:28,412
such a good assistant to Koo Young at the shoot.

3368
02:01:28,413 --> 02:01:31,183
So he might have earned a lot of points for that.

3369
02:01:31,483 --> 02:01:33,443
But all of my parts are a bit iffy.

3370
02:01:34,243 --> 02:01:35,813
My position is really iffy.

3371
02:01:36,413 --> 02:01:38,493
Renan, MIN JUN, and Kasper. That sounds about right.

3372
02:01:38,653 --> 02:01:41,533
I'm considering the possibility that I might be the Worst Choreographer.

3373
02:01:41,593 --> 02:01:45,623
Hash didn't get a lot of parts.

3374
02:01:45,793 --> 02:01:48,063
Oh, no. What am I going to do? I'm so nervous.

3375
02:01:48,433 --> 02:01:50,363
I think the judges' evaluation...

3376
02:01:50,793 --> 02:01:52,303
will matter more than...

3377
02:01:52,433 --> 02:01:53,463
Koo Young's.

3378
02:01:53,933 --> 02:01:56,972
Wouldn't they focus more on the dancers who stand out...

3379
02:01:56,973 --> 02:01:59,403
when they watch the video?

3380
02:02:00,203 --> 02:02:01,943
- Hello. Nice to meet you. - I'm Sean.

3381
02:02:02,343 --> 02:02:03,442
- Very nice to meet you. - I'm Koo Young.

3382
02:02:03,443 --> 02:02:04,689
- Nice to meet you. Yes. - Koo Young?

3383
02:02:04,713 --> 02:02:05,982
Welcome to Korea.

3384
02:02:05,983 --> 02:02:07,643
Thank you.

3385
02:02:17,053 --> 02:02:18,669
(Sean Lew is a globally recognized director.)

3386
02:02:18,693 --> 02:02:20,893
(The judges greet each other enthusiastically.)

3387
02:02:23,793 --> 02:02:26,403
(The winning crew of "Street Woman Fighter" in 2021)

3388
02:02:27,033 --> 02:02:29,603
(The leader of HolyBang, Honey J)

3389
02:02:29,903 --> 02:02:31,372
(She established herself in the dance scene...)

3390
02:02:31,373 --> 02:02:32,773
(with her impressive dance skills.)

3391
02:02:33,243 --> 02:02:34,472
(Her unique artistic vision as a director...)

3392
02:02:34,473 --> 02:02:36,219
(stood out during the mega crew performance.)

3393
02:02:36,243 --> 02:02:37,372
(Honey J was the general director...)

3394
02:02:37,373 --> 02:02:39,483
(during the Mega Crew Missions in Seasons 1 and 3.)

3395
02:02:39,643 --> 02:02:40,883
When did you come to Korea?

3396
02:02:41,583 --> 02:02:43,283
- Three days ago. - Three days.

3397
02:02:44,153 --> 02:02:45,282
(The first Asian dancer...)

3398
02:02:45,283 --> 02:02:47,129
(to win in the hip-hop category in Juste Debout)

3399
02:02:47,153 --> 02:02:48,622
(The world-class battler with 22 years of experience...)

3400
02:02:48,623 --> 02:02:50,093
(who conquered the globe)

3401
02:02:50,423 --> 02:02:51,993
(It's Kyoka.)

3402
02:02:52,423 --> 02:02:55,562
So this sounds like what we did for the second mission. Right?

3403
02:02:55,563 --> 02:02:58,102
I remember being completely focused...

3404
02:02:58,103 --> 02:03:01,972
when I was filming my Director's Cut.

3405
02:03:01,973 --> 02:03:03,133
(Let's do one last time.)

3406
02:03:04,073 --> 02:03:06,873
And I was aware that we could show the director...

3407
02:03:07,173 --> 02:03:12,542
how desperately we were trying to execute the performance.

3408
02:03:12,543 --> 02:03:17,483
I feel like with any video project, it's just really important...

3409
02:03:17,983 --> 02:03:21,082
to understand the story behind...

3410
02:03:21,083 --> 02:03:22,522
whatever is being shot.

3411
02:03:22,523 --> 02:03:24,592
Every dancer, the way they're dancing,

3412
02:03:24,593 --> 02:03:26,473
where they're dancing, and why they're dancing.

3413
02:03:26,693 --> 02:03:30,633
And that plays along with screen presence...

3414
02:03:30,963 --> 02:03:33,803
which I think is going to be really important to catch.

3415
02:03:34,903 --> 02:03:36,273
My heart is pounding.

3416
02:03:37,333 --> 02:03:38,802
We'll win the Director's Cut, right?

3417
02:03:38,803 --> 02:03:39,973
We'll win it.

3418
02:03:40,603 --> 02:03:42,043
- We must. - We must.

3419
02:03:42,373 --> 02:03:44,682
Koo Young didn't use any moves from my routine.

3420
02:03:44,683 --> 02:03:47,342
If I can't win the Director's Cut,

3421
02:03:47,343 --> 02:03:49,543
I'll be in big trouble. I'll go to Last Stage for sure.

3422
02:03:49,853 --> 02:03:51,723
If we win the Director's Cut,

3423
02:03:51,983 --> 02:03:53,282
I'll probably be safe.

3424
02:03:53,283 --> 02:03:55,293
- I wonder which one he chose. - I have no idea.

3425
02:03:55,393 --> 02:03:57,253
Objectively speaking, ours looks pretty good.

3426
02:03:57,693 --> 02:03:58,962
Just dancers?

3427
02:03:58,963 --> 02:04:00,393
No, I can't let that be.

3428
02:04:01,293 --> 02:04:03,262
I just want to get it over with. I want to see how it came out.

3429
02:04:03,263 --> 02:04:04,293
- Right? - Yes.

3430
02:04:05,263 --> 02:04:06,333
He's here.

3431
02:04:06,433 --> 02:04:08,103
(Utterly nervous)

3432
02:04:08,433 --> 02:04:10,103
In the Title Sequence Film Mission,

3433
02:04:10,173 --> 02:04:12,049
you had to prove your talent with your choreography...

3434
02:04:12,073 --> 02:04:14,713
and compete to get your name on the board.

3435
02:04:15,243 --> 02:04:16,273
Gosh, I'm nervous.

3436
02:04:17,073 --> 02:04:18,942
Those who failed to prove their talent...

3437
02:04:18,943 --> 02:04:20,019
through their choreography...

3438
02:04:20,043 --> 02:04:22,453
will receive one last chance to prove themselves on stage.

3439
02:04:22,753 --> 02:04:25,223
It's called Last Stage.

3440
02:04:26,253 --> 02:04:28,953
There are nine choreographers here.

3441
02:04:29,153 --> 02:04:31,863
Three of you will head to Last Stage.

3442
02:04:32,193 --> 02:04:34,022
The nerve-racking feeling and the anxiety...

3443
02:04:34,023 --> 02:04:35,032
started to hit me already...

3444
02:04:35,033 --> 02:04:36,433
when I hadn't even been eliminated.

3445
02:04:36,693 --> 02:04:38,833
I don't think I contributed a lot to this mission.

3446
02:04:39,003 --> 02:04:40,763
I don't want to go to Last Stage.

3447
02:04:40,933 --> 02:04:42,632
The number of choreographers...

3448
02:04:42,633 --> 02:04:46,203
who can return to the Directors' Lab after surviving Last Stage...

3449
02:04:46,343 --> 02:04:48,543
I couldn't stop feeling nervous.

3450
02:04:49,073 --> 02:04:50,343
Is just one.

3451
02:04:51,143 --> 02:04:54,442
It was shocking that only one person survived.

3452
02:04:54,443 --> 02:04:56,312
I think it's really cruel.

3453
02:04:56,313 --> 02:04:59,322
I really don't want to go to the Last Stage.

3454
02:04:59,323 --> 02:05:01,252
To determine...

3455
02:05:01,253 --> 02:05:03,753
who would ultimately survive and preserve their name,

3456
02:05:04,553 --> 02:05:05,962
Director Back Koo Young gave...

3457
02:05:05,963 --> 02:05:09,062
the participants the opportunity to have their names listed...

3458
02:05:09,063 --> 02:05:10,892
as choreographers on the Credit Board...

3459
02:05:10,893 --> 02:05:13,413
during the process of completing the final title sequence film.

3460
02:05:13,663 --> 02:05:17,103
The first choreographer Back Koo Young chose was...

3461
02:05:18,643 --> 02:05:19,843
BADA.

3462
02:05:21,713 --> 02:05:25,883
It is the title I wanted to win the most.

3463
02:05:26,443 --> 02:05:30,012
So, I think I'll get a high score...

3464
02:05:30,013 --> 02:05:34,423
for my creative contribution.

3465
02:05:34,683 --> 02:05:37,552
Secondly, Director Back Koo Young...

3466
02:05:37,553 --> 02:05:40,292
personally selected the choreography...

3467
02:05:40,293 --> 02:05:44,093
he wanted to use in the final film from the initial draft videos.

3468
02:05:44,633 --> 02:05:45,633
The choreographers are...

3469
02:05:46,463 --> 02:05:49,173
NaiN and Kasper.

3470
02:05:49,303 --> 02:05:50,572
I'm jealous.

3471
02:05:50,573 --> 02:05:53,673
BABYZOO's choreography was also selected,

3472
02:05:53,773 --> 02:05:57,043
but ultimately failed to make it onto the credit board.

3473
02:05:57,173 --> 02:05:58,842
My choreography wasn't included,

3474
02:05:58,843 --> 02:06:01,342
and the choreography for the outro wasn't selected either.

3475
02:06:01,343 --> 02:06:05,053
I have a feeling the Director's Cut will change my destiny.

3476
02:06:05,153 --> 02:06:08,822
The recipients of all the credits have not yet been decided.

3477
02:06:08,823 --> 02:06:11,823
It's because the most important choice still remains.

3478
02:06:12,563 --> 02:06:13,693
That is...

3479
02:06:14,393 --> 02:06:16,093
the Director's Cut.

3480
02:06:16,893 --> 02:06:18,233
(Director's Cut Revealed)

3481
02:06:18,563 --> 02:06:19,833
- Gosh. - Revealed?

3482
02:06:20,163 --> 02:06:22,203
Goodness.

3483
02:06:22,573 --> 02:06:24,272
Even if I'm not chosen,

3484
02:06:24,273 --> 02:06:25,713
I'm curious about how it turned out.

3485
02:06:26,073 --> 02:06:28,772
Who will be the star of the Director's Cut...

3486
02:06:28,773 --> 02:06:31,173
chosen by Director Back Koo Young?

3487
02:06:31,583 --> 02:06:32,583
Please.

3488
02:06:32,743 --> 02:06:33,743
Please.

3489
02:06:33,943 --> 02:06:35,252
- Gosh. - Goodness.

3490
02:06:35,253 --> 02:06:37,112
Title Sequence Film Mission.

3491
02:06:37,113 --> 02:06:40,082
Let's watch the final video.

3492
02:06:40,083 --> 02:06:42,122
Please.

3493
02:06:42,123 --> 02:06:43,483
I feel like I'm going to throw up.

3494
02:06:45,793 --> 02:06:47,462
(Royalty)

3495
02:06:47,463 --> 02:06:48,833
(Synopsis and Film Directionality)

3496
02:06:52,003 --> 02:06:53,163
Let's go.

3497
02:06:58,203 --> 02:06:59,203
Yes.

3498
02:07:02,673 --> 02:07:04,672
(Director Back Koo Young enters.)

3499
02:07:04,673 --> 02:07:05,943
Why do I feel so embarrassed?

3500
02:07:06,683 --> 02:07:08,143
That's so cool.

3501
02:07:09,713 --> 02:07:11,753
(Focused)

3502
02:07:13,123 --> 02:07:14,922
How does he get up so effortlessly?

3503
02:07:14,923 --> 02:07:16,653
I was nervous.

3504
02:07:23,433 --> 02:07:24,833
NaiN is so pretty.

3505
02:07:26,003 --> 02:07:28,284
I danced until it felt like my whole body was shattering.

3506
02:07:28,573 --> 02:07:30,473
- Nice. - Yes.

3507
02:07:30,873 --> 02:07:33,073
It's very clear. I feel like it's really important.

3508
02:07:34,943 --> 02:07:36,643
Yes.

3509
02:07:40,943 --> 02:07:42,512
(Oh! BADA)

3510
02:07:42,513 --> 02:07:45,082
As expected, BADA is incredibly skilled...

3511
02:07:45,083 --> 02:07:46,623
at expressing herself.

3512
02:07:48,923 --> 02:07:50,923
- Yes. - Hey.

3513
02:07:53,093 --> 02:07:55,793
Renan lacked impact in that scene.

3514
02:07:59,103 --> 02:08:00,262
(Heelmeez!)

3515
02:08:00,263 --> 02:08:02,303
The one wearing heels is amazing.

3516
02:08:09,773 --> 02:08:11,643
- Hey. - Hey.

3517
02:08:11,843 --> 02:08:13,143
I was just into myself.

3518
02:08:15,153 --> 02:08:16,783
The video is thrilling.

3519
02:08:23,393 --> 02:08:25,493
(Look at his eyes.)

3520
02:08:26,093 --> 02:08:27,723
- Hey. - That's good.

3521
02:08:27,793 --> 02:08:31,492
I gave my absolute best in every single scene to ensure...

3522
02:08:31,493 --> 02:08:34,063
they would dare choose me as the worst choreographer.

3523
02:08:39,073 --> 02:08:40,143
Here it comes.

3524
02:08:43,143 --> 02:08:44,172
(Here comes the Director's Cut.)

3525
02:08:44,173 --> 02:08:45,682
(Group Simeez, NaiN, BADA?)

3526
02:08:45,683 --> 02:08:47,243
(Group BABYZOO, JEONG MIN JUN, INGYOO?)

3527
02:08:47,343 --> 02:08:48,483
Wait.

3528
02:08:48,653 --> 02:08:51,582
I was about 80 percent certain that we would be chosen.

3529
02:08:51,583 --> 02:08:53,352
Please. If I'm not chosen,

3530
02:08:53,353 --> 02:08:55,152
I have to do the Last Stage.

3531
02:08:55,153 --> 02:08:57,922
I think I'll only feel at ease...

3532
02:08:57,923 --> 02:08:59,792
if I get chosen for the Director's Cut.

3533
02:08:59,793 --> 02:09:01,162
Wait a minute.

3534
02:09:01,163 --> 02:09:03,192
Who is it?

3535
02:09:03,193 --> 02:09:05,503
(Director's Cut Revealed)

3536
02:09:07,003 --> 02:09:08,923
(Director's Cut, BABYZOO, JEONG MIN JUN, INGYOO)

3537
02:09:09,703 --> 02:09:11,102
It was a matter of life and death.

3538
02:09:11,103 --> 02:09:12,773
It was really thrilling.

3539
02:09:14,343 --> 02:09:15,343
I'm doomed.

3540
02:09:15,344 --> 02:09:16,572
(So close)

3541
02:09:16,573 --> 02:09:17,672
This is driving me nuts.

3542
02:09:17,673 --> 02:09:19,082
(Director's Cut, BABYZOO, INGYOO, MIN JUN)

3543
02:09:19,083 --> 02:09:22,253
No!

3544
02:09:26,653 --> 02:09:28,393
Will this actually count as a plus?

3545
02:09:30,423 --> 02:09:32,023
I'm so embarrassed.

3546
02:09:32,593 --> 02:09:33,922
(Simeez is awesome.)

3547
02:09:33,923 --> 02:09:35,533
The dopamine rush was off the charts.

3548
02:09:35,833 --> 02:09:36,892
Gosh.

3549
02:09:36,893 --> 02:09:39,503
Simeez's part is essential right here.

3550
02:09:44,003 --> 02:09:45,343
Hey!

3551
02:09:46,603 --> 02:09:47,943
- Yes! - Hey!

3552
02:09:49,273 --> 02:09:50,643
This is cool.

3553
02:09:51,173 --> 02:09:52,642
(Kasper's favorite part, nodding)

3554
02:09:52,643 --> 02:09:54,583
I can nod anywhere.

3555
02:10:02,253 --> 02:10:03,723
Yes.

3556
02:10:03,853 --> 02:10:05,393
We're cool.

3557
02:10:06,993 --> 02:10:08,262
NaiN.

3558
02:10:08,263 --> 02:10:09,733
I looked good.

3559
02:10:10,133 --> 02:10:11,833
NaiN is so good.

3560
02:10:13,433 --> 02:10:15,173
She's gritting her teeth.

3561
02:10:18,473 --> 02:10:19,903
- Let's go. - Hey.

3562
02:10:23,243 --> 02:10:25,283
The director is so cool.

3563
02:10:28,853 --> 02:10:30,812
There is an energy that comes from Koo Young's choreography.

3564
02:10:30,813 --> 02:10:32,553
It makes you excited.

3565
02:10:35,253 --> 02:10:37,793
- Gosh. - Yes.

3566
02:10:41,623 --> 02:10:43,262
(You can watch the full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

3567
02:10:43,263 --> 02:10:44,762
(Wow)

3568
02:10:44,763 --> 02:10:46,302
("Royalty" by Yoonmirae and Tiger JK...)

3569
02:10:46,303 --> 02:10:47,979
(is available on various music streaming sites.)

3570
02:10:48,003 --> 02:10:49,532
It's so cool.

3571
02:10:49,533 --> 02:10:50,832
Thank you.

3572
02:10:50,833 --> 02:10:53,802
- I want to give you a ten. - I know. I can't give you a ten.

3573
02:10:53,803 --> 02:10:55,343
It doesn't make sense.

3574
02:10:55,573 --> 02:10:56,642
Thank you.

3575
02:10:56,643 --> 02:10:58,172
(The Title Sequence Film satisfied all the Fight Judges.)

3576
02:10:58,173 --> 02:11:00,742
Achieving this level of quality in such a short time is impressive.

3577
02:11:00,743 --> 02:11:02,152
I love the coloring.

3578
02:11:02,153 --> 02:11:05,222
I like some of the transitions. I think it's very clever.

3579
02:11:05,223 --> 02:11:08,552
And the mirrors. I think it's really great.

3580
02:11:08,553 --> 02:11:12,792
Throughout the video, I caught glimpses of the emotions...

3581
02:11:12,793 --> 02:11:18,562
or expressions of each person wanting to take first place.

3582
02:11:18,563 --> 02:11:20,962
Since it was a title sequence,

3583
02:11:20,963 --> 02:11:22,972
I put a lot of effort into capturing shots...

3584
02:11:22,973 --> 02:11:25,843
that would deliver real impact during the editing process.

3585
02:11:26,573 --> 02:11:27,842
Guys.

3586
02:11:27,843 --> 02:11:29,163
(The 3 happiest people right now)

3587
02:11:29,473 --> 02:11:31,172
The choreographers of the Director's Cut...

3588
02:11:31,173 --> 02:11:32,943
chosen by Director Back Koo Young are...

3589
02:11:33,183 --> 02:11:37,412
BABYZOO, INGYOO, and JEONG MIN JUN.

3590
02:11:37,413 --> 02:11:39,723
- Congratulations. - I'm jealous.

3591
02:11:39,753 --> 02:11:41,123
(Bitter)

3592
02:11:41,353 --> 02:11:42,992
I was really happy.

3593
02:11:42,993 --> 02:11:46,322
I thought I might be able to move further away from being the worst.

3594
02:11:46,323 --> 02:11:47,492
I was very relieved.

3595
02:11:47,493 --> 02:11:49,192
I won't go to the Last Stage.

3596
02:11:49,193 --> 02:11:50,193
I'm jealous.

3597
02:11:50,194 --> 02:11:52,462
Things aren't going the way I thought they would.

3598
02:11:52,463 --> 02:11:54,002
It's a huge shame.

3599
02:11:54,003 --> 02:11:55,832
I want to know why.

3600
02:11:55,833 --> 02:11:57,572
I chose this cut...

3601
02:11:57,573 --> 02:12:01,072
because it effectively captures both a clean aesthetic...

3602
02:12:01,073 --> 02:12:02,772
and creativity.

3603
02:12:02,773 --> 02:12:04,172
(Agreed)

3604
02:12:04,173 --> 02:12:05,782
Even without the lyrics,

3605
02:12:05,783 --> 02:12:07,742
the mise-en-scene effectively captures...

3606
02:12:07,743 --> 02:12:09,653
the mood of the music.

3607
02:12:10,953 --> 02:12:12,722
In the case of BADA, Simeez, and NaiN,

3608
02:12:12,723 --> 02:12:16,752
the choreography features slow tempos and transitions.

3609
02:12:16,753 --> 02:12:19,722
The performance is flat and lacks impact.

3610
02:12:19,723 --> 02:12:21,832
It didn't look right.

3611
02:12:21,833 --> 02:12:23,432
It was like oil and water.

3612
02:12:23,433 --> 02:12:24,862
- You know. - Right.

3613
02:12:24,863 --> 02:12:28,362
In the case of Kasper, Hash, and Renan,

3614
02:12:28,363 --> 02:12:30,402
holding the phone in the mouth...

3615
02:12:30,403 --> 02:12:31,972
turned out to be not bad at all.

3616
02:12:31,973 --> 02:12:33,842
Like this. You know, it's not dance,

3617
02:12:33,843 --> 02:12:37,072
but it's a moment. It's a frame. It's a feeling.

3618
02:12:37,073 --> 02:12:38,472
I feel like the lip sync thing... I don't know.

3619
02:12:38,473 --> 02:12:39,482
I like weird stuff.

3620
02:12:39,483 --> 02:12:43,282
I like weird dance ideas specifically.

3621
02:12:43,283 --> 02:12:46,922
That's why I kept thinking.

3622
02:12:46,923 --> 02:12:48,482
Ultimately, the reason I chose it...

3623
02:12:48,483 --> 02:12:50,492
was the expressive ability shown as a dancer.

3624
02:12:50,493 --> 02:12:53,792
That played a major role in the decision.

3625
02:12:53,793 --> 02:12:55,463
Yes. It makes sense.

3626
02:12:56,163 --> 02:12:58,762
With this, the choreographers for all credits...

3627
02:12:58,763 --> 02:13:01,303
in the Title Sequence Film Mission have been determined.

3628
02:13:01,463 --> 02:13:02,632
The choreographers...

3629
02:13:02,633 --> 02:13:05,172
who did not make it onto the Credit Board...

3630
02:13:05,173 --> 02:13:08,473
for this mission are Renan, Simeez, and Hash.

3631
02:13:08,573 --> 02:13:09,772
What are we going to do?

3632
02:13:09,773 --> 02:13:11,243
Hash. Renan.

3633
02:13:11,443 --> 02:13:14,042
Did they do this on purpose to send us to the Last Stage?

3634
02:13:14,043 --> 02:13:16,282
Goodness. I'm so nervous.

3635
02:13:16,283 --> 02:13:18,452
This is bad. I might end up going to the Last Stage.

3636
02:13:18,453 --> 02:13:19,453
However,

3637
02:13:19,953 --> 02:13:22,222
having your name on the Credit Board...

3638
02:13:22,223 --> 02:13:24,592
doesn't guarantee survival.

3639
02:13:24,593 --> 02:13:25,593
Really?

3640
02:13:26,623 --> 02:13:27,623
Thank goodness.

3641
02:13:27,624 --> 02:13:28,633
Please.

3642
02:13:28,963 --> 02:13:30,632
This is too hard. Stop.

3643
02:13:30,633 --> 02:13:32,562
Nobody knows the future.

3644
02:13:32,563 --> 02:13:33,962
So I'm very anxious.

3645
02:13:33,963 --> 02:13:35,902
It could be me.

3646
02:13:35,903 --> 02:13:37,172
You can't let my guard down.

3647
02:13:37,173 --> 02:13:39,503
